33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-07T10:02:40-07:00","id":1406801,"title":"","content":"Oh, history repeat , and we know have 2 Sabbats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-07T10:17:13-07:00","id":1406804,"title":"","content":"The Setites aren't fascists, they're Libertarians, hence the snake imagery. They're Libertarians who actively want to destroy the world, which makes them unusually well informed Libertarians.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-07T10:17:45-07:00","id":1406805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1406801#post1406801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, history repeat , and we know have 2 Sabbats.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like the Sabbat will probably split.<br /> <br /> 1. The weird occult military and cult? The Sabbat.<br /> <br /> 2. The bunch of crazy burning things down anarchists? The Anarchs.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-07T13:21:04-07:00","id":1406830,"title":"","content":"The Sabbat elders have joined the camarilla; the war in the middle east is a childer cull, just like the Camarilla giving up many of it's members. Kill the young; the youth are rotten; if the species is to survive, it needs to remove its population of fools. God will know his own. <br /> <br /> The Camarilla shift to open religion was an ammendment to get the Sabbat elders on board; Camarilla elders were perfectly happy with their secretive cults (and will continue to use secretive cults; we can't openly hate viccissitude with our new fiend friends around, can we?) The Tremere split was also in part to deal with an influx of Sabbat elders (Many Tzmisce will not abide living in a city with Tremere. House Carna on the otherhand...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-07T15:01:18-07:00","id":1406837,"title":"","content":"<b>The First Anarch Revolt</b><br /> <br /> In the darkness of the Dark Ages creatures of darkness waged wars against each other across Europe in the darkness and this led hunters to attacking the darkness.<br /> <br /> (clears throat)<br /> <br /> As some background\u2026<br /> <br /> The Ventrue of the High Middle Ages were nominally based out of what is now called Germany. Over the centuries they waged war across everyone around them, including the Toreador in France, Lasombra across Southern Europe and most disastrously the Tzimisce of Eastern Europe. At the same time the Tremere transformed from a group of treacherous and unpleasant blood wizards to a group of treacherous and unpleasant magic wielding vampires\u2026 in the middle of Tzimisce territory. A world already soaked in violence and chaos sank deeper into chaos and violence. And as always the number one tactic the elders used was to throw ancilae and neonates at lethal problems. The younger vampires got tired of this and turned on the elders. This overall warring revealed the existence of vampires to mortal hunters, principally the Inquisition. The Inquisition attacked vampires as well, which increased pressure on them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The first Anarchs were born in the fires of the Inquisition. They learned to survive and to fight a war against the worst foe to ever threaten our kind until the present day. Many died in the betrayal of the elders, but many more learned they could take charge of their own lives.<br /> - Nakache </div> </div> </div>This over all war of the relative youths against the elders lasted for centuries before petering out at the end of the 15<sup>th</sup> century. The then Baby Camarilla was able to force a meeting between the combatants in the village of Thorns made on October 23, 1493.<br /> <br /> French Anarch and revolutionary ideologue Dalia Nakache discusses this meeting. Apparently it did not go well. At least not for the Anarchs, the Banu Haqim, the Tzimisce and the Lasombra. The Camarilla was able to force the Banu Haqim to sign a magical treaty which hobbled the clan until the Demonic Ur-Shulgi recently woke and destroyed the magical aspect of the treaty. However, the follow through of the Camarilla on the subject at the time also debatable, as the Tzimisce and the Lasombra were able to escape and form their own sect, one with blackjack and hookers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Anarchs and the nascent Camarilla sent representatives to the town of Thorns to negotiate. This was the first mistake the Anarchs made. There is no negotiating with the Camarilla. You can't win against political manipulators who've spent centuries perfecting their craft.<br /> - Nakache </div> </div> </div>The original treaty struck at Thorns supposedly gave Anarchs the protection of the Camarilla. That changed recently, in the setting, with the destruction of Hardestadt the Younger by Theo Bell. However, even during the 500 or so years of the existence of the treaty it was widely ignored by the Camarilla and the spat upon by the Anarchs. Even at the time of the treaty some then Anarch leaders cried foul on the entire affair, with Sasha Vykos throwing his (her?) genitals at Hardestad the Elder, and Tyler later killing and diablerizing Hardestadt. All in all, it was a bad time to be Hardestadt.<br /> <br /> Nakache notes parallels between modern times, with the disappearing Elder leaving youths to deal with the Second Inquisition. She also asserts that the Anarch movement respresnts the majority of vampires, but that is debatable.<br /> <br /> More interesting is her hardline stance that members of the Camarilla cannot be negotiated with; you cannot talk to the opposition and there is no room for opposition.<br /> <br /> Thorns is, or was, a rural village near Silchester in Hampsire. Interestingly, notably notorious Noddist Cuthbert Beckett maintains one of his rare fixed havens in the Silchester pub, the Calleva Arms. The pub is apparently a real place. I believe Matthew Dawkins lives in South Central England, he might have visited the pub \u2013 otherwise Beckett keeping a haven in the place feels pretty random. Though Thorns, as a village, is a fictional place it should be reasonable to place it on the site of the ruins of Calleva Atrebatum.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-07T15:13:57-07:00","id":1406838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1406830#post1406830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Sabbat elders have joined the camarilla; the war in the middle east is a childer cull, just like the Camarilla giving up many of it's members. Kill the young; the youth are rotten; if the species is to survive, it needs to remove its population of fools. God will know his own. <br /> <br /> The Camarilla shift to open religion was an ammendment to get the Sabbat elders on board; Camarilla elders were perfectly happy with their secretive cults (and will continue to use secretive cults; we can't openly hate viccissitude with our new fiend friends around, can we?) The Tremere split was also in part to deal with an influx of Sabbat elders (Many Tzmisce will not abide living in a city with Tremere. House Carna on the otherhand...)</div> </div> </div> </div>Is that Cannon? Or head cannon?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-07T15:21:08-07:00","id":1406840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1406838#post1406838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is that Cannon? Or head cannon?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's just his head canon.<br /> <br /> SOME elders of the Sabbat have joined the Camarilla, some others did NOT.<br /> <br /> The Tzimisce have NOT joined the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> The Tremere's schism caould have been caused by a number of causes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-07T16:35:12-07:00","id":1406859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1406840#post1406840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's just his head canon.<br /> <br /> SOME elders of the Sabbat have joined the Camarilla, some others did NOT.<br /> <br /> The Tzimisce have NOT joined the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> The Tremere's schism caould have been caused by a number of causes.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25794_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25794\" data-vbnamecard=\"25794\">MyWifeIsScary</a> doesn't care for the Elders being portrayed as short-sighted idiots and prefers them to be incredibly brilliant 3 dimensional chessmasters that are playing the long game.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 08-07-2020, 11:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-07T16:51:41-07:00","id":1406860,"title":"","content":"<b>CT Phipps' thoughts on the First Anarch Revolt</b><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1406837#post1406837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>The First Anarch Revolt</b><br /> <br /> In the darkness of the Dark Ages creatures of darkness waged wars against each other across Europe in the darkness and this led hunters to attacking the darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the grim dark past of the Middle Ages, there is only war.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The original treaty struck at Thorns supposedly gave Anarchs the protection of the Camarilla. That changed recently, in the setting, with the destruction of Hardestadt the Younger by Theo Bell. However, even during the 500 or so years of the existence of the treaty it was widely ignored by the Camarilla and the spat upon by the Anarchs. Even at the time of the treaty some then Anarch leaders cried foul on the entire affair, with Sasha Vykos throwing his (her?) genitals at Hardestad the Elder, and Tyler later killing and diablerizing Hardestadt. All in all, it was a bad time to be Hardestadt. </div> </div> </div>It should be noted that Tyler killed Hardestadt before the Convention of Thorns. Indeed, she had a theatrical breakdown when Hardestadt showed up and Tyler went, &quot;I KILLLLEDDD YOU!&quot; This certainly didn't do much for her credibility. Mind you, we all know it was an imposter but given that Dominate is capable of convincing individuals of whatever you want them to or replacing memories, it makes sense that Tyler might have had her memory changed by Hardestadt the Elder as a last ditch attempt to escape being murdered. It also is a rather brilliant master stroke. Tyler is humiliated and much of her cred with the Anarchs is destroyed. Ironically, it might actually go a long way to explaining why she gave up revolution as her greatest accomplishment was apparently all for naught.<br /> <br /> I have this mental image of Beckett then casually revealing that she DID kill the &quot;real&quot; Hardestadt and unknowingly reigniting her Anarch fire. I also believe she's the person who helped Theo Bell kill Hardestadt II and escape in the aftermath.<br /> <br /> Why? Because Beckett ruins everything.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Nakache notes parallels between modern times, with the disappearing Elder leaving youths to deal with the Second Inquisition. She also asserts that the Anarch movement respresnts the majority of vampires, but that is debatable. </div> </div> </div>&quot;History does not repeat but it rhymes.&quot; - Mark Twain.<br /> <br /> In retrospect, its kind of funny that the Brujah and Assamites surrendered but that was pretty much it for Anarch surrenders.<br /> <br /> Even then, the Assamites claim they did so because the Tremere curse actually was a way to reign in the diablerie curse by the Baali.<br /> <br /> Which I don't buy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> More interesting is her hardline stance that members of the Camarilla cannot be negotiated with; you cannot talk to the opposition and there is no room for opposition. </div> </div> </div>Mind you, this is both a ridiculous assertion and also fairly good politics. For the majority of vampires, at least until Prague, the Camarilla means absolutely nothing other than a vague organization that exists only if you screw up. Most Kindred aren't going to have to deal with the Sheriff or Prince unless they screw up. The thing is that also means the majority of vampires have no strong feelings for the Camarilla either. For most Camarilla vampires prior to Prague, the Camarilla was an &quot;Elders only&quot; thing that you hopefully never had to deal with. It neither engendered loyalty or hate--and so the Anarch Movement was quiescient unless you were Caitiff, Brujah, or Thin Blooded.<br /> <br /> Prague is important because it radicalized the Camarilla as much as it radicalized the Anarchs. Now you had to make displays of loyalty and obedience if you were Brujah or Gangrel. You also were expected to report to the Sheriff if you had any suspicious friends or dealings. You also needed to remove any and all technology beyond a landline (or just hoped they never noticed). You were either VERY FOR the Camarilla or you were against it.<br /> <br /> Fully expect your domain, which most Kindred were aware of but not going to explode over, to have the Final Death given to you if you hunted in it without permission and were not somebody's friend,<br /> <br /> RL terrorists use this in real life. You spank the government or authorities in an area, they crack down on people who are LIKE the terrorists, and the people like the terrorists then get pissed and join the terrorists. It was actually the focus of an ASSASSINS CREED: ORIGINS DLC where one of the Assassins allies was murdering Roman troops so the Romans would sack the local villages and thus generate a dozen new recruits.<br /> <br /> As much as I love the Anarchs, they're a force to be reckoned with now because the hardcore Anarchs have made life miserable for a lot of non-Anarchs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 08-07-2020, 08:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-07T19:53:21-07:00","id":1406887,"title":"","content":"There is also a practical aspect to it - the enemies here can wreck each other's minds when they make eye contact. So, you avoid talking to them and making eye contact. That is in addition to everyone involved being a vampire, and thus an untrustworthy murderer and liar. And I really like the idea of Beckett accidentally setting Tyler off on another killing spree.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-07T23:36:57-07:00","id":1406909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1406838#post1406838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is that Cannon? Or head cannon?</div> </div> </div> </div>Doesn't it sound like actual canon though? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1406859#post1406859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> doesn't care for the Elders being portrayed as short-sighted idiots and prefers them to be incredibly brilliant 3 dimensional chessmasters that are playing the long game.</div> </div> </div> </div>on the suspicion that this might be sarcastic... <br /> 1 If i thought of it, it can't be that complicated right? Seems like it would be pretty simple from their points of view. <br /> 2 you know a lot of elders had intellegence ratings of 6 and above, right? I'm not saying they're all geniuses, but there's enough if those to make the plan work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T07:27:18-07:00","id":1406963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1406909#post1406909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Doesn't it sound like actual canon though? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> on the suspicion that this might be sarcastic...<br /> 1 If i thought of it, it can't be that complicated right? Seems like it would be pretty simple from their points of view.<br /> 2 you know a lot of elders had intellegence ratings of 6 and above, right? I'm not saying they're all geniuses, but there's enough if those to make the plan work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, it's weird because multiple people wrote me assuming it was sarcastic.<br /> <br /> It was not.<br /> <br /> I had a little :sincere: underneath it too but removed it because I assumed that it would be obvious I was sincere. I also gave you a compliment that it actually showed an improved relationship to V5 and appreciated your attempt to try to reconcile it to your playstyle.<br /> <br /> :thumbs up:","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 08-08-2020, 11:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T09:42:49-07:00","id":1406986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1406963#post1406963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had a little :sincere: underneath it too but removed it because I assumed that it would be obvious I was sincere. I also gave you a compliment that it actually showed an improved relationship to V5 and appreciated your attempt to try to reconcile it to your playstyle.<br /> <br /> :thumbs up:</div> </div> </div> </div>You say this, but I still can't come to grips with v5's mechanics; The Metaplot? Salvagable, potentially even good. Mechanics? Given prior editions, Some of it is subjectively bad, some of it is objectively bad insofar as it interacts with the story but I suppose if you don't care for a coherent story it's not really that big of an issue, and some of it is just terrible in all aspects unless you become willfully ignorant. When I talk about V5 metaplot, I'm thinking under the assumption of the mechanics of the prior editions, because if I did think about any metaplot with V5 mechanics, I'd be destracted by thoughts like &quot;Why isn't suicide more common? Why do lasombra exist now? Shouldn't the average humanity rating be 3 now since it's way to expensive to buy back up? Shouldn't golconda take ten thousand years? Should I take the fact that armour doesn't work for vampires as a purely mechanical oversight or is it a mystical thing and I should delete all my dark-age imagination concerning vampire knights? Can Vampires really be blamed for their beasts acting up when there's much less they can do to mitigate things. Why did the elders fear diablerie when it's a really bad idea unless you're a saint and thus unlikely to diablerise? how.... how does vampire society come to even remotely resemble what it is? <br /> <br /> Metaplot good<br /> Mechanics bad<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.politicalcompass.org/crowdchart2?spots=7%7C3%7CCamarilla,9%7C9%7CGiovanni,-2%7C7%7CAssamites,1%7C8%7CSabbat,-2%7C-6%7CAnarchs%20(Ideal),5%7C-2%7CAnarchs%20(actual),6%7C-9%7CSettites,-4%7C9%7CBahari\" target=\"_blank\">Anyhow, I whacked up this political compass,</a> of course I couldn't do every detail (like sabbat factions) without it becoming a mess. <br /> <br /> Some notes<br /> -Anarchs could totally take anyone else's spot on that compass. <br /> -This concerns vampires and their direct servants; If we concerned ourselves with mortal politics , being vampires, they'd all be in the blue corner, because that's the best place to feed in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T11:09:14-07:00","id":1406996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1406909#post1406909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2 you know a lot of elders had intellegence ratings of 6 and above, right? I'm not saying they're all geniuses, but there's enough if those to make the plan work.</div> </div> </div> </div>For one thing, an intelligence of 6 is a specific designation for a particular ability - it does not automatically translate into surpassing competence in other areas. It just means they can pass the written portion of a driving test with flying colors, but they might still crash into a telephone pole before leaving the parking lot.<br /> <br /> For another, unless the PCs are playing elders the game is not about elders. It is about the PC vampires dealing with (among other things) elders. A high level of intelligence on paper for and NPC does not mean the elder automatically wins at everything the ST has them do with tangling with the PCs. It does not allow a ST to hand wave away any time the PCs performed well in their own dice rolls or just out maneuvered the ST.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T11:42:16-07:00","id":1407003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1406986#post1406986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://www.politicalcompass.org/crowdchart2?spots=7%7C3%7CCamarilla,9%7C9%7CGiovanni,-2%7C7%7CAssamites,1%7C8%7CSabbat,-2%7C-6%7CAnarchs%20(Ideal),5%7C-2%7CAnarchs%20(actual),6%7C-9%7CSettites,-4%7C9%7CBahari\" target=\"_blank\">Anyhow, I whacked up this political compass,</a> of course I couldn't do every detail (like sabbat factions) without it becoming a mess.</div> </div> </div> </div>In what sort of ways do you think Bahari are that authoritarian?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T12:57:05-07:00","id":1407018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1407003#post1407003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In what sort of ways do you think Bahari are that authoritarian?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm glad you asked: Literal chains. (I might've put them that high as a joke)<br /> <br /> In seriousness , they do have several concerning authoritarian tendancies:<br /> <br /> Groupthink<br /> Demands of like-minded behaviour<br /> Acceptance of dogma; questions are punishable.<br /> plentiful self sacrifice for a higher purpose<br /> A long list of external enemies to be mad at.<br /> Belief in a conspiracy against them (or lilith)<br /> Assertions of superiority over other 'cainites'<br /> Owing to the amount of time you spend with the group in torture and the push for &quot;knowledge&quot; rather than material power, you are unlikely to have any really holdings of your own, and so Ostracism should you speak out would be a terrifying prospect.<br /> <br /> <br /> So yeah, Bahari are quite the frightening collection of cults, even if they weren't turning themselves inside out on the regular. There might be nicer cults, but they probably don't last as long.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T14:44:46-07:00","id":1407034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1407018#post1407018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm glad you asked: Literal chains. (I might've put them that high as a joke)<br /> <br /> In seriousness , they do have several concerning authoritarian tendancies:<br /> <br /> Groupthink<br /> Demands of like-minded behaviour<br /> Acceptance of dogma; questions are punishable.<br /> plentiful self sacrifice for a higher purpose<br /> A long list of external enemies to be mad at.<br /> Belief in a conspiracy against them (or lilith)<br /> Assertions of superiority over other 'cainites'<br /> Owing to the amount of time you spend with the group in torture and the push for &quot;knowledge&quot; rather than material power, you are unlikely to have any really holdings of your own, and so Ostracism should you speak out would be a terrifying prospect.<br /> <br /> <br /> So yeah, Bahari are quite the frightening collection of cults, even if they weren't turning themselves inside out on the regular. There might be nicer cults, but they probably don't last as long.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah. I've been tempted to think of them as VtM's Circle of the Crone, which I think would be approaching the Setites' position, but this is more like how they're written, at least in V5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T16:49:53-07:00","id":1407047,"title":"","content":"<b>The Reign of Terror</b><br /> <br /> <i>Vive la revolution!<br /> <br /> Vive la terreur!</i><br /> <br /> Agata &quot;guillotine fangirl&quot; Starek discusses vampire politics and trends during this stage of the French Revolution. She admits to not being present, but it is not clear if she was simply somewhere else or had not been born yet.<br /> <br /> There are a lot factors going into the French Revolution, including large scale social changes across Europe, discontent in France itself but all the issues were exacerbated by a financial crisis. The system could no longer support the Ancien Regeme.<br /> <br /> The Ancien R\u00e9gime (&quot;old rule&quot;) was the political and social system of the Kingdom of France from the Late Middle Ages until the French Revolution of 1789, which led to the abolition of hereditary monarchy and of the feudal system of the French nobility. The late Valois and Bourbon dynasties ruled during the Ancien R\u00e9gime. As much as they could European nobility and the royal families of the time tended towards absolute power. The French, more so than most others, formalized it into law and into legal and moral philosophy. However, the system was always rotten for the general population, and in the end brittle and unsustainable. Naturally, it was heavily infested with vampires.<br /> <br /> Francois \u201cThe weenie\u201d Villon fled Paris when the city descended into the chaos of the revolution. And the revolution did fall into chaos, eating itself and eventually turning into a dictatorship under Napoleon. Some of the worst of the violence is called the Reign of Terror.<br /> <br /> The Reign of Terror was a period of the French Revolution following the creation of the First French Republic, massacres and numerous public executions took place in response to revolutionary fervor, anticlerical sentiment, and accusations of treason by Maximilien Robespierre and the Committee of Public Safety.<br /> <br /> There is disagreement among historians over when exactly &quot;the Terror&quot; began. However, there is a consensus that it ended with the fall of Robespierre in 1794. By then, 16,594 official death sentences had been dispensed throughout France, of which 2,639 were in Paris alone; and an additional 10,000 died without a trial.<br /> <br /> Not everyone was executed with a guillotine \u2013 those were elaborate mechanisms. Many people were just killed with the usual tools of swords, guns, knives, bricks, baguettes, and so on. Even so, Starek writes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I wish I could have just laid down right next to the guillotine and let the blood from each decapitation flow into my mouth. </div> </div> </div>During the chaos of the revolution \u2013 and the Terror in particular \u2013 Starek asserts\u2026<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u201c\u2026dozens of Camarilla vampires who had lived among the aristocracy died, sometimes dragged out of their havens during the day by the new revolutionary authorities. </div> </div> </div>Wiping out dozens (as in multiple of 12, so anywhere from 12 to 148) of vampires would have really gutted the local Camarilla. This is probably why some of the more high minded reforms of the revolutionaries and the Anarchs were able to make it into law and become a part of society. These included equality before the law and due process \u2013 neither or which exist in Camarilla law.<br /> <br /> Part of the take away here is that while the Anarchs had essentially been defeated and consumed by the Camarilla at Thorns, anarchs and other malcontents continued to exist. The system of the Camarilla created them, and every war and revolution gave them an opportunity to strike out and strike back. The French revolution was simply one such instance \u2013 albeit a more successful one.<br /> <br /> First Digression: As an aside, a lot of modern ideas, or at least visual imagery, of the French revolution and the Terror comes from <i>The Scarlet Pimpernel</i> a novel by Baroness Orczy, published in 1905. Western Movies have a similar influence about our ideas about the American West. The Scarlet Pimpernel has been made into a movie a few times. The novel is a bit like someone in the 1% writing fan-fic about another person in the 1% saving yet other people in the 1% from BLM protestors.<br /> <br /> Second Digression: My heuristic is that everything in the WoD is at least 10% worse than in the Real World. So, 18,254+ official death sentences had been dispensed throughout France since June 1793, of which 2,903+ were in Paris alone; and an additional 11,000+ executed without trial or prison. The Terror, depending on who you asked, ran from September of 1772 through July of 1794. That is 23 months, 92 week, or about 700 days. Which means on average 26 were being executed nationwide every day, and 4 every day in Paris.<br /> <br /> What a time to be a vampire in France.<br /> <br /> Third Digression: I hope Robespierre survived in the WoD as a vampire or a wraith.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T18:13:03-07:00","id":1407057,"title":"","content":"<b>CT Phipps' opinion on the French Revolution</b><br /> <br /> One of the things that V:TM runs into the problem of is the fact that it attempts to condense all of history into easily digestable bites that can sort of run into the problem of making it nonsensical. For example, there's &quot;two&quot; Anarch Revolts with the original one happening in the High Middle Ages and the 2nd one happening with the death of Prince Sebastian Juan Dominguez. You know, an entirely fictious revolt that only affects the state of California.<br /> <br /> This, of course, ignores the following events that seem like they would be rather important to the Anarchs vs. Camarilla:<br /> <br /> * The American Revolution<br /> * The French Revolution<br /> * The Haitian Revolution<br /> * The Scottish Uprising<br /> * The Mejii Revolution<br /> * The Bolshevik Revolution<br /> <br /> There's always a discussion over how much vampires should be involved in &quot;real&quot; world's history, I tend to view vampires always on the edge of it. They make things bloodier, nastier, and more violent while rarely changing the shape of history. For example, John Brown's Rebellion isn't going to have John Brown be a Brujah (albeit you can if that's going to be the focus of your game) but you might have some Brujah trying to help behind the scenes while Ventrue and Toreador try to stop it or blacken his name afterward.<br /> <br /> I take the view that Anarchs are not &quot;the good guys&quot; but they're sometimes on the right side of history. During the Civil War, I can easily see Brujah fighting for the Union and the Underground Railroad while also a bunch of Brujah fighting for the Confederacy. Not because of &quot;States' Rights&quot; but because some Brujah are just racist fucks. I imagine there were Nazi, Soviet, Anarchist, and French Resistance Brujah too.<br /> <br /> The French Revolution is a good setting for a Anarch revolt because it is the perfect place for a Brujah revolt against Toreador and Camarilla Elders before the usual problems happen: Brujah turning on each other, disagreeing on what sort of society to build after victory, and those getting bribed into betraying the cause. The Brujah are dominated by their rage and Beasts so they tend to &quot;lose&quot; whatever revolts they make because their rage never subsides.<br /> <br /> Interestingly, Jason Carl canonized some interesting facts about the French Revolution for LA By Night that are a bit &quot;Second Edition-esque&quot; but are still fun:<br /> <br /> * Francois Villon was living in Versailles as his haven.<br /> * He ghouled Marie Antoinette.<br /> * He and his guests openly did atrocities to amuse themselves.<br /> * He helped himself liberally to the French purse despite starvation.<br /> * Xelios built an elaborate underground complex underneath the place.<br /> * The Anarchs were aided by the Sabbat (and it's implied the two groups were indistinguishable at the time).<br /> * Lucita and Karsh were often his guests<br /> * Francois would sometimes murder his ghouls for no reason.<br /> * Francois claimed to have been a 2500 year old Carthagian vampire when he was, of course, just a 5th generation childe of Helena barely 200 years old at this time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/YmWogxyaIjA\" data-code=\"YmWogxyaIjA\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/YmWogxyaIjA/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> My view of the French Revolution is that I imagine that it was probably the center of another &quot;hunter's paradise&quot; where vampires got careless and arrogant in their power, only to result in hunters going on killing sprees and burning down the homes of wealthy undead or dragging them out into the sun. This decadent psychosis and Jason Carl's handling of things is also basically what happened in TRANSYLVANIA CHRONICLES.<br /> <br /> I'm intrigued by also the idea the European Sabbat and Anarchs weren't necessarily distinguishable at this time because much of the &quot;Modern Day&quot; Sabbat as we know them are products of the American Revolution as well as the absortion of the culture there. Before the power base moved to Mexico City, European Sabbat are basically indistinguishable from &quot;normal&quot; Anarchs and Pre-Dark Age elders.<br /> <br /> This is also when Madame Guile is Embraced and the French Revolution made a powerful impression on her of just how much Camarilla vampires Elders sucked. No pun intended. It might explain also how some Anarchs got away to fester since one of the most feared and hateful Justicars was on their side.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 08-08-2020, 09:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-09T00:00:52-07:00","id":1407096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1407057#post1407057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>CT Phipps' opinion on the French Revolution</b><br /> This, of course, ignores the following events that seem like they would be rather important to the Anarchs vs. Camarilla:<br /> <br /> * The American Revolution -Might start off encouraging some Anarch stuff, but is primarily a Cam vs Cam affair. This war is far too idealized. <br /> * The French Revolution - sure, it was a big enough clusterfuck. No doubt became Camarilla in the end.<br /> * The Haitian Revolution - looking at the event; There's no way this was anarch<br /> * The Scottish Uprising - not anarch, though more possible than Haiti.<br /> * The Meijii <i>Restoration</i> - not anarch, namely because it was successful.<br /> * The Bolshevik Revolution - Sure. But mortal opinion has so turned against this that maybe it's not a great idea to emphasize; Even if the USSR became a great place for vampires, the human reputation kinda spoils it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The first anarch revolt occuring during the end of the medieval/early renaissance was a smart move. That was the first big cultural shift with huge leaps in technology in a long, long time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-09T00:12:30-07:00","id":1407097,"title":"","content":"The American Revolution would have concerned the Sabbat a lot more at the time, but the Revised Anarchs book does put emphasis on the French Revolution which was influenced by the American Revolution. The French Revolution is pretty much the first event after the anarch revolt the book mentions. There's some mention of the American Revolution, but it seems like it wasn't influenced by kindred and more influenced vampires with it's writings by mortals like Jefferson, Franklin and the Brit Thomas Payne.<br /> <br /> The Haitian revolution seems like it'd offer a lot of good material. It is the only time in history that slaves managed to actually overthrow their masters and start governing themselves. Maybe some anarchs decided to ride the wave, but it'd seem like the locals were the main instigators and movers. You could have a lot of fun with various factions of Setites, Samedi, Brujah instigators, Cam plantation owners and anarch pirates taking advantage of the situation, though. Hmm, now I kind of want to run a game in the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14519-drhappyangry","name":"DrHappyAngry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14519_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-09T09:21:52-07:00","id":1407149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1407057#post1407057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* He helped himself liberally to the French purse despite starvation.<br /> * Xelios built an elaborate underground complex underneath the place.</div> </div> </div> </div>In game the complex is probably still under Versailles. That is a bit amusing. <br /> <br /> In terms of vampires controlling things, it is worth reiterating vampires can control - through Dominate, Presence and the blood bond - individuals and small groups of people. They cannot directly control masses of people and situations. Villon, in the WoD, probably influenced the selection of the finance ministers running up to the Revolution (and the decisions they made), this did not mean he was in real control of the French economy. Just that he made it all worse, which contributed to the French Revolution and the destruction of the Ancien R\u00e9gime and his own power base for decdes. This is the difference between having a 6 in intelligence on the character sheet and actually knowing what you are doing.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-09T09:28:30-07:00","id":1407150,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> in my opinion, the Jacobite Rebellion was a Toreador-backed uprising against the Ventrue power structure controlled by Mithras.<br /> <br /> Btw I love Outlander \ud83d\udc95.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-09T10:49:32-07:00","id":1407155,"title":"","content":"<b>\u201868</b><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wikipedia</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beginning in May 1968, a period of civil unrest occurred throughout France, lasting some seven weeks and punctuated by demonstrations, general strikes, and the occupation of universities and factories. At the height of events, which have since become known as May 68, the economy of France came to a halt. The protests reached such a point that political leaders feared civil war or revolution; the national government briefly ceased to function after President Charles de Gaulle secretly fled France to Germany at one point. The protests spurred movements worldwide, with songs, imaginative graffiti, posters, and slogans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agata &quot;the problem&quot; Starek missed the Revolution proper but was around for the May 68 protests.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And you know what? It was pretty great. This is one of those classic uprisings that people remember, and the first one I'm old enough to have participated in.<br /> -Sterek </div> </div> </div>I take it from that she has only been a vampire for 60 years or so. In any case, the May 68 riots in France drew many Anarchs (the vampires) and anarchs (the humans) from all over the place. She says she spent a night with Tyler, but that again may be a case of personifying Tyler in every hard ass independent woman who is unidentified. Vampires might be identifying Sterek as Tyler if they do not know who Sterek is and she doesn\u2019t name herself.<br /> <br /> So the Camarilla retreated and Villon again went into hiding. Sterek apparently diablerized a Camarilla vampire and generally enjoyed herself immensely.<br /> <br /> As with the Camarilla book, Anarchs is composed of multiple in-character discussions of one thing or another. Sterek\u2019s voice seems the most clearly developed, in her bouncing back and forth morally and ethically. She has moments of considerable violence and considerable insight \u2013 she notes the riots did not last long enough for the Anarchs to poison the events and what happened later. Few other vampires seem to have that level of insight into what they are and what they do.<br /> <br /> A takeaway here is the cyclical nature of these things. An established order becomes unsupportable. There is a revolution and riots that thrash things out, and often settle into becoming the new established order. Which becomes unsupportable\u2026<br /> <br /> A digression: And again, history does not repeat so much as it rhymes. Currently in America the economy has been massively slowed, if not stopped (albeit by a pandemic rather than protests) while schools and universities are closed, protests are ongoing, with supporting protests appearing in other nations. And so on\u2026<br /> <br /> In the WoD version of the demonstrations of the summer 2020, Sterek is probably involved a throwing flaming cars at people who irritate her.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-09T10:54:44-07:00","id":1407156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1407149#post1407149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In game the complex is probably still under Versailles. That is a bit amusing.<br /> <br /> In terms of vampires controlling things, it is worth reiterating vampires can control - through Dominate, Presence and the blood bond - individuals and small groups of people. They cannot directly control masses of people and situations. Villon, in the WoD, probably influenced the selection of the finance ministers running up to the Revolution (and the decisions they made), this did not mean he was in real control of the French economy. Just that he made it all worse, which contributed to the French Revolution and the destruction of the Ancien R\u00e9gime and his own power base for decdes. This is the difference between having a 6 in intelligence on the character sheet and actually knowing what you are doing.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>As one of my players said, &quot;A man with Intelligence 6 can fake being as good as a Intelligence 3 and Finance 3 financer. But he's got nothing on the actual experts.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-09T12:44:36-07:00","id":1407170,"title":"","content":"Honestly it just sounds like you don't want to believe in smart people. They're a myth that hurts the ego.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-09T12:51:11-07:00","id":1407171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1407170#post1407170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly it just sounds like you don't want to believe in smart people. They're a myth that hurts the ego.</div> </div> </div> </div>Being a former Mensa member, the important thing to know is that the smartest person in the world is not good at EVERYTHING and can make astoundingly stupid mistakes -- in large part because they believe that their expertise in one area translates to expertise in all areas.<br /> <br /> Plus just because you ARE smart doesn't mean you can't be tripped up by emotions or arrogance.<br /> <br /> Besides, if you're a perfect super genius elder who never makes ANY mistakes--you're a boring as shit character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-09T13:31:15-07:00","id":1407176,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m really smart too and I\u2019ve made major mistakes in judgment. Also, emotional intelligence is just as important as traditional intelligence.<br /> <br /> Not sure how we got from talking about Anarchs to talking about this, but that\u2019s my take on the issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-09T13:36:28-07:00","id":1407177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1407171#post1407171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Being a former Mensa member, the important thing to know is that the smartest person in the world is not good at EVERYTHING and can make astoundingly stupid mistakes -- in large part because they believe that their expertise in one area translates to expertise in all areas.<br /> <br /> Plus just because you ARE smart doesn't mean you can't be tripped up by emotions or arrogance.<br /> <br /> Besides, if you're a perfect super genius elder who never makes ANY mistakes--you're a boring as shit character.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. Emotions cloud your judgment, but they also form the basis for making that judgment in the first place. And anyone no matter how smart can mess up when they get too arrogant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-09T14:12:56-07:00","id":1407179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1407170#post1407170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly it just sounds like you don't want to believe in smart people. They're a myth that hurts the ego.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh for pity's sake. No one is saying that - what we are saying is 6 dots in Int on a character sheet doesn't make problems go away.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-09T14:18:40-07:00","id":1407182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1407179#post1407179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh for pity's sake. No one is saying that - what we are saying is 6 dots in Int on a character sheet doesn't make problems go away.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno, I think a guy who can fake being a mid-tier stock broker is pretty awesome by itself.<br /> <br /> It's just Intelligence 6 isn't what Lex Luthor has.<br /> <br /> Lex Luthor has Intelligence 6 *AND* Finance 5 *AND* Technology 5 *AND* Science 5.<br /> <br /> Not all Elders do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-09T14:39:13-07:00","id":1407186,"title":"","content":"there's intelligence 6+ in v5?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-09T14:48:30-07:00","id":1407188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1407186#post1407186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">there's intelligence 6+ in v5?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope.<br /> <br /> I think that's silly, though, as devoted a fanboy of V5 as I am.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-09T14:57:34-07:00","id":1407189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1407182#post1407182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lex Luthor has Intelligence 6 *AND* Finance 5 *AND* Technology 5 *AND* Science 5.<br /> <br /> Not all Elders do.</div> </div> </div> </div>First, Luthor might have those score but he can't get past his hate-boner for Superman causing him to make errors in judgement.<br /> <br /> Second, the Elder's have minions, who do work for the elder and fleece everyone as much as they can.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-09T19:45:41-07:00","id":1407216,"title":"","content":"There\u2019s a interesting discussion about how we measure \u201cintelligence\u201d and what counts as it, even really smart people make mistakes, or do things out of emotion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-10T01:35:28-07:00","id":1407247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1407216#post1407216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There\u2019s a interesting discussion about how we measure \u201cintelligence\u201d and what counts as it, even really smart people make mistakes, or do things out of emotion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. And even Kindred get overwhelmed by passion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-10T17:44:52-07:00","id":1407403,"title":"","content":"<b>Ten Nights that Shook the World</b><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u201cThe proletarians have nothing to lose but their chains. They have a world to win.\u201d<br /> \u2015 Karl Marx, The Communist Manifesto </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u201cThe Bolsheviks killed their own most loyal supporters at Kronstadt in 1921, because they failed to understand that the revolution no longer required revolutionaries, but obedient servants.\u201d<br /> \u2015 Peter Hitchens </div> </div> </div>The title of this section is a play on <i>Ten Days That Shook the World</i>, a 1919 book by the American journalist and socialist John Reed about the October Revolution in Russia in 1917, which Reed experienced firsthand.<br /> <br /> Oksana Dimitrovna Domasheva, a former member of the Brujah Council narrates this section of the book. She opens the entry with a section describing the USSR as a paradise, and has the insight to make the following statement.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Before you object to that statement, I ask you to consider <i>paradise for whom?</i><br /> \u2015 Domasheva </div> </div> </div>She goes on to assert that Camarilla vampires like to see themselves as apart from humanity, and cannot understand other approaches. This suggests the Brujah Council had a different approach, and she is going to tell us about it. However, there are apparently sharp limits to her insight, because the rest of the section is about how the Communist Vampires turned the entire nation into a kind of cattle pen, ruling over the humans. The hungry cold ones were destroying the idealists within a decade of the revolution, rejecting the idea of equality and destroying those who embraced the philosophy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Kindness is a virtue, but it doesn't make sense to advocate for full rights to mortals any more than it does to grant them to cows or dogs.<br /> \u2015 Domasheva </div> </div> </div>This sounds like an articulation of the view of many Camarilla elders and leaders, and even the philosophy of the characters of <i>LA by Night</i>, given their involvement in the nightclub massacre. The point being that Domasheva\u2019s denials are lies and fancy words \u2013 the Council\u2019s vampires were as separate from the humans at least as much as the Camarilla vampires. The Brujah Council worked like a carcinoma inside the Communist Party, in the same way groups of vampires do for whatever community or institution they infest and infect.<br /> <br /> Also, Anarchs is just the term the Camarilla uses now for all the vampires that are not a part of the Camarilla. The Soviet system, and the Brujah Council, were a long ways from anarchists. In fact, the communist system was one of the most controlling and stultifying in the world.<br /> <br /> Domasheva not only does not mention Baba Yaga, who in past editions defeated the Brujah Council by eating it. She says the system failed because of nostalgia and sentimentality on part of the vampires involved. For one thing, I do wonder how the Brujah Council worked and ruled cities, but Domasheva\u2019s statement and its tacit erasure of Baba Yaga is interesting on its own.<br /> <br /> More in a moment\u2026","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-10T17:55:11-07:00","id":1407404,"title":"","content":"<b>Follow up</b><br /> <br /> It occurs to me that a cold war era VtM game could be interesting, one where a major threat to the Camarilla is not the Sabbat but the Brujah Council. VtM itself did not appear until after the collapse of Communism and the fall of the USSR, so having communist spies and saboteurs as the villains felt done. And the Sabbat which started a unknown menace at the edge of Camarilla territory, were introduced as the major antagonists and later codified as a grab-bag of blood cultists terrorists lunatics.<br /> <br /> But it would be an interesting set up for a VtM game, set in the 1950s or 1960s, in Europe, were the Camarilla \u2013 in Europe at least \u2013 fears infiltration, subversion and attack by agents of the Brujah Council.<br /> <br /> It would be a bit like a Connery James Bond movie, or one of John le Carr\u00e9's books on Smiley, except all the major characters are vampires. And assholes without any redeeming characteristics.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1208,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","user":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","date":". 08-10-2020, 09:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-10T18:10:45-07:00","id":1407409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1407404#post1407404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Follow up</b><br /> <br /> It occurs to me that a cold war era VtM game could be interesting, one where a major threat to the Camarilla is not the Sabbat but the Brujah Council. VtM itself did not appear until after the collapse of Communism and the fall of the USSR, so having communist spies and saboteurs as the villains felt done. And the Sabbat which started a unknown menace at the edge of Camarilla territory, were introduced as the major antagonists and later codified as a grab-bag of blood cultists terrorists lunatics.<br /> <br /> But it would be an interesting set up for a VtM game, set in the 1950s or 1960s, in Europe, were the Camarilla \u2013 in Europe at least \u2013 fears infiltration, subversion and attack by agents of the Brujah Council.<br /> <br /> It would be a bit like a Connery James Bond movie, or one of John le Carr\u00e9's book on Smiley, except all the major characters are vampires. And assholes without any redeeming characteristics.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I really like this idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-10T19:25:36-07:00","id":1407419,"title":"","content":"So the Anarchs are massive hypocrites that end up even worst then the Camarilla at least with the treatment of Kine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-10T19:30:17-07:00","id":1407421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1407419#post1407419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the Anarchs are massive hypocrites that end up even worst then the Camarilla at least with the treatment of Kine.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that is a grievous error because many Anarchs are very openly about their hatred and disdain for Kine. Remember the first Anarchs were the basis for the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> SOME Anarchs are very much about caring for kine.<br /> <br /> OTHER Anarchs are disgusted by how much the Camarilla restricts their ability to abuse them (little as that may be).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-10T19:35:06-07:00","id":1407423,"title":"","content":"<span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> Thanks.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23952_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23952\" data-vbnamecard=\"23952\">Konradleijon</a> Yes, but that is hardly a surprise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-10T20:05:15-07:00","id":1407433,"title":"","content":"<b>CT Phipps on Soviet Russia</b><br /> <br /> In Soviet Russia, Brujah oppress Ventrue!<br /> <br /> I feel the need to take a moment to share my &quot;Ten Tips for running the Anarchs in V5&quot; list. <a href=\"http://unitedfederationofcharles.blogspot.com/2020/04/ten-tips-to-playing-anarchs.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://unitedfederationofcharles.blo...g-anarchs.html</a><br /> One of the things that I talked about there was the fact that I believed there was a substantial number of <i>Vampire: The Masquerade</i> players who disdained the Anarchs because they were the &quot;good&quot; faction in V:TM. One of the chief appeals of this game is the option of playing a &quot;bad guy&quot; with options ranging from being an Anti-hero like Wolverine and Ghost Rider to being a full-blown villain protagonist who eats humans like Pez.<br /> <br /> The Anarchs are not the good-guys of course, though you're probably going to find SLIGHTLY more High Humanity vampires among them than in the Camarilla's upper echelons. However, what makes the Anarchs interesting is that they're just as likely to be scumbags that terrify people as they are to be Maldavis Civil Rights activists. <i>The Lost Boys</i> are often talked about as a Sabbat pack but they're really just as likely to be Brujah Anarchs, riding up and down the boardwalk and murdering at will because they don't respect the Prince.<br /> <br /> The use of the Soviet Union as the ultimate example of an Anarch Free State is a very good choice because it nicely shows that a bunch of Anarchs are interested solely in making themselves the top dogs of Kindred society versus any societal reform. Even then, I think that may be overstating things for the article. The Soviet Union was a lot of things to a lot of people and while as a Christian anarchist, it was pretty much my idea of hell, I imagine the Brujah of it all had various ideas for what it should be.<br /> <br /> * Brujah who wanted to use it as the basis for a equalized post-capitalism society across the world.<br /> * Brujah who saw it as a way to establish vampire superiority over Kine.<br /> * Brujah who saw it as a nightmarish Empire and in need of overthrowing, especially Ukrainians.<br /> * Brujah who might give two shits about Kine but want a equalist society among vampires.<br /> * Brujah who saw it as the ultimate piggy bank for funding overthrows of vampire societies across the globe (mortals as well).<br /> <br /> Mind you, the 21st century makes it seem like the Brujah Council has basically reformed itself in the former Soviet Union and is back to its old tricks in the Russian Federation. I'm imagining that the &quot;New&quot; Anarch Free State probably has a few more Ventrue, Toreador, Tremere, and the like but they're all publicly Anarchs. Just the oligarch police state kind that are different from the Camarilla because, &quot;fuck you, we say we are.&quot;<br /> <br /> And if you think they'd join the Camarilla because of this, I'll laugh at you because the Brujah Council ruled as much territory at its height as the Camarilla ever did.<br /> <br /> As for Baba Yaga? Well, would YOU admit that 80% of your society was wiped out by the Wicked Witch of the West? A children's story?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This sounds like an articulation of the view of many Camarilla elders and leaders, and even the philosophy of the characters of <i>LA by Night</i>, given their involvement in the nightclub massacre. </div> </div> </div>Victoria Ash was having a bad day it seemed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 08-10-2020, 11:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-11T02:28:19-07:00","id":1407469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> * Brujah who wanted to use it as the basis for a equalized post-capitalism society across the world.<br /> * Brujah who saw it as a way to establish vampire superiority over Kine.<br /> * Brujah who saw it as a nightmarish Empire and in need of overthrowing, especially Ukrainians.<br /> * Brujah who might give two shits about Kine but want a equalist society among vampires.<br /> * Brujah who saw it as the ultimate piggy bank for funding overthrows of vampire societies across the globe </div> </div> </div>And the first category were killed off very quickly; some survived Lenin, none survived Stalin. Virtually everybody else to be embraced after that were chosen from 'the communist elite' (yeah, that should've been an oxymoron) <br /> <br /> Was it Brujah leadership on a local level though? I can't imagine it so. They are, after all, more people of a revolution than more people of a status quo; They can take the castle, but they can't hold the castle; They'll kill their own servants if they get mad enough.<br /> <br /> I do think there's a group you missed though:<br /> Globaly minded vampires who realise that cold war polarization makes thing bad for mortals everywhere and great for vampires everywhere. Would the USA have became such a right wing freedom shithole had the US not feared communism so much that mild socialist systems would be demonized for years to come? Would there be so many fascist dictators were they not 'needed' to overthrow communist regimes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-11T06:36:37-07:00","id":1407489,"title":"","content":"<i>The Nights that Shook the World</i> doesn't really say how much freedom, necessities and amenities the kindred of the Soviet Union had, or how they were organised. If we take Domasheva's word for it, it might have been a fair and plentiful society for kindred. She might have been part of a more priveliged class within that society if it wasn't. For a start, she evidently lived in Moscow, which has to be preferable to gulags, even if gulags have more accesssible food per kindred.<br /> <br /> I'd love to see a book about this or even a series. I've considered:<ul><li>New Wave Masquerade. Sort of like <i>New Wave Requiem</i>, it would be an immediate prequel to the first VtM books. I picture it more focussed on America, but this could be when the Brujah Council is really falling apart.</li> <li>A Cold War book about the time when there were effectively four sects: the Camarilla, Sabbat, Anarch Free States (as opposed to Anarch subjects of princes) and the Brujah Council. This could start in 1940s, possibly covering the early Anarch Free States of California and post-war Europe. Maybe it could feature the odd cross-sect nuclear apocalypse conspiracy.</li> <li>A book starting with the birth of the Brujah council. This could show the Brujah Council when some of them gave a damn about kine and how they overcame the old regime of the Camarilla, Sabbat or whoever else was there.</li> </ul><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-11T06:53:31-07:00","id":1407493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1407421#post1407421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that is a grievous error because many Anarchs are very openly about their hatred and disdain for Kine. Remember the first Anarchs were the basis for the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> SOME Anarchs are very much about caring for kine.<br /> <br /> OTHER Anarchs are disgusted by how much the Camarilla restricts their ability to abuse them (little as that may be).</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh so it\u2019s like the American Revolution? A bunch of entitled hypocrites that (partly) rebelled against The slightly less racist British.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-11T07:09:06-07:00","id":1407497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1407493#post1407493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh so it\u2019s like the American Revolution? A bunch of entitled hypocrites that (partly) rebelled against The slightly less racist British.</div> </div> </div> </div>\ud83d\ude02\ud83d\ude02\ud83d\ude02 you\u2019re not entirely wrong...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-11T07:19:25-07:00","id":1407499,"title":"","content":"It's almost <i>precisely</i> like the American revolutin<br /> <br /> Cam: We just busted our asses calming the inquisition for you, do you think you could obey the rules as payment/to keep us all safe so we don't struggle with that the next time? <br /> <br /> An: What? You want something from us? No<br /> <br /> Cam: but we've given you rights and saved you from...<br /> <br /> An: Well, can I have way more say in what goes on despite being a businessmen who's only interest is lowering taxes for myself? <br /> <br /> Cam: What? No, we were the ones who put in the effort, we've been... <br /> <br /> An: FREEDOM, FREEDOM, NO TAXATION WITHOUT REPRESENTATION, FUCK THE MAN, <span style=\"font-size:10px\">LET ME KEEP MY SLAVES</span>. <br /> <br /> Other neonates: What? <br /> <br /> An: I can give you what you want! screw the Camarilla and their rules!<br /> <br /> Those that botched the Int+pol roll: FREEDOM, FREEDOM, NO TAXATION WITHOUT REPRESENTATION, FUCK THE MAN. <br /> <br /> <br /> An: Great, we've fought off the Camarilla thanks to... nevermind, definetly not any other sect: no more rules or regulations; you're all going to be my bitches. <br /> <br /> An neonates: What? <br /> <br /> An: I've taken away everything that protected you. Now drink my blood and become mine. You're all going to owe me boons just for staying in my territory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-11T07:58:34-07:00","id":1407507,"title":"","content":"What do you mean we can\u2019t own fifty ghouls? Fuck, we are not allowed to randomly murder Kine. Stop oppressing me, let me murder all the Kine I dislike.<br /> <br /> <br /> Fun tip, if you want a lot of ghouls , just blood bound a Neonate Vampire and instruct them To blood bound lots of ghouls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-11T08:31:44-07:00","id":1407512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1407493#post1407493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh so it\u2019s like the American Revolution? A bunch of entitled hypocrites that (partly) rebelled against The slightly less racist British.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, I'm not sure where the hypocrisy is coming from?<br /> <br /> Don't you have to claim you're for Kine in the first place?<br /> <br /> Seriously, if you think the Anarchs are one group then you have failed to grasp them at all. They are multiple groups that all hate the Camarilla more than each other.<br /> <br /> I'd argue it's the French Resistance more. You have the Gaulist and you have the Communist.<br /> <br /> The only reason they're not killing each other is the Vichy and the Nazis.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1407507#post1407507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you mean we can\u2019t own fifty ghouls? Fuck, we are not allowed to randomly murder Kine. Stop oppressing me, let me murder all the Kine I dislike.<br /> <br /> <b>Fun tip, if you want a lot of ghouls , just blood bound a Neonate Vampire and instruct them To blood bound lots of ghouls.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>How awful a ST am I that my immediate reaction is, &quot;Your haven is then burned down by a dozen ghouls out to free their master from his evil slave lord&quot;?<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 08-11-2020, 11:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-11T08:34:47-07:00","id":1407513,"title":"","content":"Will they can\u2019t claim to be about liberty and equality, when 99.99% of the population need not apply to your freedom, even if they don\u2019t make any claims of Protection for the Kine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-11T08:35:23-07:00","id":1407514,"title":"","content":"Anarch vs Camarilla has never been about Kine...has it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-11T08:40:50-07:00","id":1407515,"title":"","content":"Will no like the feeding source is like super important. And I know both leaderships don\u2019t give a shit about the feeling and life quality of the Kine.<br /> <br /> But the Camarilla never makes any claims about being about \u201cequality\u201d and bitching about oppression while treating less powerful people, A,E the Kine like shit,<br /> <br /> The Camarilla treats Kine like shit but they don\u2019t claim to be a force for equality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-11T08:42:18-07:00","id":1407516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1407513#post1407513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Will they can\u2019t claim to be about liberty and equality, when 99.99% of the population need not apply to your freedom, even if they don\u2019t make any claims of Protection for the Kine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes it can.<br /> <br /> If you're a black Brujah living in the Antebellum South and have the sole goal of killing the white plantation class as well as their Toreador and Ventrue masters then you are not a hypocrite if you claim to be fighting for freedom. Said Brujah may have absolutely no sympathy for the former slave-owning class and offer them no protection against Kindred that want to prey upon them and may only extend protections to ex-slaves even if he's Prince of Atlanta.<br /> <br /> Similarly, a Brujah who in occupied Poland.<br /> <br /> Or a Lakota Caitiff who insists that you only feed on white people outside of his Reservation.<br /> <br /> The heart of the Anarchs is they are angry at the system They have very good ideas of who exactly is a victim and who exactly is a victimizer. Very rarely are they fighting for a utopian Star Trek society where everyone is equal because they are usually Embraced from or keenly aware of the oppressed.<br /> <br /> It also runs into the fact that the ONLY group that will have ANY vampire who wants to protect Kine is in the Anarchs. It's just not all of them or a doctrine of their organization as a whole. They're the vegans of the vampire world.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Will no like the feeding source is like super important. And I know both leaderships don\u2019t give a shit about the feeling and life quality of the Kine.<br /> <br /> But the Camarilla never makes any claims about being about \u201cequality\u201d and bitching about oppression while treating less powerful people, A,E the Kine like shit,<br /> <br /> The Camarilla treats Kine like shit but they don\u2019t claim to be a force for equality. </div> </div> </div>Yes, which is why they will always be worse and the worst Anarchs are better than the best Camarilla.<br /> <br /> &quot;What about the Sabbat?&quot;<br /> <br /> Shut up!<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 08-11-2020, 11:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-11T08:59:51-07:00","id":1407524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1407499#post1407499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's almost <i>precisely</i> like the American revolutin<br /> <br /> Cam: We just busted our asses calming the inquisition for you, do you think you could obey the rules as payment/to keep us all safe so we don't struggle with that the next time?<br /> <br /> An: What? You want something from us? No<br /> <br /> Cam: but we've given you rights and saved you from...<br /> <br /> An: Well, can I have way more say in what goes on despite being a businessmen who's only interest is lowering taxes for myself?<br /> <br /> Cam: What? No, we were the ones who put in the effort, we've been...<br /> <br /> An: FREEDOM, FREEDOM, NO TAXATION WITHOUT REPRESENTATION, FUCK THE MAN, <span style=\"font-size:10px\">LET ME KEEP MY SLAVES</span>.<br /> <br /> Other neonates: What?<br /> <br /> An: I can give you what you want! screw the Camarilla and their rules!<br /> <br /> Those that botched the Int+pol roll: FREEDOM, FREEDOM, NO TAXATION WITHOUT REPRESENTATION, FUCK THE MAN.<br /> <br /> <br /> An: Great, we've fought off the Camarilla thanks to... nevermind, definetly not any other sect: no more rules or regulations; you're all going to be my bitches.<br /> <br /> An neonates: What?<br /> <br /> An: I've taken away everything that protected you. Now drink my blood and become mine. You're all going to owe me boons just for staying in my territory.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the Camarilla's view on the subject and generally how idealistic Anarchs often feel the Movement ends up betraying its views. People who actually think that the Movement has the potential to become better. You also forgot:<br /> <br /> 1. <b>Camarilla Subversion</b>: Anarch Leader: OH yes, I'm going to be playing the system to our advantage. You can call me &quot;Prince&quot; now. Here's the Justicar to recognize me as your leader.<br /> <br /> 2. <b>Camarilla Rebound</b>: The Camarilla comes back and kills everyone in a couple of months and hands out the domain to someone new (and executes the Prince for failure).<br /> <br /> 3. <b>Did you really think you could control the Mob?</b>: The Anarchs have ANOTHER revolt to overthrow the slave-owning Blood Bound Prince. You see the guy asking to Blood Bond everyone is now surrounded by a bunch of people who promptly rip him apart and diablerize him as a &quot;traitor to the revolution.&quot;<br /> <br /> The problem with being an Anarch leader is the fact that the Camarilla EXPECTS you to be treacherous and scheming then rewards you for it. When you do it with the Anarchs, they're quite happy to put you up against the wall with the rest of the traitors.<br /> <br /> So, I suppose it's less the Americna Revolution than the French.<br /> <br /> The best ending for Anarch Revolts are probably:<br /> <br /> 1. <b>The Primogen are You</b>: The Anarchs successfully overthrow the Prince and then proceed to divide up their territory among them as equals. Together, as a group, they kill anyone who tries to take their territory away from them.<br /> <br /> 2. <b>Reform under Siege</b>: An Anarch who establishes a place where Kindred aren't oppressed or Kine is going to have a helluva time staving off attacks against Sabbat, Camarilla, or other Anarchs. How long can their utopia last and what compromises do they have to make like Embracing new soldiers to fight for it and controlling businesses to keep the Masquerade?<br /> <br /> 3. <b>Doesn't Matter</b>: For some Anarchs, it doesn't matter what replaces the Old Prince. All that matters is the Old Prince is dead. All debts are cleared and you've established you're a force to be reckoned with. Maybe it was never about ending the Prince system but just letting people know that they'll be treated like Mussolini or Qadaffi.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-11T09:09:02-07:00","id":1407526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1407512#post1407512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Again, I'm not sure where the hypocrisy is coming from?<br /> <br /> Don't you have to claim you're for Kine in the first place?<br /> <br /> Seriously, if you think the Anarchs are one group then you have failed to grasp them at all. They are multiple groups that all hate the Camarilla more than each other.<br /> <br /> I'd argue it's the French Resistance more. You have the Gaulist and you have the Communist.<br /> <br /> The only reason they're not killing each other is the Vichy and the Nazis.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> How awful a ST am I that my immediate rea