rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-11T18:28:10-07:00","id":1407634,"title":"","content":"The Tzimisce have all the big eyes, small mouth ghouls. No, really, they do. They ghouls didn't start that way...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-11T18:34:11-07:00","id":1407639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1407634#post1407634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Tzimisce have all the big eyes, small mouth ghouls. No, really, they do. They ghouls didn't start that way...</div> </div> </div> </div>My headcanon is that Lucita is dozens of Elders' waifu and she HATES it.<br /> <br /> Victoria Ash gets all Tsundere about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T16:56:06-07:00","id":1408282,"title":"","content":"<b>Dee\u2019s Blood Guide to the Anarch Free States</b><br /> <br /> Here Dee, a thirsty Brujah, discusses getting blood in the Anarch Free States of Southern California. This is more about her encouraging people to go out and find their own personal preference than it is a nuts and bolts discussion of hunting. In any case, it is surprising how often this gets over looked in a game about game about playing murderous vampires.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Politics is boring, but there's something funny about the way so many people just can't grasp the idea of a de-centralized system.<br /> -Dee </div> </div> </div>Dee notes that there is no singular prince (at least no recognized prince) in the Free States \u2013 and one of these responsibilities of a prince is to dole out recognized hunting territories. Without the centralized authorities assigning hunting grounds, those territories are a free for all. Which is probably part of the appeal of playing a party of vampires in the Free States.<br /> <br /> She expressly notes the number of gangers is shifting, and so it the territories they try to claim.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> However, if you have the guts for it, poaching is very easy.<br /> -Dee </div> </div> </div>Given the shifting nature of the territories, accidental poaching is probably inevitable. This I am calling a story hook; the PCs getting permission to hunt somewhere only for them to run into another ganging asserting that territory is theirs.<br /> <br /> Dee makes a reference to Louis Fortier as an acilla, but the Ventrue is just another of the local barons. I don\u2019t know if this is supposed to be an error on the part of Dee herself, or whomever wrote the section.<br /> <br /> As always vampire social life seems to involve a bar \u2013 according to Dee one of the best places for vampires seeking to expand their palate is A Taste of L.A.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's a dim, ramshackle warehouse, but it's also neutral territory between the gangs, so you can drop by, get a lay of the land and do some comparison shopping between all the local tough guys.<br /> -Dee </div> </div> </div>Dee also makes mention of the \u201cChinese vampires trying to establish their own place here,\u201d which is enigmatic in its ambiguity. Chinese vampires are present, but they may or may not be Cathayan, and the Great Leap Outward may or may not have happened.<br /> <br /> There is a similar note of ambiguity with \u201cPrince\u201d Tara, who is openly known as a Camarilla stooge. Dee does not get into the status of Tara, only that the bad faith Anarch leader will not succeed.<br /> <br /> Given Dee\u2019s obsession with at least trying all types of blood it is reasonable to ask if she is a reliable narrator. (Well, no she is not.) A better question is, Is Dee any more unreliable than any of the other narrators? Probably not.<br /> <br /> Arguably, vampires are all about blood and all the politicking they do is just busy work. With that perspective, Dee is refreshingly straight forwards in her goals and objectives.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What kind of blood truly makes me happy?\u201d<br /> -Dee </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T17:34:29-07:00","id":1408289,"title":"","content":"I should point out that this section replaces a bunch of Thin Blood parents discussing how to care for their kids. Apparently, this really creeped the fuck out of a lot of people and was removed for some reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T17:38:27-07:00","id":1408291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1408289#post1408289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I should point out that this section replaces a bunch of Thin Blood parents discussing how to care for their kids. Apparently, this really creeped the fuck out of a lot of people and was removed for some reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>That part is still in the version I am reviewing, I've just not gotten to it yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T17:41:52-07:00","id":1408292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1408291#post1408291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That part is still in the version I am reviewing, I've just not gotten to it yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Weird, I had heard otherwise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T17:53:27-07:00","id":1408294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1408282#post1408282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Dee\u2019s Blood Guide to the Anarch Free States</b>Dee notes that there is no singular prince (at least no recognized prince) in the Free States \u2013 and one of these responsibilities of a prince is to dole out recognized hunting territories. Without the centralized authorities assigning hunting grounds, those territories are a free for all. Which is probably part of the appeal of playing a party of vampires in the Free States. She expressly notes the number of gangers is shifting, and so it the territories they try to claim.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the things in ANARCHS UNBOUND was the fact that basing the LA Free State on gangs was, perhaps, not the most tasteful of things to be done. Bluntly, because of so many young African American and Latino men being murdered in a crisis being exploited for FUN. It's part of the reason that Franklin was created as a contrast to CJ in GRAND THEFT AUTO because they wanted to show the dark side to the somewhat glamourized version of gang life in LA. So they stated that the constant warring and modeling of Anarch gangs on, well, gangs, had changed after the 90s.<br /> <br /> In LA by Night with Jason Carl, the Barons have formed a &quot;Baron's Council&quot; consisting of Therese, Isaac Abrams, Nines, and a couple of other characters. The video game characters trumping over the ones in LA by Night.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Given the shifting nature of the territories, accidental poaching is probably inevitable. This I am calling a story hook; the PCs getting permission to hunt somewhere only for them to run into another ganging asserting that territory is theirs. </div> </div> </div>I think Anarchs respecting each other's domains runs the risk of being a little too Camarilla-ish personally. The Sheriff beating you down for drinking out of your lane is pretty much a run of the mill action in Camarilla domains so I think that any Anarch who wants to punish someone for drinking in their territory has to do that by themselves (or get their buddies to help). Even then, I wonder how much the fights over domain really are. It seems like people might only care if they kill on their territory, do it messily, and/or maybe target the vampires' own preferred vessels.<br /> <br /> Which is something you almost have to do deliberately as a provacation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Dee makes a reference to Louis Fortier as an acilla, but the Ventrue is just another of the local barons. I don\u2019t know if this is supposed to be an error on the part of Dee herself, or whomever wrote the section. </div> </div> </div>I've always been fond of Louis Fortier due to the fact he's a horny (thirsty?) as fuck Ventrue with three vampire brides like Dracula. One of the vampire brides is actually a member of the Sabbat and I wondered if that's why Louis isn't mentioned in modern nights. Even then, Louis was also a collaborator with the Cathayans because he's always been a guy who sides with the strongest side. Don Sebastian, the Anarchs, and then the Chinese vampires.<br /> <br /> The thing is that I can see Ming Xiao OR the Anarchs killing him for that last bit of treason, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Dee also makes mention of the \u201cChinese vampires trying to establish their own place here,\u201d which is enigmatic in its ambiguity. Chinese vampires are present, but they may or may not be Cathayan, and the Great Leap Outward may or may not have happened. </div> </div> </div>The focus on making Vampire: The Masquerade: Bloodlines one of the big parts of canon kind of puts the White Wolf developers who hate the Cathayans inbetween a rock and a hard place. The game doesn't make any sense without the Kuei-Jin but they may not even exist. I think this is a decent compromise with the assumption that Ming Xiao and other Chinese vampires invaded but their exact nature is questionable.<br /> <br /> I've actually converted Ming Xiao to a Tzimisce bloodline in the past. Which actually fits her given she displays Spirit Thaumaturgy and Koldunic-esque sorcery plus the ability to shift her body, features, and become an enormous octopus monster.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There is a similar note of ambiguity with \u201cPrince\u201d Tara, who is openly known as a Camarilla stooge. Dee does not get into the status of Tara, only that the bad faith Anarch leader will not succeed. </div> </div> </div>An update on Tara:<br /> <br /> In LA by Night [which is canon], Tara was captured by Isaac Abrams and San Diego has fallen into civil war between the Anarchs and Camarilla factions there after she tried to bring in the city to the Camarilla only for her followers to revolt.<br /> <br /> Which...of course they would.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 08-14-2020, 08:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-15T04:23:59-07:00","id":1408331,"title":"","content":"Huh, neat timing with this thread. I finally got around to reading 5e Anarchs.<br /> <br /> For the most part, I like the book a lot. But one of the things that jumps out to me is how the vampires... are dicks.<br /> <br /> Like, Agata commits diablerie for fun and giggles. The vampire she helps out casually admits to killing his ghoul's family. The &quot;Beast on a Leash&quot; Toreador couple kill their doms and remark it's okay. Juniper casually kills men who pick her up at gas stations so she can hold up in their houses for the day. The vampire parents on the private forum feed vitae to their children (or just feed from them) and kill nosy social workers. The Bahari vampire says her sire killed her family. The Brujah Council vampire says brutally oppressive and authoritarian regimes are awesome because it's easier to feed. And so on and so forth.<br /> <br /> I mean, okay. Vampires <i>are</i> dicks. But compare this to 1e/2e Chicago by Night. There are tons of asshole vampires like Son, Gordon Keaton, Ballard, Jacob Schumpter, etc. who had Humanity scores of 0 and committed atrocities in line with the ones described above. But the book <i>also</i> had vampires who tried to do better than that, or who simply felt ashamed and revolted at the atrocities they committed. When Critias killed a 12-year-old girl in frenzy, he couldn't live with himself and fled into seclusion for decades (centuries?). When Cedrick Calhoun murdered his brother, he served as a guardian angel to the man's children and ensured they were financially provided for. Damien broke the Masquerade using Celerity to save a mortal from a speeding car. Tons of characters commit &quot;remorse Embraces&quot; on victims they kill (DuSable and Maldavis) or otherwise make efforts to atone for the wrongs they commit. One of the most nuanced characters of all was Khalid, who was a Humanity 2 Golconda seeker and committed twisted crap like Embracing a pair of emotionally damaged, incest-committing underage siblings, but still valued morality and aspired to be something better than he was. (He just wasn't very good at it.)<br /> <br /> I don't feel like many (any?) of the characters in this book hold much value for human life or feel particularly bad about the atrocities they commit. The most we see are some almost sarcastic-feeling &quot;I feel bad&quot; remarks, and a Gangrel mountain climber who tried to use his powers to save his stranded mountaineer human friend, but was too late and decided to feed on the guy's fresh corpse. I feel like there is an almost tongue-in-cheek sense of humor from the authors that trying to be anything besides a monster is a joke, in a way that was missing even from Revised (where the vampires were also more dickish, but the predominant tone was serious). Very few vampires feel horrified over their condition on a moral level, even though the book takes pains to emphasize what monsters they are. I think that really cuts out a lot of the game's pathos, and that the book would have benefited from some Critias, Calhoun, Damien, etc. characters to contrast the &quot;diablerie feels good&quot; Agatas.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1408289#post1408289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I should point out that this section replaces a bunch of Thin Blood parents discussing how to care for their kids. Apparently, this really creeped the fuck out of a lot of people and was removed for some reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's the wrong way to go about it. I mean, it was delightfully fucked up. The problem was that <i>all three</i> of the vampires in their discussion forum advocated feeding on or ghouling their kids, so I didn't feel any sympathy for cleavers as a movement. Why not have added a &quot;voice of reason&quot; vampire parent who called out the others for being so fucked up?<br /> <br /> Anarchs Unbound had a cleaver parent who didn't do anything bad to her own kid. She was mentioned as having surprisingly ruthless hunting methods, and that her son was shy and clingy for his age, but that was it. She seemed like she was just trying to get by and prioritizing her son's welfare over that of strangers. Possibly to their terminal expense, but it felt like actually feeding on or ghouling her son was a line she wouldn't cross. I thought that was a nuanced and compelling take on cleavers. <br /> <br /> I feel like the authors might be conflating &quot;sympathetic vampire parent&quot; with &quot;endorsement of being a vampire parent.&quot; Obviously, being a cleaver is a bad idea, because all it takes is one ill-timed frenzy for things to go horribly wrong. But maybe there are cleavers with no other options, as far as childcare, and who don't want to consign their kids to life in the foster care system (assuredly even more dysfunctional in the WoD than in our own world). There is no sense of heartbreak or parents trying to do right by their kids when the only options are bad options. Just twisted fucks who enjoy feeding on their kids and murdering social workers and who I can write off as monsters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":3110,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","user":"False Epiphany","date":". 08-15-2020, 07:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-15T07:18:36-07:00","id":1408350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>False Epiphany</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1408331#post1408331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Very few vampires feel horrified over their condition on a moral level, even though the book takes pains to emphasize what monsters they are.</div> </div> </div> </div>I will be discussing the art in the book later. I mention this here because in the first version of the book a Salubri appears in some of the art. And that is as close as the book ever gets to what you are discussing. But both the <i>Anarchs </i>and <i>Camarilla </i>books received reedits and changes after the problems with the Chechnya section in the <i>Camarilla </i>book. In these changes, the &quot;feeding blood to babies&quot; section was cut, and the Salubri art edited to just be a vampire. So even that was removed from the book.<br /> <br /> I hope Salubri reappear sooner or later. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-15T10:18:55-07:00","id":1408371,"title":"","content":"I still haven't read these books for myself, so I'm on the outside looking in and this is probably an ignorant question:<br /> <br /> Has Golconda been touched upon at all, and if not, could the Salubri be on hold until someone finds a way to make the idea gel with the new Humanity system?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-15T10:47:18-07:00","id":1408380,"title":"","content":"Golconda was mentioned a few times in Camarilla and once (so far) in Anarchs. No one, in character, seems to know what it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-16T14:43:20-07:00","id":1408580,"title":"","content":"<b>The Conclave of Prague</b><br /> <br /> This entry, by Dalia Nakache, opens with section that thematically connects to the last section, Specifically, about vampires who may want to just hunt and do their thing and generally ignore larger sect politics. Basically she says no one \u2013 Anarchs included \u2013 can just be hunters anymore because of the Camarilla Inner Circle.<br /> <br /> In short, as the Second Inquisition emerged as a threat, the Camarilla began feeding it specific information on the Anarchs and the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When the SWAT team comes to knock on your door, they're there because a bunch of aged assholes half the world away decided you were expendable.<br /> -Nakache </div> </div> </div>This is probably more hyperbole than literal fact. Consider, this assumes the vampires in question have something as specific as a recognized address, which the Camarilla leadership knows and can turn over to the SI. I don\u2019t think I\u2019ve ever played a vampire who had a haven in the form of an apartment or anything so mundane. The last one I played dwelled in the ruins of abandoned high school. Also, why would a vampire tell others about their havens \u2013 or at least why would they not lie about their havens?<br /> <br /> Even so, the rhetoric stands. Worldwide some surprisingly well trained, well informed, and well equipped hunters began killing vampires. And a SWAT team raid during the middle of the day could easily wreck some neonates or even ancilla foolish enough to just sleep in the closet of an apartment or duplex. Nakache argues this is why Bell killed Hardestadt at the Conclave of Prague in 2012, which led to the larger Brujah defection from the Camarilla and to the Anarch. Bell has never specified why he did it, which just leaves it all open for speculation \u2013 and lets Storytellers fill in the details.<br /> <br /> Nakache is also critical of viewing elders as masters of the jyhad and manipulation, creatures capable of foreseeing and controlling everything. She argues rightly that the blowback from the elders response to the SI specifically triggered the murder of Hardestadt, the Brujah defection, strengthening the Anarchs, and so on. These are probably not things the elders wanted, at least not all those events.<br /> <br /> Nakache says that the Camarilla no longer has \u201cno claim to universality,\u201d but they Anarch do. This is debatable. The Camarilla never really claimed universality, or dominion over the Giovanni, Settites, Ravnos, and Banu Haqim. I don\u2019t think they now try to claim Dominion over the Brujah and Gangrel. So this is a bit of rhetorical bluster, which sounds more better to an Anarch than to a Camarilla vampire.<br /> <br /> However, she does make a solid point, which has game possibilities, about Camarilla withdrawing and abandoning territory.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So what does this mean for you? In many cities, the Camarilla has had to retreat, only controlling part of the territory, leaving the rest to Anarchs. Many of their holdings in the mortal world have been abandoned, and if you're smart enough you can find them and take them over. After all, the banker addicted to vampire Blood doesn't really have the option of saying no to you if you're her only hope of avoiding blood withdrawal.<br /> -Nakache </div> </div> </div>Finding such weaknesses, and claiming them and exploiting them, and fighting to hold them, could easily be the subject of an entire campaign for an Anarch pack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1208,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","user":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","date":". 08-16-2020, 06:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-16T15:32:21-07:00","id":1408600,"title":"","content":"The Camarilla actually did claim all vampires were members of the Camarilla by nature. It's just some were more members than others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-17T20:43:57-07:00","id":1408841,"title":"","content":"<b>Untitled Section</b><br /> <br /> This bit has no title, and doesn\u2019t appear in the table of contents \u2013 which I think has to be an error.<br /> <br /> Anyway, Hesha Ruhadze writes about how the Ministry (formally the Followers of Set) almost joined the Camarilla. However, he also writes an observation about how the retreat of the Camarilla has opened up new areas of war between the elders and the youth. This thematically connects to the last entry, which more or less said the same thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The elders are as deadly as ever, but the war between the old and the young acts as a convenient distraction if you want to pursue other goals altogether.<br /> -Ruhadze </div> </div> </div>Ruhadze does not get into what he thinks of as the weakness of the Camarilla, though he suggests it is cowardice (probably among other flaws). He also does not specify what those \u201cother goals\u201d might be. He does appear to be resigned to his (temporary) fate as an Anarch, following the Ministry joining the movement. Ruhadze, 400 year old survivor and corruptor, is also savvy enough to know the Ministry is stronger among the Anarchs than it would be on its own when it comes to dealing with the SI.<br /> <br /> Ruhadze argues that for many elders, personal relationships will trump sect allegiance. So vampires (Ventrue, Tremere) who are BFF with Brujah will probably remain BFF even after the events of the Prague Conclave. This is debatable I think, given how betrayal is second nature to vampires of all clans and ages.<br /> <br /> However, he also says\u2026<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This has always been the rule in high level sect politics: The rules apply to the young, not to the old.<br /> -Ruhadze </div> </div> </div>Which is to say, the rules do not apply to people with power.<br /> <br /> He circles back to an earlier point about the burgeoning war between Anarchs and the Camarilla (and the SI by implication) will provide a lot of chaos he can exploit. But he does not specify what he wants.<br /> <br /> He probably remains a Theophidian, which is to say someone who follows the doctrine of Set. This doctrine is something of a cross between Gnosticism and Sith philosophy. Pursuing these goals, and teaching the philosophy to the Anarch will define his goals (and probably the goals of other members of the Ministry) in general terms, but not specific ones. What this means specifically is up to the Storyteller.<br /> <br /> As an aside, Ruhadze is a Georgian (as in the nation) surname. But Hesha himself supposedly comes from Nubia, or in southern Egypt and northern Sudan (as modern nations). Which is to say it is a long ways from the nation on the Black Sea.<br /> <br /> Edit: I wonder what the Path of Typhon would look like in the V5 moral system.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1208,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","user":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","date":".  Hesha dared me to do it. 08-17-2020, 11:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-17T21:16:56-07:00","id":1408846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1408841#post1408841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> He probably remains a Theophidian, which is to say someone who follows the doctrine of Set. This doctrine is something of a cross between Gnosticism and Sith philosophy. Pursuing these goals, and teaching the philosophy to the Anarch will define his goals (and probably the goals of other members of the Ministry) in general terms, but not specific ones. What this means specifically is up to the Storyteller.<br /> <br /> As an aside, Ruhadze is a Georgian (as in the nation) surname. But Hesha himself supposedly comes from Nubia, or in southern Egypt and northern Sudan (as modern nations). Which is to say it is a long ways from the nation on the Black Sea.<br /> <br /> Edit: I wonder what the Path of Typhon would look like in the V5 moral system.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, I wouldn't be surprised if Hesha's membership in the Ministry is due to a catastrophic loss of faith in the traditional Typhonist interpretation of Set. The events of Beckett's Jyhad Diary ended in a tremendously shocking place for Hesha as he and the others (supposedly) recovered a coffin of Enoch at the direction of Kemintiri.<br /> <br /> Hesha is, basically, Belloq to Beckett's....well, Belloq. Even Belloq-er. However, he IS an archaeologist and discovering the coffin of Enoch basically is heavy proof of the Caine myth versus the Set one.<br /> <br /> Like if you're a devout (for lack of a better) atheist and discover Jesus' tomb with no body but some blood-soaked bandages.<br /> <br /> No, it MIGHT NOT change your opinion on the subject and doesn't necessarily mean you'll become a believer but it certainly will cause you to reevaluate some things.<br /> <br /> Mind you, it isn't likely to change what kind of person Hesha is, just put him in an irreconcilable doctrinal split with the orthodox Church of Set.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 08-18-2020, 12:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-18T00:28:49-07:00","id":1408862,"title":"","content":"Weird analogy, If I found myself in such a tomb, what would make me think it's the tomb of jesus? And if his body is missing, could it not be stolen... <br /> <br /> So too, if I was a dedicated Setite, and found some &quot;proof&quot; of nodism over set, i'd have to wonder what part of the story was wrong, or what wrong assumptions I made, or perhaps at what point did the setites start saying X rather than Y. The Setites know they're not that reliable when it comes to the Truth and that many of their stories are allegorical rather than the actual Truth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-18T00:39:00-07:00","id":1408864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1408862#post1408862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Weird analogy, If I found myself in such a tomb, what would make me think it's the tomb of jesus? And if his body is missing, could it not be stolen...</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't need to make you believe Jesus is divine. Just acknowledges there's proof of SOMETHING here and that contradicts your previous worldview.<br /> <br /> Same with Enoch being real and Hesha or so my idea goes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So too, if I was a dedicated Setite, and found some &quot;proof&quot; of nodism over set, i'd have to wonder what part of the story was wrong, or what wrong assumptions I made, or perhaps at what point did the setites start saying X rather than Y. The Setites know they're not that reliable when it comes to the Truth and that many of their stories are allegorical rather than the actual Truth. </div> </div> </div>Except in BJD the Church of Set and the Children of Weppawaut declare Set is the absolute truth and literal along with the execution of all who deviate from the doctrine in the slightest way.<br /> <br /> *sarcasm mode* Strangely, this does not end their schism problems. *sarcasm mode*<br /> <br /> But I admit I am tickled by the idea of fundamentalists for a God of Chaos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 08-18-2020, 03:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-18T02:28:57-07:00","id":1408878,"title":"","content":"As Camp as the Settites might be, Church of Set/Children of Weppawaut are too ridiculous and realistically, would be destroyed quite quickly for their unpopular bullshit heresy. &quot;Fundamentalists for a God of Chaos&quot; aren't going to be the best of the Followers. And sure I guess you could have one charismatic leader duping his followers into crusading for political reasons but...<br /> <br /> Yeah that's definitely something that belongs to a radical fringe group, not anything major. It's not a very attractive prospect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-18T05:59:16-07:00","id":1408898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1408878#post1408878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As Camp as the Settites might be, Church of Set/Children of Weppawaut are too ridiculous and realistically, would be destroyed quite quickly for their unpopular bullshit heresy. &quot;Fundamentalists for a God of Chaos&quot; aren't going to be the best of the Followers. And sure I guess you could have one charismatic leader duping his followers into crusading for political reasons but...<br /> <br /> Yeah that's definitely something that belongs to a radical fringe group, not anything major. It's not a very attractive prospect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, I see the change to the Followers of Set as something that's been kicking off for the past 1000 years. They assumed they could integrate all these other religions into Set worship and it turned out that they severely overestimated how much your average Satanist, sincerely decent Voodoo worshiper (who dropped the ball there?), Loki worshiper, and Erisian cultist wanted to join the Sith Way.<br /> <br /> I admit, I'd like to see the Children of Osiris and Serpents of Light [yes, the Sabbat group] official parts of the Ministry, having decided to help the other Setites form their own faction.<br /> <br /> I also see Kemmnitri's hand in slowly forcing this split.<br /> <br /> It's been building for a long time.<br /> <br /> Mind you, you need the Elders to be dramatic, overreact, and tyrannical to justify an Anarchs game.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-18T06:14:25-07:00","id":1408904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1408898#post1408898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mind you, you need the Elders to be dramatic, overreact, and tyrannical to justify an Anarchs game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is why they usually don't do that sort of shit. <br /> <br /> Also they tend not to embrace people outside of the cults they control. So... If your satanist isn't a gnostic champion against the demiurge it'd be really strange she ever got taken into the fold. <br /> <br /> Now, The SotL, other than having a rainbow snake, I don't know much about. But the CoO... Completely opposed belief system. Just because mainstream setites hate these... control freaks, does not mean they're going to get into bed with Osiris. Sure the Nazis and the Soviets might take out Poland together, but that was really so they could get closer to killing eachother...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-18T07:27:20-07:00","id":1408925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1408904#post1408904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is why they usually don't do that sort of shit</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? How dull. How many have the self insight to realize they are being dramatic, overreact, and tyrannical so they can stop themselves? I have a pet theory that the most successful vampires were sociopaths and psychopaths while alive - those people are normally known for their ability to self regulate. And given human pettiness (and vampire pettiness grows out of human pettiness) I can totally believe that some of them probably have strict rules about how to go about being chaotic and if you are getting them wrong, then you are doing chaos wrong.<br /> <br /> In any case, the gnonist Sith scholars and warriors should find fertile ground among the Anarchs. The Camarilla may regret driving the one to join the other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-18T07:45:48-07:00","id":1408928,"title":"","content":"vampire elders (and most vampires really) truly are drama queens,<br /> that's part of the fun,<br /> pragmatics get boring real quick<br /> <br /> according to the players guide (revised), they're not very mature either,<br /> at least, not anymore than they were at the time of their embrace<br /> <br /> even the kuei-jin view cainites as children who never grow up","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":10998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","user":"Pleiades","date":". 08-18-2020, 10:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-18T09:10:39-07:00","id":1408944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1408904#post1408904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is why they usually don't do that sort of shit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have yet to meet an Elder other than Anatole who isn't a raging narcissistic psychopath. They're smart assholes but every one of them is basically a cat: addicted to pleasure, murder, and absolute rule of its territory.<br /> <br /> Here's the Gangrel antediluvian in torpor.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://static.boredpanda.com/blog/wp-content/uploads/2019/07/1-5d2cd2a0ac058__880.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">https://static.boredpanda.com/blog/w...ac058__880.jpg</a><br /> <br /> The thing is they're SMART about these fundamentally corrupt things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1408904#post1408904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also they tend not to embrace people outside of the cults they control. So... If your satanist isn't a gnostic champion against the demiurge it'd be really strange she ever got taken into the fold.</div> </div> </div> </div>We've met like 5 4th Generation Setites, BTW. Quite a lot of them turn out to have been women Set wanted to fuck. That's not to say they weren't capable, quite the opposite as we see with Kemnintiri, but its a point that Set gave the gift of godlike power to a number of people for absolutely petty reasons. Which fits with the fact that he's a cult leader and takes advantage of his followers.<br /> <br /> We also have a huge section of SETITES REVISED that is devoted to the fact that more progressive Setites are not actually interested in orthodoxy but spreading a more generic &quot;corruption&quot; through local cults.<br /> <br /> Which is to say, &quot;There's a lot of Setites who aren't gnostic champions against the demiurge. Which is why the Church of Set wants to kill them.&quot;<br /> <br /> Ironically, you've just shown why you think the Church of Set and Wepawaut vampires are RIGHT.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now, The SotL, other than having a rainbow snake, I don't know much about. But the CoO... Completely opposed belief system. Just because mainstream setites hate these... control freaks, does not mean they're going to get into bed with Osiris. Sure the Nazis and the Soviets might take out Poland together, but that was really so they could get closer to killing eachother... </div> </div> </div>My enemy is my enemy is my enemy in the Jyhad. Mind you, I fully believe that Keminitiri's writer implied the Children of Osiris aren't actually a good guy organization but a fanatical cult designed by Kemintiri purely to get revenge on her sire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 08-18-2020, 12:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-18T10:57:41-07:00","id":1408974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1408925#post1408925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Really? How dull.</div> </div> </div> </div>Key word: Usually <br /> But the settite puritan thing is too large scale. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How many have the self insight to realize they are being dramatic, overreact, and tyrannical so they can stop themselves? . </div> </div> </div>Now here's the thing: Most elders who survive that long probably do have the self insight to realize such things. The issue is they feel external pressures that cause them to feel they need to be dramatic, react big, and behave tyrannical in order to survive. <br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> I like the Settite religion's the issue. Spreading corruption without a purpose is wank; You either need a convincing philosophy or a Demon needs to be offering you the goods. The Setites cover the former and Baali are their mirror for the latter. Just using non-demonic insanity as an excuse creates shitty NPCs and even shittier PCs. It's one thing to tell snake-puritans to fuck off and get out, it's another thing to utterly abandon the philosophy just because a the snake-puritans were dicks about it. <br /> <br /> Also I really want to play a Settite who has the goal of wanting to become Set's concubine....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-18T11:12:59-07:00","id":1408976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1408974#post1408974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">0<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> I like the Settite religion's the issue. Spreading corruption without a purpose is wank; You either need a convincing philosophy or a Demon needs to be offering you the goods. The Setites cover the former and Baali are their mirror for the latter. Just using non-demonic insanity as an excuse creates shitty NPCs and even shittier PCs. It's one thing to tell snake-puritans to fuck off and get out, it's another thing to utterly abandon the philosophy just because a the snake-puritans were dicks about it.<br /> <br /> Also I really want to play a Settite who has the goal of wanting to become Set's concubine....</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Clan Book: Baali did a good job of separating the two.<br /> <br /> The Setites revel in sex, drugs, and rock and roll while also laud selfishness as well as ambition. They are a religion of &quot;evil&quot; in so much that they believe restraint is bad and society is full of repressive rules you must break. It's not actually EVIL necessarily and will appeal to people like the Anarchs who hate society. Oppressed minorities and religious dissidents will find themselves drawn to the Setites as well.<br /> <br /> The Hyborian influences of John Milinus' CONAN THE BARBARIAN are more than just snake motiffs as John Milinus used the most heinous and evil thing to inspire his Set cultists:<br /> <br /> HIPPIES<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://encrypted-tbn0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn%3AANd9GcRZ0f8iK3EmkE0IWpzsRZxWk4XGq9O_iN7dIw&amp;usqp=CAU\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Manson would be a Follower of Set leader in that he combines the hippie &quot;peace, love, and sex&quot; thing with total control. Mind you, the racism is a bit hard to justify.<br /> <br /> The Baali are not playing Conan the Barbarian or the Judeo-Christian &quot;angst&quot; setting that other vampires are. They are playing Call of Cthulhu. They're both SAN 0 Investigators and Cthulhu cultists simultaneously. The Baali, IMHO, shouldn't be spreading corruption and acting like handsome Devils. They are playing <i>Call of Cthulhu</i> and their cults are not interested in sex, drugs, or freedom.<br /> <br /> No, the Baali are like, &quot;Okay, I need to roast this baby over the BBQ here because otherwise the enormous snake monster that lives under the city will rise and destroy us all.&quot;<br /> <br /> Or:<br /> <br /> &quot;Okay, I need to roast this baby over the BBQ here because otherwise the enormous snake monster that lives under the city will NOT rise and destroy us all.&quot;<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.stack.imgur.com/hWw1Q.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> I think the best way to differentiate them is Baali are Nephandus or some very warped version of the Technocracy in that their focus is entirely keeping reality safe or blowing it sky high. The Followers of Set are more like a very evil branch of the Cult of Ecstasy or Demon: The Descent. They think they're Morpheus in The Matrix, freeing your mind so one day the God-Machine can be beaten.<br /> <br /> The Baali are like, &quot;Sexy? Right. Have you come to the wrong religion. I toss Gulfora 6 teenagers to torture to death and eat. There's nothing sexy about what she does to them even if they die with a smile on their face.&quot;<br /> <br /> The thing is about the Setites is that by &quot;freeing your mind&quot; from rules, you will find people who find the rules stupid. Like, why SHOULD we worship Set over our own God of Sex and Chaos?<br /> <br /> Hecate, Aphrodite, and Eris are just fine for Ambrosia the Greek Setite.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 08-18-2020, 02:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-18T13:31:17-07:00","id":1408995,"title":"","content":"Yet you've been indoctrinated into a setite cult, passed through the gates of mystery, earned your embrace, and taught that the other faiths are masks<br /> <br /> at best, you can tell yourself that Set is really a mask for your way more cool and ancient god. Or you could go the other way and make yourself the god, but it's pretty unlikely you'll adopt a sincere faith in something 'newer' than Set, unless your sire was real sloppy with you. <br /> <br /> Re Baali: The lovecraftian lot shouldn't be the whole clan. <br /> -Thralls serving a demon master who wants a cult because of course it does. Such Baali often tangle with other Baali and infernalists who serve different demons. <br /> -folks who want nothing to do with the bloodline or demons and really try hard to hide their identity. Think of nosferatu Cleopatras. Unfortunately the writers of late seem to be under the misguided belief that Baali are the vampire nephandi or BSD and you need to be willing to get your soul inverted... nah they're just another bloodline that have a link to demons. <br /> Baali make great anarchs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 08-18-2020, 04:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-18T14:08:50-07:00","id":1409002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1408995#post1408995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yet you've been indoctrinated into a setite cult, passed through the gates of mystery, earned your embrace, and taught that the other faiths are masks<br /> <br /> at best, you can tell yourself that Set is really a mask for your way more cool and ancient god. Or you could go the other way and make yourself the god, but it's pretty unlikely you'll adopt a sincere faith in something 'newer' than Set, unless your sire was real sloppy with you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, you seem to be taking the orthodox Church of Set view about this. &quot;THEY'RE DOING IT WRONG!&quot;<br /> <br /> You just don't believe the dissidents exist versus thinking they should be stamped out.<br /> <br /> Quite a few of these faiths are older than Set as we know it. Set is not really an &quot;old&quot; Egyptian god. But yes, basically I see plenty of Setites indoctrinate people into their faiths and then these people either reject it later or just flat out lie about accepting it. We have plenty of signature characters who talk about their faith in the Midgard Serpent or Loki while basically thinking Set is just irrelevant.<br /> <br /> Of course part of the problem is a lot of these faiths are polytheist and the Setite Aeon talk is nonsense to them since their &quot;mask of Set&quot; doesn't have a Satanic adversarial relationship to the gods.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Re Baali: The lovecraftian lot shouldn't be the whole clan.<br /> -Thralls serving a demon master who wants a cult because of course it does. Such Baali often tangle with other Baali and infernalists who serve different demons.<br /> -folks who want nothing to do with the bloodline or demons and really try hard to hide their identity. Think of nosferatu Cleopatras. Unfortunately the writers of late seem to be under the misguided belief that Baali are the vampire nephandi or BSD and you need to be willing to get your soul inverted... nah they're just another bloodline that have a link to demons.<br /> Baali make great anarchs. </div> </div> </div>Eh, Baali look at Infernalists and think of them as poseurs. It's ignorance of infernalism by outsiders that the Baali are the &quot;Infernalist&quot; clan. The Sabbat have many more infernalists than the Baali and there's undoubtedly many Tremere who regularly deal with demons in a transactional fashion.<br /> <br /> Baali looked down on these guys as Hot Topic Goths versus their hardcore Punk.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-18T14:23:52-07:00","id":1409008,"title":"","content":"The split between the fundamentalist elders and the gnostic or polytheist younger vampires is what completely justifies the Ministry's move to the Anarch faction.<br /> <br /> For all the character development Hesha has received over the decades, this is also the most development the clan has received since they were first introduced. Somebody finally embraced how weird they are and gave the clan a story that could be meaningful in the modern nights.<br /> <br /> ETA: I take it as self-evident that those 4th Generation Hierophants in Egypt and Africa know better than anybody that Set is dead and not coming back. They're his heirs, who rebuilt the cult to serve themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11599,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","user":"Reasor","date":". 08-18-2020, 05:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-18T14:50:02-07:00","id":1409014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1409008#post1409008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ETA: I take it as self-evident that those 4th Generation Hierophants in Egypt and Africa know better than anybody that Set is dead and not coming back. They're his heirs, who rebuilt the cult to serve themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>But is he dead or DEAD-DEAD?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-18T15:09:12-07:00","id":1409021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1409008#post1409008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The split between the fundamentalist elders and the gnostic or polytheist younger vampires is what completely justifies the Ministry's move to the Anarch faction.</div> </div> </div> </div> but that in itself isn't very justified. These so-called &quot;fundamentalist&quot; elders don't have great reasons to make this move. There's little to no benefit for them. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ETA: I take it as self-evident that those 4th Generation Hierophants in Egypt and Africa know better than anybody that Set is dead and not coming back. They're his heirs, who rebuilt the cult to serve themselves. </div> </div> </div>And thus it would be wise not to dismantle it. <br /> <br /> <br /> Setites taking over the anarchs because it looks like good ground for spreading influence is fine, but the setites don't need their own anarch revolt; their whole clan is about that revolutionary-cult life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-18T15:11:17-07:00","id":1409023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1409021#post1409021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> but that in itself isn't very justified. These so-called &quot;fundamentalist&quot; elders don't have great reasons to make this move. There's little to no benefit for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is you basically are going, &quot;Because the people who would make up the Ministry don't exist.&quot;<br /> <br /> Except they did and have since Revised.<br /> <br /> The thing is I don't think the Church of Set are wrong. Sometimes you need to exterminate half your clan. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Setites taking over the anarchs because it looks like good ground for spreading influence is fine, but the setites don't need their own anarch revolt; their whole clan is about that revolutionary-cult life. </div> </div> </div>Because when I think of groups that never have any internal divisions, civil strife, and divisions I think of religions and revolutionaries.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-18T17:07:11-07:00","id":1409039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1409014#post1409014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But is he dead or DEAD-DEAD?</div> </div> </div> </div>That heifer's ultradead. I like to think the World of Darkness version of the Dead Sea Scrolls contains an apocryphal gospel about how Jesus struck Set down with fire, lightning, and roundhouse kicks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-18T19:11:52-07:00","id":1409052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1409008#post1409008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The split between the fundamentalist elders and the gnostic or polytheist younger vampires is what completely justifies the Ministry's move to the Anarch faction.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are also parallels between the split in the Banu Haqim - some are traditionalists, and some are not. And those who are not have defected from the main clan and joined a sect, for protection from their many (many) enemies and for fresh opportunities to exploit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-18T23:42:48-07:00","id":1409081,"title":"","content":"I don't see a oroblem with young setites (not on the path of typhon) fighting against the elders, but these theopodians are really in a weird caricature level of antagonism towards the rest of the clan. like they want to be the aeons the whole clan is geared towards fighting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-19T11:56:27-07:00","id":1409185,"title":"","content":"Walk Among Us<br /> <br /> The next section proper is a fit of flash fiction serving as a transition from one thematic section of the book to another. In the flash fiction section she is almost encouraging another vampire to dress like they shop entirely at HotTopic. I'm starting to think of Dee, the Brujah, as more or less Gilly the Perky Goth from Dork Tower.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://scontent-dfw5-2.xx.fbcdn.net/v/t1.0-9/15894728_1213936558643605_5587937842459559631_n.jpg?_nc_cat=107&amp;_nc_sid=e3f864&amp;_nc_ohc=IEeusB91olMAX8_9DBu&amp;_nc_ht=scontent-dfw5-2.xx&amp;oh=10a0e822fbdd41be667b60568271e52a&amp;oe=5F6327A8\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> In any case, the previous sections were about Anarch history and some other general uniting themes. The next sections move on to the current state of the world for Anarchs. I think <i>Anarchs </i>is flowing better than <i>Camarilla</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-19T15:27:25-07:00","id":1409237,"title":"","content":"The Anarchs are rebuilt enough as a concept as this point that I'm being won over from my objection to the sidelining of the Sabbat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-19T15:30:39-07:00","id":1409238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1409237#post1409237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Anarchs are rebuilt enough as a concept as this point that I'm being won over from my objection to the sidelining of the Sabbat.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that was necessary, personally.<br /> <br /> Imagine the plotlines of defections to the Anarchs from Loyalists and the Sabbat suddenly finding the &quot;joke&quot; sect stealing cities as well as having three Clans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-19T18:35:21-07:00","id":1409257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1409238#post1409238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Imagine the plotlines of defections to the Anarchs from Loyalists and the Sabbat suddenly finding the &quot;joke&quot; sect stealing cities as well as having three Clans.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see Tzimisce - always tetchy and independent minded anyway - going to the Anarchs in the same way Lasombra are going to the Camarilla. On a related note, I have long thought all the clans and bloodlines should be represented among the Anarchs. Runaways, defectors, spies pretending to be defectors, dissidents, the hunted and persecuted, and so on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-19T18:40:22-07:00","id":1409259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1409257#post1409257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can see Tzimisce - always tetchy and independent minded anyway - going to the Anarchs in the same way Lasombra are going to the Camarilla. On a related note, I have long thought all the clans and bloodlines should be represented among the Anarchs. Runaways, defectors, spies pretending to be defectors, dissidents, the hunted and persecuted, and so on.</div> </div> </div> </div>I always found it a little weird that was the Sabbat's hat. That they've appealed somehow to every single clan with their Blood cult military.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-19T18:44:22-07:00","id":1409262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1409259#post1409259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That they've appealed somehow to every single clan with their Blood cult military.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. I can see a lot of vampires being too lazy, too selfish, to0 indifferent to the jyhad, too cowardly, and so on to ever join or function inside the Sabbat. But they could all work well inside the what-ever-goes Anarchs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-19T23:27:03-07:00","id":1409302,"title":"","content":"The Sabbat would always beat the Anarchs. They've got so much more cohesion. Your average anarch would be thinking *It's not on my territory so I won't do anything till it is* and they'll get swallowed one by one as a result. <br /> <br /> Now, as to the Sabbat having the most blood diversity... <br /> Yeah, of course they do. <br /> They win wars, they press gang anyone, and those people embrace more into their ranks. <br /> <br /> The Camarilla is built from the best clans for the modern world; Bar dementation They don't have clan specifics, they have three broadly applicable disciplines that let them fit a variety of roles, whilst, say, Obtenebration might be powerful in warfare but it's pretty shitty for nightly living. Generalists in nature are just way more successful than specialists. The Camarilla accomadates the in-group of generalist clans and the Sabbat attracts all the freak clans because it's all about living a very specialist friendly lifestyle where the effort is more communal and they can divide labour more, also they go to war a lot for all those clan-specific combat disciplines to work well... and the Anarchs tend to lean far more to the Camarilla than the Sabbat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-20T00:28:54-07:00","id":1409308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1409302#post1409302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Sabbat would always beat the Anarchs. They've got so much more cohesion. Your average anarch would be thinking *It's not on my territory so I won't do anything till it is* and they'll get swallowed one by one as a result.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd argue we already have the answer to that because the Camarilla has no military so its always the Anarchs fighting the Sabbat and driving them out.<br /> <br /> The Camarilla's Elders no sense of nationalism so the only people actually willing to fight for their cities who aren't brainwashed ghouls are the Neonates, Ancilla, and rebels who live there.<br /> <br /> It helps that the Anarchs are also not necessarily Low Humanity nutjobs with only the barely remains of a brain left.<br /> <br /> Mind you, if the Black Hand-Black Hand shows up, the Anarchs are fucked but that's what you get with vampire Special Forces.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Camarilla is built from the best clans for the modern world; Bar dementation They don't have clan specifics, they have three broadly applicable disciplines that let them fit a variety of roles, whilst, say, Obtenebration might be powerful in warfare but it's pretty shitty for nightly living. Generalists in nature are just way more successful than specialists. The Camarilla accomadates the in-group of generalist clans and the Sabbat attracts all the freak clans because it's all about living a very specialist friendly lifestyle where the effort is more communal and they can divide labour more, also they go to war a lot for all those clan-specific combat disciplines to work well... and the Anarchs tend to lean far more to the Camarilla than the Sabbat. </div> </div> </div>FYI, an illustration of how different games have different interpretations?<br /> <br /> <b>My Take</b>: The Camarilla is ruled by a bunch of decadent sociopathic nobles who live off the wealth and blood of humans while cowardly hiding behind wealth as well as power. The Anarchs are formed of the more down to Earth vampires from a variety of ideologies as well as competing gangs. The Sabbat are a bunch of bestial cultists and their Elders who are identical to the Camarilla's, just a bit more willing to show the stuffed human family art and baby wine upfront.<br /> My take on MyWifeIsScary's?<br /> <br /> <b>MyWifeIsScary</b>: The Camarilla is ruled by incredibly intelligent super-predators, geniuses, and chessmasters who are protected by savagely loyal citizens willing to die for them. The Sabbat is equally comeptent, following posthuman morality and brainwashed soldiers following their own Illuminati-esque Elders. Anarchs are kind of the spoiled children unable to cut it in either sect.<br /> <br /> Both are equally valid because it's all up to your Storyteller.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 08-20-2020, 03:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-20T01:11:27-07:00","id":1409313,"title":"","content":"The Anarchs fight the Sabbat for the Camarilla because they live under Camarilla rule. In the event of No Anarchs, The Camarilla throws their Camarilla neonates at the problem whilst their ghouls hunt the Sabbat during the day and the Ventrue, Toreador and Tremere arrange for buildings to be demolished and filled with concrete or for people to be arrested or for. <br /> <br /> Neither sect is filled with hyper competent people, but there are enough competent people to guide and manipulate their lessers into conflict. Anarch cities, having the least amount of social pressures by the nature of anarchs, are piss poor. Even if the anarchs are all motivated, they're still like the spanish republic during their civil war. And unlike the Camarilla, their attempts to hide behind their wealth and power (A perfectly legitimate strategy) aren't as successful since they average at a dot less when it comes to resources and more than a few dots when it comes to influence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-20T07:33:19-07:00","id":1409350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1409313#post1409313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Anarchs fight the Sabbat for the Camarilla because they live under Camarilla rule.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not anymore. The Camarilla has disowned them. So whatever replaces the Sabbat will not be contending with the Anarchs to get to the Camarilla.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-20T08:26:19-07:00","id":1409359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1409350#post1409350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not anymore. The Camarilla has disowned them. So whatever replaces the Sabbat will not be contending with the Anarchs to get to the Camarilla.</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems so far that this idea isn't going to be one that holds traction in many cities. There's some backpedaling in the supplements. In any case, the Cam can still likely use prestation to get the anarchs to fight the Sabbat, and the Sabbat primarily waged war against the Camarilla because they were THE other sect 90% of the time. Now the Camarilla are secluded,fortified and closer knit whilst the Anarchs are the big target ripe for the conquest. The Camarilla would be grabbing popcorn if it didn't make them vomit blood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-20T10:04:44-07:00","id":1409375,"title":"","content":"So archons and justicars aren't a thing anymore?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-20T10:42:34-07:00","id":1409379,"title":"","content":"<b>Enlightenment in the Blood</b><br /> <br /> In this section an unnamed vampire provides commentary on an ongoing series of stories about a Masquerade breach in Berlin.<br /> <br /> First up, the vampire making these comments is named by himself or others. However, does identify themselves as a former Archon turned Anarch. I think it is probably Theo Bell \u2013 I cannot think of any other Archon\u2019s who defected to the Anarchs.<br /> <br /> The Masquerade breach occurs in Friedrichshain in 2017. Friedrichshain is a district in Berlin, Germany. Formerly part of East Berlin, Friedrichshain is now one of the trendy districts of Berlin and has experienced gentrification. This breach occurred near nightclub hopping crowds of mortals and involved the destruction of the then Prince of the city by Anarchs. Though not named the Prince was probably Abraham Wolff (he appears in Beckett\u2019s Jyhad Diary).<br /> <br /> The evolving story, and the comments from the former Archon, basically shows how a Masquerade breach is more of a process than an event. It also shows how these things will bring about SI involvement, and that is also a process. Do not forget that the SI itself is a major player.<br /> <br /> The Anarchs are not, and cannot be, as centralized and tyrannical as the Camarilla. This means its leadership is less prone to dealing out random cruelties and humiliations. It also means the Anarchs are less able to control and cover up a Masquerade breach. In this case, Wolff had compromised and corrupted local law enforcement. None of the Anarchs had that level of control. Without his singular control, no one was around to keep the Masquerade neat and tidy. And this goes on for months, leads to the revelations by the media of wide spread corruption inside the police force and so on. It further leads to an \u201cinternational task force, coordinated by Interpol\u201d stepping in to handle the situation because of connections to international criminal syndicates. That international group is (or at least easily could be) a front for the SI.<br /> <br /> Berlin is in the hands of the Anarchs, and has been since the destruction of Wolff in 2017. But how long will it take for the SI to do to Berlin what they did to London?<br /> <br /> All of which leads to the idea of using a Masquerade breach, and the ensuing SI hammer drop, as a strategy in the jyhad. Some Anarchs cause a breach in a Camarilla domain, or the other way around, and then get out of the way. The SI comes in a kills a lot of vampires. This makes the domain vulnerable to the one who triggered the breach in the first place.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-20T11:03:19-07:00","id":1409387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1409375#post1409375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So archons and justicars aren't a thing anymore?</div> </div> </div> </div>They're Special Forces and Generals without an army.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-20T11:30:07-07:00","id":1409395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1409379#post1409379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Anarchs are not, and cannot be, as centralized and tyrannical as the Camarilla.</div> </div> </div> </div>Absurd.<br /> <br /> The Camarilla can no longer be so tyrannical; If they treat you unfairly, it's now easy to leave, so they can't really do that if you have value to them. The Camarilla have given up their monopoly. They aren't the only law of the land, the anarchs are right over there, there's a lot of them, and they're doing just fine.<br /> <br /> The Anarchs, meanwhile, are bound by no rules but their own. The only checks and balances for anarch tyranny is the mentality that someone might fight back because, y'know, the baron is a neonate. But I suppose if said neonate baron was clever, got his fingers into key pies and bound a number of vampires to himself... yeah. The Camarilla prince will it least reach for a plausible excuse when he removes your head, and at least a blood hunt is sporting; the Anarch Baron can execute you just because he doesn't like the way you look. A lot of the 'Bullshit Camarilla rules and regulations' protected <i>you</i>, and they're gone with the anarchs. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-20T11:34:52-07:00","id":1409398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1409395#post1409395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Absurd.<br /> <br /> The Camarilla can no longer be so tyrannical; If they treat you unfairly, it's now easy to leave, so they can't really do that if you have value to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Camarilla no longer needs a reason to kill Anarchs and Caitiff and Thin Bloods. Besides, where are you going to leave TO?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-20T11:43:03-07:00","id":1409402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1409398#post1409398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Camarilla no longer needs a reason to kill Anarchs and Caitiff and Thin Bloods. Besides, where are you going to leave TO?</div> </div> </div> </div>All of this - the Camarilla no longer extends its (dubious anyway) legal protection to anyone called Anarch. And one Camarilla city is much like any other, in terms of administration; rule by undead sociopaths who don't like outsiders. That is assuming the Anarchs survive the trip in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-23T19:44:53-07:00","id":1410000,"title":"","content":"<b>No Prince, No Caine</b><br /> <br /> Right. This section. It\u2019s not bad, or good, but that rather forgettable middle ground.<br /> <br /> Here Salvador Garcia (who Dee described as a &quot;Che&quot; Guevara figure - or at least he wants to be), writes about the different types of Anarch groups and individual roles of vampires in Anarch communities.<br /> <br /> According to Garcia\u2019s essay, different Anarch groups include; a simple life (those withdrawing from the jyhad and Anarch v Camarilla battles as much as possible to do their own thing), gangs (your proto typical biker outfit or street gang or gun running outfit or smugglers or some such), cells (groups acting in a covert manner for some reason), and everything else.<br /> <br /> Different roles include; Barons (local leaders, ideally there are a number of them in any large territory the Anarch hold), Defense (keeping the Camarilla out), Emessaries (messengers and ambassadors between Barons and Anarch groups), Sweepers (Anarch who patrol the territory and eliminate problems), spies (who, well, spy on other group \u2013 usually but not always the Camarilla).<br /> <br /> Garcia also says that suicide among Anarch is high \u2013 it is high among the Camarilla as well. I wonder for which group the rate is higher?<br /> <br /> He also describes Rants, which are apparently the only time Anarchs get together \u2013 so they can bitch about the Man.<br /> <br /> As an aside, the title appears to be a play on the Irish phrase \u201cBona na Croin.\u201d In English this is \u201cNeither collar nor crown.\u201d Which is to say, \u201cI will not be a slave (held by a collar) and will acknowledge no king above me.\u201d Probably all of Anarch philosophy might be boiled down to this single sentence.<br /> <br /> I appreciate the brevity of the sections in this book \u2013 and brevity is the soul of wit. However, here it could have used some examples, which Garcia does not really get into. Some of sections which follow give examples of the different groups, but they are scattered about. Likewise the idea that the only time Anarchs really get together is for a Rant is both dull and hard to believe \u2013 that\u2019s it, really?<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1208,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","user":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","date":". 08-23-2020, 11:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-23T20:05:20-07:00","id":1410002,"title":"","content":"My examples\u2026<br /> <br /> Simple Life Group \u2013 Omega Omega Omega; an unofficial frat house at Humbolt University in Berlin. They rarely get up to the usual frat house stuff, but spend a lot of time reading ancient tomes, experimenting with things man was not meant to know, and so forth. They are home to a lot of Ipsissimus Tremere, but are not limited to that group.<br /> <br /> Gangs - Perros Malvados; a group of coyotes (human traffickers) who smuggle people across the US / Mexico border. Someone is every group they move across always disappears into the darkness with them, forever.<br /> <br /> Cells \u2013 Chicago Underground; a group of Anarchs in the Windy City trying to stay off the radar of Prince Jackson and Sheriff Damien. Baby Chorus is too well known to really be a cell.<br /> <br /> Event \u2013 The Anniversary of the death of the old prince is usually a time for Anarch to get together and enjoy themselves. This includes a Rant, but it is not limited to such an event. Barons may offer minor boons to whomever gives the best performance during the event.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-24T12:58:02-07:00","id":1410115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1409259#post1409259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always found it a little weird that was the Sabbat's hat. That they've appealed somehow to every single clan with their Blood cult military.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's mainly an error by the writers who attach onto the wrong thing when they originally read about whatever topic. With the Sabbat, that was obviously the concept of &quot;anti-tribu&quot; so that all clans had to have anti-tribu although this made little sense. (Another big issue is the idea that the Anarch Revolt only seemed to affect the clans of the Camarilla and Sabbat, and not the Independent Clans (except as helpers to the Anarchs of other clans). We should have seen more details on how the Setites, Giovanni, and Ravnos experienced the Revolt in their own ranks. I'm willing to give the Assamites a pass because they're supposed to be very different from the other clans - much smaller, greater control, and the Revolt presented them with an opportunity they never had before or since. Although the revised depiction with its subclans now creates the same dynamic as everyone else.)<br /> <br /> Although I think Montreal By Night is great in many ways, I think they shoved every clan or bloodline into it that they could even though it didn't make sense for there to be any Samedi in the city's Sabbat. I think there were a few other nonsense clans also in there.<br /> <br /> While I do think that in these very large sects like the Sabbat and Camarilla, there probably are members of every clan in there for whatever odd historical reason, it goes a bit too far with the Sabbat. In Revised, they listed the Kiasyd as a Sabbat bloodline, and that caused me to wonder if the writers even bothered to read their own material. While that bloodline was revealed for the first time in the Storyteller's Guide to the Sabbat, it clearly states the bloodline does not belong to any sect and is included only as a story element although the bloodline does have more contact with the Sabbat than it does with other groups. Not to mention the creation of the Salubri anti-tribu and others in Revised. These additions made zero sense except the metaplot required it. Now they stick out weirdly because even that metaplot is thrown out.<br /> <br /> The solution for this for STs of course is just to purge everything they don't like. We shouldn't feel bound to canon anymore because none of the latter editions ever did so. Take what you want and leave the rest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-24T13:08:53-07:00","id":1410120,"title":"","content":"It makes sense that the Sabbat has every bloodline possible within it: Imagine a press gang with blood bonds.<br /> <br /> The Kiasyd shouldn't exist. That's their problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-25T19:57:30-07:00","id":1410439,"title":"","content":"<b>Blood Vagrants</b><br /> <br /> An Anarch by the name of Auntie Juniper talks about hunting and gaining admittance to Camarilla and Anarch territories when you are a nomadic vampire. Basically, lie your undead ass off. The advice she offers is solid enough, though I debate her dismissal of hotels. For one thing, you can hang that like \u201cDo not clean\u201d sign on your door. For another, you can hide under the bed.<br /> <br /> In any case, this section has a punchy style, and offers generally solid guidance.<br /> <br /> It does occur to me that a vampire could probably make a killing by owning a hotel, or motel, and providing some \u201cspecial\u201d services to itinerant vampires who are just passing through.<br /> <br /> <b>Blood of the Redeemer</b><br /> <br /> I used to live in Alabama, and this passage is set in Alabama, which amuses me. Here a preacher smoothly, and with a large amount of chutzpah, inverts the actual and clear moral of a Biblical passage into something that endorses vampires and vampiric behavior.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve not known any actual vampire preachers, but I\u2019ve known bloody minded preachers and others who distort Biblical teaching smoother than an experienced gambler can perform a card trick.<br /> <br /> With the collapse of the traditional Sabbat, the Camarilla has moved from being a strictly secular institution to one which does permit pursuit if faith, assuming some elder benefits from that pursuit. This section does address Anarch spirituality, such as it is, and acts as a counterpart to the Camarilla\u2019s efforts.<br /> <br /> That said, the only thing that keeps this Preacher in the Anarchs (as compared to the Camarilla) is likely his theatrically. Because nothing in his statements or message are political, or against anything the Camarilla does or says.<br /> <br /> The section also makes for an interesting Masquerade breach just asking for SI involvement.<br /> <br /> <b>The Parasite Way</b><br /> <br /> Here Agata \u201cthat sound made when to run your finger horizontally across your lips quickly\u201d Sterek discusses vampire nature with a vampire named Rudi. This is probably the Rudi who wrote \u201cMonsters of the Recent Past.\u201d<br /> <br /> Anyway, Sterek compares vampires to tapeworms, blood diseases and fungal infections. Again, Sterek is written with the fictional insanity \u2013 which is to say writers who have done no research into insanity say she is crazy, and the depiction of it are all over the place. Even so, Sterek has the strongest and most recognizable voice of any of the characters in this book, and the clearest grasp of vampire nature. That she has no illusions about her nature, and vampire nature, might be way others take her to be insane.<br /> <br /> Also, she is a bit like the Joker in that she is not as crazy as she seems, or at least more rational than people assume. To wit, Sterek\u2019s fucking with Rudi via a death threat.<br /> <br /> The section is brief, and amusing but ends with an error in that the last lines are needlessly repeated.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-25T20:53:55-07:00","id":1410444,"title":"","content":"A few points:<br /> <br /> 1. Speaking as a neurodivergent person, vampires are all naturally insane because they suffer from spontaneous emotional freak outs as well as sanguinary animism. Most are also narcissicists to begin with. So, I've always felt that quite a lot of Malkavians aren't going to stand out nearly as much as people think. I do note that I also think rather than &quot;insane&quot; as typical mental illness, the majority of &quot;insane&quot; vampire are simply suffering from possessing extreme personality traits. This is almost an inevitability given the freedom from consequence and traumatizing experiences they regularly endure.<br /> <br /> Which is a long way of saying Agata isn't that weird for me and I like her.<br /> <br /> 2. The preacher and many other ancilla are people I think who would join the Anarchs because age is far less a barrier to power as well as &quot;mortal&quot; methods of gaining power are easier. One of my all time favorite Anarchs is 1st Edition Chicago by Night's <b>Gordon Keaton</b>. Gordon Keaton is exactly the opposite of your typical Anarch and is basically Patrick Bateman. He's a serial killing yuppie, WASP, snobbish, and rich. Why is he an Anarch?<br /> <br /> Well, he's a Caitiff and not a Ventrue. Also, because he can gain real power among the Anarchs that he could never gain among the Camarilla. Authority though money, charisma, and populism over Disciplines or ancient webs of pawns.<br /> <br /> 3. I recommend locking the door twice and using the chain because some hotel staff don't observe that or it falls off. I also recommend using the closet or the bathroom bathtub because Kindred don't care about comfort while they're, well, dead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-25T21:51:50-07:00","id":1410448,"title":"","content":"Off topic, but you're not alone on the Malkavians. I was diagnosed with Bipolar Disorder years ago, and shudder at the idea of someone pretending to have it as a game mechanic.<br /> <br /> V:tR's Clan Mekhet is a much more interesting take on the Auspex + Obfuscate &quot;seer who hides in the shadows&quot; concept, but even that execution isn't a perfect fit for the clan of Cassandras that I want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-26T00:52:54-07:00","id":1410463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1410444#post1410444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A few points:<br /> <br /> 1. Speaking as a neurodivergent person, vampires are all naturally insane because they suffer from spontaneous emotional freak outs as well as sanguinary animism. .</div> </div> </div> </div>Uhh... they don't all suffer from sanguinary animalism, that's a rare kindred condition, and the beast is an illness of the body rather than the mind; Unless malkavian, a vampire is no less neurotypical post -mbrace than they were before. Their violent unlives might bring about trauma, but that isn't any more (It's probably less) than a mortal's response to trauma.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-26T07:05:47-07:00","id":1410508,"title":"","content":"My comments about insanity are more meta in nature; insanity means whatever an often lazy writer wants it to mean. That is somewhat irritating, but also standard in media depictions of mental illness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1208,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","user":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","date":". 08-26-2020, 10:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-26T09:16:11-07:00","id":1410524,"title":"","content":"Agata didn't strike me as insane, so much as blissfully detached and murderously hedonistic. She seems functional enough for her own purposes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1410448#post1410448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Off topic, but you're not alone on the Malkavians. I was diagnosed with Bipolar Disorder years ago, and shudder at the idea of someone pretending to have it as a game mechanic.<br /> <br /> V:tR's Clan Mekhet is a much more interesting take on the Auspex + Obfuscate &quot;seer who hides in the shadows&quot; concept, but even that execution isn't a perfect fit for the clan of Cassandras that I want.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find it tempting to think of Malkavian characters by making a Mekhet character, then (so far as V5 is concerned) simply considering what sort of &quot;episodes&quot; they experience when the mechanical clan flaw comes into play.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-03T19:38:35-07:00","id":1411735,"title":"","content":"<b>Dawn of Stan Millennium</b><br /> <br /> Here Karoliina Koski is interviewed by Chinasa Adeyemi. <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MPKODzv1PD4\" target=\"_blank\">Koski\u2019s name reminds me of Klausi Kinski, the late actor noted for his mellow temperament.</a><br /> <br /> Koski is a vampire and a perennial groupie for Finnish black metal groups. Adeyemi informs us that the ratio of black metal to the general population is highest in the world. I\u2019m not certain what to make of that fact.<br /> <br /> This section of the book made me think of \u2018Lords of Chaos,\u2019 the 2019 mostly non-fiction movie about a Finnish black metal band that tried to overcome its own mediocrity by burning down churches, among other things. I will admit to knowing little about black metal or about the Finnish take on the artistic mode, but I can easily understand (through a reasonable understanding of human behavior) how some hacks might commit crimes in an effort to boost their brand, rather than doing something like practicing. Black metal, in form and substance, is a mode that rejects most convictable standards in terms of society, music and so on \u2013 but the performers with even a spoonful of skill and talent can make it work without committing arson, murder, and jaywalking (and possibly cannibalism).<br /> <br /> The point being, if Koski were a performer she like would be one lucky to get a spot opening for no-name bands operating in the boonies. She is also one who would lean on the entire arson, murder, and cannibalism heavily. However, rather than being a performer, Koski is (to the credit of the human writer of this section) a walking-talking personification of the bad fan. The black metal scene is one of violent performances, so one groupie biting another during a concert would raise little suspicion. Or at least less suspicion than it would at a Celene Dion event.<br /> <br /> If you can get past the relative obnoxiousness of Koski, the entire scene black metal scene is pure rebellion at its loudest and most theatrical. It rejects not simply the rule of ancients, but anything which would prohibit violence, spraying strangers with pig\u2019s blood, glorifying suicide, corpse desecration, and so on. So it tacitly asks, how deep does your rebellion go? Where is the line between nihilistic music as rebellion and an expression of mental illness?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-03T20:46:45-07:00","id":1411743,"title":"","content":"This reminds me a good deal of Svein Forinbras.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Svein_Fortinbras\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Svein_Fortinbras</a><br /> <br /> He's a Satanist Follower of Set metal musician who gained notoriety for burning down churches but lucked out into destroying the hold of a Society of Leopold cell that made him a hero to the local Prince.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-03T23:11:02-07:00","id":1411747,"title":"","content":"Auntie Juniper is from The Anarch Cookbook, way back when.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://imgur.com/IDwGLEJ\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://imgur.com/IDwGLEJ\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://imgur.com/IDwGLEJ\" target=\"_blank\"> https://imgur.com/IDwGLEJ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://imgur.com/2XixImT\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://imgur.com/2XixImT\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://imgur.com/2XixImT\" target=\"_blank\"> https://imgur.com/2XixImT </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I liked her concept and have thought about using her in my current game, though PCs have yet to run into her. Was neat to see her turn up again here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T09:22:46-07:00","id":1411813,"title":"","content":"A bunch of teens: Yahoo! We\u2019re all going mountain climbing this weekend!<br /> <br /> Grizzled Old Man: Don\u2019t do it. There is a beast, a monster, a walking death on the mountain, a blood hungry curse.<br /> <br /> Teens: \u2026<br /> <br /> Old Man: He\u2019ll be the death of each and everyone one of you!<br /> <br /> Teens: \u2026<br /> <br /> Old Man: And he\u2019s sporting the latest in <a href=\"https://www.rei.com/h/climbing\" target=\"_blank\">mountain gear from REI </a>and is a frequent contributor to <i>Mountain Climbing</i> <i>Monthly</i>!<br /> <br /> Survivor Girl: Guys, we don\u2019t we just go to Santa Clara and go swimming, like I suggested in the first place?<br /> <br /> <b>Death at the Roof of the World</b><br /> <br /> In this section roving vampire reporter Chinasa Adeyemi interviews Antoni<br /> Morawski, a gangrel who maintains a predilection for mountain climbing he possessed while alive.<br /> <br /> There are thematic notes connecting sections of the <i>Anarch</i> book, which are tonally stronger than the structural connections in the <i>Camarilla</i> book. This section, much like the last one, profiles a vampire who is the personification of the bad fan (they use their nominal fandom to murder and eat other people in subculture), who follows their interest around but who does not actually perform.<br /> <br /> And to reiterate something that is a reoccurring theme, if not outright stated; vampires are only ever bad people. Morawski murders a fellow mountain climber, whom he knew personally. Morawski says the other climber was dead when he found him, but the statement feels like a lie.<br /> <br /> The observation I have about both sections is that they do provide plot hooks, but more for a group running mortals or hunters in the WoD than for vampires. Both Morawski and Koski are apparently solitary vampires (no evident pack or coterie) running around in a human subculture, murdering and eating members of that subculture. Discovering the murders are occurring, that the murderer is a vampire, and then discovering that vampire is a respected and trusted fan\u2026 that would be an engaging horror story. For mortals. It might have less traction for a group of vampires. In fact, there is arguably little reason for a PC group to encounter either of them, let alone tangle with them over something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1208,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","user":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","date":". 09-04-2020, 12:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T13:40:21-07:00","id":1411872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1411813#post1411813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The observation I have about both sections is that they do provide plot hooks, but more for a group running mortals or hunters in the WoD than for vampires. Both Morawski and Koski are apparently solitary vampires (no evident pack or coterie) running around in a human subculture, murdering and eating members of that subculture. Discovering the murders are occurring, that the murderer is a vampire, and then discovering that vampire is a respected and trusted fan\u2026 that would be an engaging horror story. For mortals. It might have less traction for a group of vampires. In fact, there is arguably little reason for a PC group to encounter either of them, let alone tangle with them over something.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is something I routinely struggle with as an ST. I have a great idea that checks all the boxes I want in the World of Darkness. Yet when I think about it, it turns out it is not gameable in the sense that there are things a group of PCs (of whatever game) can do about it. So I have to rethink it. Sometimes it becomes an idea reserved for another game. Other times I can rethink it and come up with something that is gameable (but which may be totally different from the first idea, though clearly inspired by it). But sometimes I just have to neglect it - either use it as simple flavor text and not a plot, or abandon it entirely.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T13:48:55-07:00","id":1411875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1410439#post1410439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It does occur to me that a vampire could probably make a killing by owning a hotel, or motel, and providing some \u201cspecial\u201d services to itinerant vampires who are just passing through.</div> </div> </div> </div>When I ST, one element that is found in almost all my Vampire chronicles is that there is one or more &quot;hotels&quot; (that cater to various kinds of clients so one can find a spot where they don't stick out) where new vampires to a city can go prior to any meeting with the Prince according to Hospitality. At the very least, they're a place to leave messages for the Prince even if the vampire has made alternate lodging. And those hotels are popularly known in the greater vampire sub-culture so that it's quite easy for vampires to know where they need to go when they first move to a new city. Obviously the larger the city, the more options they are. They might be hotels, slum tenements, short term apartments, or other concepts - but all cater as being a place one can crash and leave a message that will get to the Prince.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T19:26:14-07:00","id":1411981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1407421#post1407421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that is a grievous error because many Anarchs are very openly about their hatred and disdain for Kine. Remember the first Anarchs were the basis for the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> SOME Anarchs are very much about caring for kine.<br /> <br /> OTHER Anarchs are disgusted by how much the Camarilla restricts their ability to abuse them (little as that may be).</div> </div> </div> </div>The last one has no connections to any historical event.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T00:34:07-07:00","id":1412016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1411981#post1411981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The last one has no connections to any historical event.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maldavis' revolt.<br /> <br /> Also, it's stated in ANARCHS UNBOUND.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T08:06:31-07:00","id":1412088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1411813#post1411813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And to reiterate something that is a reoccurring theme, if not outright stated; vampires are only ever bad people. Morawski murders a fellow mountain climber, whom he knew personally. Morawski says the other climber was dead when he found him, but the statement feels like a lie.</div> </div> </div> </div>Funnily, I thought Morawski was one of the &quot;better&quot; vampires in the book. Because hey, at least he tried to save someone's life. Climbing up to rescue the stranded mountaineer was bad for the Masquerade and he knows it was. Doesn't feel like something he'd have done for just one meal.<br /> <br /> But, yeah. This entire &quot;vampires are always always horrible people, no exceptions&quot; take isn't one I find compelling, or consistent with the game's earlier history. There is no sense of struggle against the Beast or tragedy in the loss, because everyone has already lost and is making wisecracks about it. Or the writers are. Morawski endangering the Masquerade to save his friend only to find the guy was already dead feels like a &quot;ha ha, you shouldn't even try&quot; punchline to a take on the game the writers have interpreted as a joke. <br /> <br /> I remember in <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a>' Let's Read of 1e Chicago how one poster said &quot;a lot of the vampires feel like ordinary people who just happen to have a blood-based diet.&quot; Characters like Son, Jacob Schumpter, and Gordon Keaton served to illustrate the blackest depths of Kindred monstrosity, but there was a pretty big spectrum.<br /> <br /> Here it feels like everyone has been shoved squarely into Son territory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T08:32:14-07:00","id":1412091,"title":"","content":"My take on Morawski is maybe he meant to save the life of the other mountain climber, but he is a monster and fed on the man despite his own supposed goals.<br /> <br /> Also, not all vampires are as bad as Son, but they are not good people. It runs in shades from grey to jet black, morally and ethically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T08:44:37-07:00","id":1412096,"title":"","content":"I can't think of a single gray character from the book though. We have cleavers who feed on and feed blood to their children, &quot;diablerie feels good&quot; Agata, Juniper casually killing homeowners for temporary havens, the &quot;tee hee we sometimes kill our doms&quot; puppy play enthusiasts, a timid-feeling vamp casually mentioning how he murdered his ghoul's family... you get gray from an intermix of white and black, and here there's just black.<br /> <br /> If there's a distinction from Son, it's that many of these Anarchs commit atrocities for convenience rather than inherent pleasure, but I'm not sure how much that actually changes their body count.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T11:55:25-07:00","id":1412127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>False Epiphany</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1412096#post1412096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't think of a single gray character from the book though. We have cleavers who feed on and feed blood to their children, &quot;diablerie feels good&quot; Agata, Juniper casually killing homeowners for temporary havens, the &quot;tee hee we sometimes kill our doms&quot; puppy play enthusiasts, a timid-feeling vamp casually mentioning how he murdered his ghoul's family... you get gray from an intermix of white and black, and here there's just black.<br /> <br /> If there's a distinction from Son, it's that many of these Anarchs commit atrocities for convenience rather than inherent pleasure, but I'm not sure how much that actually changes their body count.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, I think most vampires in &quot;dark&quot; Vampire: The Masquerade settings have killed someone innocent in their lives. The Beast is terrible. I generally go with the idea that most go out of their way to avoid it, though, due to pragmatism and then what passes for morality. It's just that being a vampire is pretty awful and most people have an Angel or Nick Knight &quot;horrible backstory&quot; where they lost control sometime.<br /> <br /> These Anarchs are pretty awful but the &quot;murder suburbanites to get a haven&quot; is actually a thing that Anarchs (when they weren't so different from Sabbat) were described as doing. Dickie, a friend of Humanity 10 Maldavis, used this method.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Dickie\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Dickie</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T12:25:22-07:00","id":1412135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1412127#post1412127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, I think most vampires in &quot;dark&quot; Vampire: The Masquerade settings have killed someone innocent in their lives. The Beast is terrible. I generally go with the idea that most go out of their way to avoid it, though, due to pragmatism and then what passes for morality. It's just that being a vampire is pretty awful and most people have an Angel or Nick Knight &quot;horrible backstory&quot; where they lost control sometime.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the Circle of the Crone sourcebook for Vampire: The Requiem, they had a special position for younger Kindred who'd never killed: &quot;virgins&quot; for female ones and &quot;fools&quot; for male ones (there were mythological connotations vice &quot;fool&quot; being meant in a belittling sense). They were seen as providing a valuable perspective on humanity to their more jaded elders. <br /> <br /> I've taken that concept and made it a little broader in my games. A &quot;virgin&quot; is a vampire who's never killed someone. They're uncommon enough that vampires can brag about being one, if they're inclined to. <br /> <br /> Or lie about it. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1412127#post1412127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These Anarchs are pretty awful but the &quot;murder suburbanites to get a haven&quot; is actually a thing that Anarchs (when they weren't so different from Sabbat) were described as doing. Dickie, a friend of Humanity 10 Maldavis, used this method.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Dickie\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Dickie</a></div> </div> </div> </div>I remember that. Maldavis' best pal Uriah also liked to feed on children. I think he was Humanity 4.<br /> <br /> Maldavis kind of had terrible friends.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T12:56:25-07:00","id":1412146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1412016#post1412016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maldavis' revolt.<br /> <br /> Also, it's stated in ANARCHS UNBOUND.</div> </div> </div> </div>What\u2019s the Maldavis' revolt.?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T14:27:50-07:00","id":1412165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1412146#post1412146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What\u2019s the Maldavis' revolt.?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a weird huge part of Anarch History that almost no books ever reference despite its importance. Basically, in the 1980s, Maldavis led a massive Anarch revolt that came within inches of establishing a Second Anarch Free State in Chicago. Maldavis was heavily involved in fighting corruption, police brutality, and controlled the Mayor of the time that was seeking reform for the city.<br /> <br /> In the end, Maldavis' revolt was crushed and she was forced to go into hiding.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T15:50:17-07:00","id":1412176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>False Epiphany</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1412088#post1412088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remember in <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a>' Let's Read of 1e Chicago how one poster said &quot;a lot of the vampires feel like ordinary people who just happen to have a blood-based diet.&quot; Characters like Son, Jacob Schumpter, and Gordon Keaton served to illustrate the blackest depths of Kindred monstrosity, but there was a pretty big spectrum.<br /> <br /> Here it feels like everyone has been shoved squarely into Son territory.</div> </div> </div> </div>The game originally was supposed to be about personal horror - an ordinary person struggling with their new vampiric condition. As such, there were plenty of examples of that kind of character in Chicago By Night, and to a lesser extent other early edition material. However, these kinds of vampires were increasingly removed from play for various reasons.<br /> <br /> First, there was a confusion by some players that personal horror meant whining, pseudo-angst, and life avoidance, and that created a backlash against those kind of characters since they irritated a lot of people.<br /> <br /> Second, the game seemed to go overboard on vampires that didn't actually deal with the condition of being a vampire. They seemed more like characters in a Chris Claremont X-Men story, so again there was a backlash against that. The combined backlash of these first two elements meant the game began emphasizing truly horrific characters and any kind of vampire who struggled against her condition was dropped or shown to be a fraud.<br /> <br /> Third, as the setting became more developed, the game switched from being one based on personal experience and exploring the setting, to an increasingly militarized confrontation between Camarilla and Sabbat (or other factions). And there really isn't any room for vampires fighting against their condition in that metaplot scenario. Who cares about the personal struggles of Hannibal King, Nick Knight, or Louis when the Sabbat is burning down your haven and you have to lead the task force against their laboratory spewing out Vozhd.<br /> <br /> I think the prevalence of Humanity 10 vampires and those who've achieved Golconda went too far in first and early second edition, but the counter-reaction went too far as well. I think high humanity vampires, though rare and mostly limited to inexperienced neonates with some notable exceptions, do have a place in the game. The game just needs to acknowledge the difficult path ahead of them and present them dealing with the appropriate challenges of that lifestyle.<br /> <br /> I've never seen the Anarchs as a morally superior force to the Camarilla, but certainly there is a role for high humanity vampires in some of their ranks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-06T07:58:07-07:00","id":1412286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1407516#post1407516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes it can.<br /> <br /> If you're a black Brujah living in the Antebellum South and have the sole goal of killing the white plantation class as well as their Toreador and Ventrue masters then you are not a hypocrite if you claim to be fighting for freedom. Said Brujah may have absolutely no sympathy for the former slave-owning class and offer them no protection against Kindred that want to prey upon them and may only extend protections to ex-slaves even if he's Prince of Atlanta.<br /> <br /> Similarly, a Brujah who in occupied Poland.<br /> <br /> Or a Lakota Caitiff who insists that you only feed on white people outside of his Reservation.<br /> <br /> The heart of the Anarchs is they are angry at the system They have very good ideas of who exactly is a victim and who exactly is a victimizer. Very rarely are they fighting for a utopian Star Trek society where everyone is equal because they are usually Embraced from or keenly aware of the oppressed.<br /> <br /> It also runs into the fact that the ONLY group that will have ANY vampire who wants to protect Kine is in the Anarchs. It's just not all of them or a doctrine of their organization as a whole. They're the vegans of the vampire world.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Yes, which is why they will always be worse and the worst Anarchs are better than the best Camarilla.<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;What about the Sabbat?&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> Shut up!<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019ll disagree with the last one some Anarchs can be very nasty","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-06T14:12:21-07:00","id":1412331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1412176#post1412176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Third, as the setting became more developed, the game switched from being one based on personal experience and exploring the setting, to an increasingly militarized confrontation between Camarilla and Sabbat (or other factions). And there really isn't any room for vampires fighting against their condition in that metaplot scenario. Who cares about the personal struggles of Hannibal King, Nick Knight, or Louis when the Sabbat is burning down your haven and you have to lead the task force against their laboratory spewing out Vozhd.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this was biggest thing. <br /> <br /> In my experience, the more external politics you insert into a chronicle, the less time there is to focus on the personal struggles of being a vampire. That isn't to say one is better than other (I usually prefer a mix of both). Like action, mystery, or romance, they're simply different subgenres the game can encompass. A given chronicle is likely to focus more on some subgenres than others, as is the gameline as a whole under different creative leads. This can also, unfortunately, alienate some gamers when they feel like developers are pushing their preferred themes and subgenres as the &quot;one true way to play&quot;--see Revised's focus on inter-sect warfare and V5's on elder-less street-level play. <br /> <br /> As a sourcebook, Anarchs is most useful when it has content that GMs running different styles of games can mine. I think it does a pretty good job there. There is a balance of metaplot-central characters like Tyler or Theo Bell with with loners who are off being vampires without much concern for larger Kindred society.<br /> <br /> But they are pretty much all equally Gordon Keaton-level monsters.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1412176#post1412176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the prevalence of Humanity 10 vampires and those who've achieved Golconda went too far in first and early second edition, but the counter-reaction went too far as well. I think high humanity vampires, though rare and mostly limited to inexperienced neonates with some notable exceptions, do have a place in the game. The game just needs to acknowledge the difficult path ahead of them and present them dealing with the appropriate challenges of that lifestyle.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think 1e Chicago misplaced some of its ratings. Maldavis seemed pretty decent for a vampire, but I dunno that she warranted Humanity 10. She had really high traits in general that I recall V5 Chicago toning down. <br /> <br /> Menele wasn't Humanity 10 by any stretch, even if he wanted to achieve Golconda. His Jyhad with Helena was killing too many people and a canker upon his soul. <br /> <br /> Rebekah I like more in her Revised/BJD take where she claims to have fallen out of Golconda, and that it's &quot;like getting clean--sometimes you relapse.&quot; It's anyone's guess whether she's telling the truth. <br /> <br /> I agree there were too many Golcondites in Chicago when you also include Johann. A given city probably does not need more than one, if any at all. At the same time, I'd also agree Revised went a little too far. The only new Golcondite I can recall from any sourcebook then is Cairo's Malkavian riddler. If no one ever obtains Golconda, there's only so much mileage that chronicles can get from the concept.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-06T21:09:27-07:00","id":1412384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>False Epiphany</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1412331#post1412331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think 1e Chicago misplaced some of its ratings. Maldavis seemed pretty decent for a vampire, but I dunno that she warranted Humanity 10. She had really high traits in general that I recall V5 Chicago toning down.<br /> <br /> Menele wasn't Humanity 10 by any stretch, even if he wanted to achieve Golconda. His Jyhad with Helena was killing too many people and a canker upon his soul.<br /> <br /> Rebekah I like more in her Revised/BJD take where she claims to have fallen out of Golconda, and that it's &quot;like getting clean--sometimes you relapse.&quot; It's anyone's guess whether she's telling the truth.<br /> <br /> I agree there were too many Golcondites in Chicago when you also include Johann. A given city probably does not need more than one, if any at all. At the same time, I'd also agree Revised went a little too far. The only new Golcondite I can recall from any sourcebook then is Cairo's Malkavian riddler. If no one ever obtains Golconda, there's only so much mileage that chronicles can get from the concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>The character stats in CbN were just whacked. Not only was Humanity all over the place and not supported by the character description (I remember an early thread by CT Phipps on more realistic humanity ratings for all the characters), but Disciplines and traits often didn't make sense for the characters either. It's just an early artifact of the game. I don't think these were mistakes - they were bad design choices.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":". 09-07-2020, 04:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-07T11:35:32-07:00","id":1412457,"title":"","content":"<b>Beast on a Leash</b><br /> <br /> Never spank a vampire.<br /> <br /> Chinasa Adeyemi interviews petplay enthusiasts Janet and William Stoughton In this third of a series on vampires in sub cultures. As with the two previous entires it reminds us vampires are horrible people, the worst kind of fan, and ruin everything they touch.<br /> <br /> Specifically petplay is a kind of sexual play, a variation on a theme when compared to BDSM. The Stoughton\u2019s are involved with mortals in this, but despite their own supposed best intentions they remain vampires and so are evil and horribly dangerous to everyone around them. The Stoughtons cannot help but violate some basic tenants of sexual play of any kind, in that they are lying to and not acting on good faith with the human participants.<br /> <br /> The humans involved do not know they are dealing with vampires when they start discipline, bondage, punishment and similar activities with the Stoughtons. This gets humans killed. The vampires treat this as both a minor inconvenience and little more than a social faux pas.<br /> <br /> More so than the last two section this one is a pitch dark comedy, almost to the point of kink shaming. That nice suburban couple with the lovely house and well-kept yard are (1) into some pretty kinky stuff, (2) vampires, (3) and sometimes murder their doms because of poor planning and bad communication. Honestly, the section feels like it is (to use the British slang) taking the Mickey out of too tame BDSM stories and fantasies involving vampires \u2013 here it is asserted that will get you killed.<br /> <br /> This section, like the last two, offers plot possibilities but mostly for a group of mortals dealing with the damage vampire create. There are few reason for other vampires to get involved, except possibly to cover up a Masquerade breach created by the Stoughtons. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-07T19:21:44-07:00","id":1412516,"title":"","content":"<b>Vegas Nights</b><br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dV1HSscPYSY\" data-code=\"dV1HSscPYSY\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/dV1HSscPYSY/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> So this entry is about some Rando who goes to Vegas for an interesting weekend and gets exactly that as part of an encounter at a vampire owned and run club (and possibly casino \u2013 it\u2019s a little unclear).<br /> <br /> Specifically, Rando runs into the Voerman sisters, Jeanette and Therese. The Voerman sister appeared in the original <i>Bloodlines</i> game. The catch is there is (depending on your point of view) there is only one Voerman, and she suffers from multiple personalities. One personality is the straight-laced Therese, the other being the more daring and gregarious Jeanette.<br /> <br /> While not expressly stated, it is almost certain Jeanette uses some disciplines to lure in and subdue Rando, as he states within hours of meeting her he is asking her to marry him. She agrees \u2013 and they actually have a Vegas wedding \u2013 and then she embraces him. Later Therese is utterly exasperated by all of this and gives Rando a job as a means of finding something to do with the man. Rando talks about getting a promotion, no longer having to work as a barman, and how to use dating apps to lure in prey.<br /> <br /> The Voerman sisters have apparently moved from LA to Vegas, and opened a club, again named The Asylum, like the club they had in <i>Bloodlines</i>. What prompted the move is never stated, and probably not even very important. I find it amusing that Rando and Jeanette apparently got married when he was in an altered mental state, which is one of those stories about things that happen in that town. What happens in Vegas, stays in Vegas.<br /> <br /> This section is interesting, and even amusing. The Asylum acts like a hotspot for Anarchs in Vegas, and probably an important one for across the US. Vegas has more or less landed in the hands of the Anarchs after the Second Inquisition moved through, destroying the Camarilla. That is an interesting tidbit of information. Also, the entire section reads like the background of PC who used merits to purchase an interesting sire. That is not a bad thing, just an observation. And the section provides more plot hooks than the last few.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-07T19:34:20-07:00","id":1412518,"title":"","content":"I feel like if there was a<span style=\"color:#232323\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">ny section to have some non-unilaterally horrible people, it's with the BDSM enthusiasts. I suppose it's more mainstream now than in 1991 though, and it is hard to see how the Stoughtons could ever practice their kink safely.<br /> <br /> The dom who ignored their safeword was a jerk. At least the mortals are bad people too.<br /> <br /> I liked getting to read about Jeanette/Therese, and how much V5 pays homage to Bloodlines in general.<br /> <br /> I also liked the Voermans fi</span></span><span style=\"color:#232323\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">ne</span></span><span style=\"color:#232323\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"> in L.A., but Vegas feels a lot more like Jeanette's kind of town than Santa Monica. </span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":3110,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","user":"False Epiphany","date":". 09-07-2020, 10:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-08T03:22:38-07:00","id":1412555,"title":"","content":"<b>BDSM, Mountain Climbing, Metal, and Redundancy</b><br /> <br /> Honestly, I think the BDSM part of the book is the absolute worst part of the book and it's not because it's offensive but it's the fact that its very redundant as well as a bit of a non-sequitor. We've already had three parts of the book related to Anarchs preying on the hobbyists of topics related to their preferred topic in life. We had the heavy metal girl and the mountain climber so now we're getting a BDSM couple that murders people. It's a little weird too because there's nothing related to being an &quot;Anarch&quot; that really says, &quot;My hobbies define me.&quot; This strikes me as something that relates to the fact that they did this entire book without any OOC information. As such, they seem like they wandered a bit off-topic and just went for, &quot;Tell a horrifying story about a vampire.&quot;<br /> <br /> I feel like they could have thrown in some stories about Camarilla oppression, religious cults, or something else that would have given a better perspective on the Anarch Movement. One thing I feel like this book lacks is the world-weary &quot;survivor&quot; story that I feel like Anarchs would have. You know something like, &quot;My name is Carol. I was Embraced by a Toreador who liked my dancing and then abandoned me after he found out that I just did it for the money. Then my family was murdered by the Prince after I stayed at a friend's house and he couldn't find me. He murdered her too. I didn't ask to be a vampire but it didn't matter because of their stupid laws. The Anarchs may not be that much better but I'll someday kill Tara, the Judas Prince.&quot;<br /> <br /> Honestly, the book doesn't seem to have much focus on the Anarchs' WHYS hating the Camarilla or why at all. I find that very weird.<br /> <br /> <b>Humanity</b><br /> <br /> I understand why they chose to go the route they did with the fact virtually every Anarch in the book is a scumbag. Revised was the first of the Editions that really embraced that vampires are BAD and that had its benefits to the line. Justin Achilli, the new Justicar of our line, loved making it clear both the Camarilla and Sabbat were equally bad. The Anarchs lacking edge and being the &quot;Sabbat but whinier&quot; was a fan perception that was propagated by the fact that they didn't seem ruthless enough to seize cities or Mass Embrace or otherwise &quot;whatever it took&quot; to take down Camarilla cities.<br /> <br /> I feel they're overcompensating here to make the Anarchs edgey and have gone a bit far in making them discount Sabbat, ironically what they weren't before.<br /> <br /> <b>The Voerman Sisters</b><br /> <br /> I think the use of Bloodlines was a really smart move by V5's developers and Jason Carl in particular. The LA By Night web show on Geek and Sundry/White Wolf's Twitch channel took place in the video game version of LA versus the Anarch Free States established by Los Angeles by Night. I know they're the same setting but they had a lot of changes between the two with the show leaning much heavier on the video game.<br /> <br /> Having the Voermans move to Las Vegas is interesting and probably fits LA by Night where Vannevar Thomas declared a Blood Hunt on her last season. It also<br /> is a place that fits both of them as Jeanette is the perfect party girl and Therese is the excellent cold-blooded business woman behind such. I should note that Las Vegas was also a Giovanni city. Like Boston, it was a city that wasn't supposed to be under control of the Giovanni due to the Treaty that keeps them out of the Jyhad. However, it was under <i>de facto</i> control of the Giovanni. Here, it seems that they were overthrown and it left a power vacuum that the Anarchs moved in.<br /> <br /> The thing is that Therese/Jeanette are 6th generation vampires so they could actually be BARON of Las Vegas rather than just a immigrant to the city. It also means that the poor schmuck that was Embraced on a whim, blood bound, and then put behind the bar is a 7th generation vampire. I also like that she's just recruiting a bunch of employees for her club. I also think club instead of casino because there's more than just the Strip.<br /> <br /> A reminder that the Asylum is also a Loresheet now. It's a franchise that Therese runs from Vegas with vampire employees. Same for the Succubus Club.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 09-08-2020, 07:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-08T05:23:56-07:00","id":1412571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1412555#post1412555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly, the book doesn't seem to have much focus on the Anarchs' WHYS hating the Camarilla or why at all. I find that very weird.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>You need to understand most 'anarchs' become so simply because they don't like a prince or primogen or something or other and aren't capable of independently changing who the prince and primogen are, hence they group together with 'like-minded' people to make changes. Most Anarchs aren't firebrands. There certainly are firebrands, they're what people think of when the term 'anarchs' come to mind in camarilla circles, they're certainly the most vocal and visible of the anarchs. But to use VTMB: most Anarchs are Hollywood anarchs, not downtown Anarchs. The ones who get upset over the 'tyranny' of the camarilla are usually the ones who want to cleave or on the other end of the spectrum the ones who want to play Viovode; or the ones who can't seperate the prince who's really oppressing them from the organization he represents (IE, idiots).<br /> <br /> Most level headed anarchs (the quiet ones who last long) realise they're using the movement to further their own ends and the end result isn't much different from what the Camarilla looks like. And of course you get a few who like warfare and stiring shit up for fun...<br /> <br /> <b>Ultimately, telling players why anarchs hate the Camarilla is going to come off as preachy. It'd be far better to allow players to come to their own conclusions</b>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-08T05:35:48-07:00","id":1412576,"title":"","content":"Is killling one dom each that much worse than what most neonates have done?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","user":"Spencer from The Hills","date":".  Reread Vegas chapter 09-08-2020, 08:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-08T05:56:41-07:00","id":1412582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1412576#post1412576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is killling one dom each that much worse than what most neonates have done?</div> </div> </div> </div>It depends on how you answer the question, <b>&quot;How many people does your average vampire kill?&quot;</b><br /> <br /> Which varies from chronicle to chronicle and ST to ST.<br /> <br /> My take on the subject is that every vampire has probably killed one or two person they didn't mean to kill during their unlives, even as Neonates. However, my take on the subject is very few vampires are FLIPPANT about this (which is a small change but presentation is all). Most vampires in my games go out of their way not to kill people and their failures are things that haunt them. Anarchs and Sabbat both have people who gleefully indulge in murder as do Elders. However, those vampires who don't care are rapidly lost to wassail. An Anarch who casually kills people in his preferred feeding type is going to be someone that other Anarchs avoid or think of as sick.<br /> <br /> I don't think that these Anarchs are very Son-like but seem much more like Gordon Keaton. Which is to say he doesn't care about killing vampires but lacks the sadism. &quot;Oh, well, drank too much. Shame. Now I have to dispose of the body. That's going to be a pain in the ass.&quot; Even so, that kind of vampire is going to be on the margins of Anarch society or part of a very nasty gang.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-08T08:34:52-07:00","id":1412604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1412555#post1412555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, the book doesn't seem to have much focus on the Anarchs' WHYS hating the Camarilla or why at all. I find that very weird.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find it... interesting. And a bit liberating. An Anarch games does not have to be all about fighting the Camarilla after all. There are a great many vampires who simply do not care about the conflict between sects and the jyhad, even if the Camarilla calls them all Anarchs.<br /> <br /> That said, I do think three accounts of vampire NPCs who the PCs have no reason to tangle with is too many, and the point would have been made with one or two such entries.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1412555#post1412555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A reminder that the Asylum is also a Loresheet now. It's a franchise that Therese runs from Vegas with vampire employees. Same for the Succubus Club.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? Where does it appear?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-08T10:37:33-07:00","id":1412615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1412604#post1412604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really? Where does it appear?</div> </div> </div> </div>Page 394 of the main book.<br /> <br /> Jeanette/Therse's Loresheet says that you can operate one of her franchises at the 5th Dot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-08T14:00:44-07:00","id":1412639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1412604#post1412604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I find it... interesting. And a bit liberating. An Anarch games does not have to be all about fighting the Camarilla after all. There are a great many vampires who simply do not care about the conflict between sects and the jyhad, even if the Camarilla calls them all Anarchs.<br /> <br /> That said, I do think three accounts of vampire NPCs who the PCs have no reason to tangle with is too many, and the point would have been made with one or two such entries.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Really? Where does it appear?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah but by not talking about it. It makes it look like the Anarchs hate the Camarilla for no reason, and they are just a bunch of whiney teenagers,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-08T16:17:53-07:00","id":1412651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1412639#post1412639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah but by not talking about it. It makes it look like the Anarchs hate the Camarilla for no reason, and they are just a bunch of whiney teenagers,</div> </div> </div> </div>Everyone is going to bring their own biases, inspirations, and ideas to the Anarchs. Since they're basically defined as a negative (originally not the Camarilla, and now not the Camarilla or Sabbat) they're a blank slate the ST will project on. So the devs may be trying not to step on people's toes by &quot;defining&quot; things. Still, I agree a lack of some local groups and their ideas would be a good thing as long as it is clear that such a list is neither definitive nor comprehensive.<br /> <br /> My own view is that the Anarchs can be divided into several groups.<br /> <br /> 1) Misfits, outcasts, and oddballs who aren't political at all, but rub the people in power the wrong way so they get labelled as Anarchs. On one hand, everyone knows they're quite harmless so they usually get left alone. On the other hand, they make convenient scapegoats when one is needed. Other Anarchs really don't consider them to &quot;anarchs&quot;, but they're not seen as enemies either. Rubes to be ignored or exploited. Probably less than 10% of the Anarch population.<br /> <br /> 2) Loners who got hassled and fought back. I'll call this the John Rambo scenario when an abusive sheriff needlessly hassles a guy who just wants to move through and all hell breaks lose. This is like the first group, but the powers that be judge the situation wrong and it backfires on them. Probably happens more in low populated domains with a stable Kindred population than bigger domains when the Prince and his cronies have better things to do. These guys may not consider themselves Anarchs and would probably be willing to live in a Camarilla city provided their reputation does not precede them, but sometimes it does and they're stuck with the label. Again less than 10% of the population.<br /> <br /> 3) Adolescent vampires who don't like to be told what to do and like abusing their power. This is the typical poseur vampire and made up a lot of the original Chicago By Night anarchs. These characters would likely &quot;grow out of it&quot; provided they live long enough. I suspect many Camarilla vampires know this, and this is why the sect had many anarch sympathizers - they know these people will eventually join the system. They will mostly bitch and complain a lot, but will keep their heads down and keep their crimes minimal. Not really anarchs, but they make up a large recruitment ground for the &quot;revolution&quot;. Probably around 15%.<br /> <br /> 4) Outright criminals. These people aren't revolutionaries, they're just criminals of vampire society. But because they're hardened and willing to deal in physical violence, they make up a lot of the muscle of the &quot;revolution&quot;. However, because they're criminals, while they are useful, they will always be a problem for the &quot;movement&quot;. Both in terms of the movement's reputation and what to do with them should they succeed in creating a new &quot;free state&quot;. Some of these people would be perfectly willing to sell out to the Camarilla in return for amnesty and position. Much of Juggler's crew from the original Chicago By Night fits here. Smiling Jack too. Probably another 15%.<br /> <br /> 5) Vampires with a just (or at least reasonable) complaint against the local Prince. This is more about complaints against the despotic actions of the local guy in charge than any reasoned alternative to the Camarilla system. But it's probably the bulk of the anarch population. These people may not be happy with the Camarilla, but could tolerate it if the local guy wasn't such a jackass. Their ideals don't go beyond &quot;we need to replace this guy with another.&quot; Some of these people could very well be recruited for the greater Anarch cause, but just as many would be willing to cooperate with the Camarilla afterwards. Again, many of the Camarilla's anarch sympathizers are due to knowing people in this category. Large number of Anarchs here. Maldavis is probably a good example here, although I know some will put her in a more idealistic group. I'll say 25%.<br /> <br /> 6) Recruited into the cause. These are vampires that exist solely to be cannon fodder for the revolution. As such, they'd normally be a combination of #3, #4 and #5, but the distinction being is that they were embraced to give the Anarch numbers and their ignorance is exploited by their sires (all for the right reasons, of course). A lot probably get killed quickly. Like the criminals, they're here to provide muscle - disposable muscle. Should they survive, they'll either be angry at being exploited or become dedicated Anarchs. Anita Wainwright is probably an example early on. Maybe 10% - mostly in domains being contested to some degree.<br /> <br /> 7) Actual dissidents from the Camarilla. These people aren't just upset that the local Prince is a jerk. They have major problems with the entire system of the Camarilla - the Inner Circle, Justicars, Archons, Conclaves, and Princes. Whether out of idealism, a desire to end tyranny of the elders, or megalomania, these vampires have given serious thought as to the system of governance which will replace the Camarilla. The big probably is that there are various factions with their own system of government. So they're like the Spanish Republicans of the Spanish Civil War - constitutional democrats, socialists, anarchists, and communist all fighting against a common enemy, but hating much of their own side, and some factions are actively killing their own side as well. Without them, there really is not an Anarch movement, but they're also the reason the Anarchs will never win or unite. Hind's Socialists in CbN (including Blackjack), and Jeremy MacNeil's group are the examples here. This is also where the game has quite frankly disappointed the fans. We really don't get an idea of what the future is that they're fighting for. We never learn how exactly Hinds and Blackjack intend to apply socialist principles to a vampire domain. We do learn about Jeremy MacNeil's strange libertarian ideas, but LA By Night never presents us with other visions. This is probably the block that needs the most development in the game. Current Anita Wainwright is probably here. Probably another 25%, but they make up a disproportionate number of Anarch leaders and most of its philosophers.<br /> <br /> 8) Collaborators and Movement Exploiters. These are people not really sympathetic to the Anarchs, but jump to them either because they're on the winning side (I would say David Geduld in LABN) or because they're the best option to gain power (Gordon Keaton in CbN). They hitch their ride because its an opportunity to gain power. The game has plenty of other examples. Relatively small number, but because these are people seeking power, they have a tendency to become vital to the movement as movers and shakers especially in the middle tiers before they get big enough to run their own crew. Of course, most of them would not hesitate to defect to the Camarilla is they can. Probably less than 10% of the Anarch population.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-08T19:48:00-07:00","id":1412665,"title":"","content":"<b>Night Circus </b><br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Up7KHbJTmoo\" data-code=\"Up7KHbJTmoo\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/Up7KHbJTmoo/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> This is one of my favorite sections in the book \u2013 the <i>Night Circus</i>. A circus with vampires getting away with shit because they are vampires. It\u2019s a fun read with a lot of story possibilities.<br /> <br /> The Anarchs of the Night Circus use disciplines to draw crowds \u2013 which provide them with money and feeding victims. This is done under the guise of a grab bag of circus shows to (barely) keep it all from being one colossal masquerade breach. For example, the person compelling the animals to do tricks is using Animalism, the hypnotist getting people to do the chicken dance is using Dominate, and the trapeze artists is simply using the fact she can get up and run off after an 50-foot fall.<br /> <br /> This section carries bit of <i>Something Wicked This Way Comes</i>, <i>Freaks</i>, <i>The Cabinet of Dr. Caligari</i>, and presumably <i>Vampire Circus</i> (which I\u2019ve not seen but the title is right). The Night Circus has been around for centuries, so it might be something the PCs encountered as mortal children only to run into it again. This aspect, and the relative appeal of a circus (\u201crun away and join the circus,\u201d as the saying goes) means could the show could be a starting point for mortals who become vampires.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, that same seductive appeal of a circus \u2013 and the call of the road \u2013 might well persuade Camarilla PCs to joining the Night Circus on its travels. It does sound like a lot of fun with few responsibility or obligations to bow to Princes. Even if they don\u2019t join it, they PCs might easily get roped into dealing with the Night Circus.<br /> <br /> In 1996 (24 years? God damn it) White Wolf published <i>Midnight Circus</i>. That supplement was intended to hit similar notes, but it mostly suffered from being over stuffed. All the splats at the time (Vampire, Werewolf, Mage, Wraith, and Changeling) found representation in the book, in addition to other worldly entities and an evil plot from the dawn of time. Night Circus is leaner, but might still be home to any number of strange vampires.<br /> <br /> This section does a nice job of depicting Anarchs who are generally apolitical, but still deadly and wicked.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1208,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","user":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","date":". 09-08-2020, 10:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-10T08:30:53-07:00","id":1412851,"title":"","content":"<b>Delusions of Humanity</b><br /> <br /> This is an interesting read and another that feels like the back story of a PC.<br /> <br /> A former au pair for a British couple talks about how the husband of the couple was - and is - secretly a vampire. And he turned her into a vampire, even as he led a highly closeted life. The vampiric au pair had the wife of the couple turned into a vampire out of pity as much as anything else. Eventually the wife and the vampiric au pair fled the scene, leaving the children to the closeted vampire husband. The vampiric au pair is an Anarch probably more by Camarilla definition than by her own political stance.<br /> <br /> The section reads more like bathos than outright comedy, even dark comedy. There is some interesting, if bleak, insight into human nature with the husband in denial of his own nature and the wife drowning in her own misery and finding pitiable relief in a fantasy life. But aside from being a possible background for a PC, the section offers little for a VtM game, Anarch or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1208,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","user":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","date":". 09-10-2020, 02:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-10T16:31:26-07:00","id":1412928,"title":"","content":"It indirectly shows cleaver culture, a bit like <i>Is it OK to feed vitae to a baby?</i> but from a different perspective and healthier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-10T19:52:24-07:00","id":1412951,"title":"","content":"I'm not certain i would call it healthier...<br /> <br /> <b>Is it OK to feed vitae to a baby? </b><br /> <br /> This is my favorite single part of the book because it is utterly made of wrong.<br /> <br /> In this short section an Anarch with a mortal child posts to Anarch Reddit, asking if it is alright to feed vitae to the human baby. You know, to settle them down if they are fussy or something and you are out of the whiskey you normally use. A bunch of other Anarchs jump in to say yes, or no, and even discuss moderate feeding from their own human children. Assuming that the respondents are not utterly full of crap, then a striking number of Anarchs have mortal children. It is worth considering if those children are actually their own (as in ones they had in the normal way while still human), or ones they picked up somewhere along the way. The Anarchs arguably are taking the children of others - possibly their murder victims - and then raising and grooming the children to be ghouls. At which point the Anarchs have children in the same way humans have cats and dogs. In any case, one or more of the children's actual parents may be out and about looking for them, putting posters up on telephone poles and the like.<br /> <br /> Vampires are not good people. Vampires cannot be good people. The Camarilla is simply Control, and the Anarchs are simply Chaos.<br /> <br /> This section was also sadly cut when the book was reworked, following the issues with the <i>Camarilla </i>book. It is disappointing this section was removed as it clearly depicts the Anarchs as monsters in a way almost nothing can.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-11T01:18:46-07:00","id":1412973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1412951#post1412951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not certain i would call it healthier...<br /> <br /> <b>Is it OK to feed vitae to a baby? </b><br /> <br /> This is my favorite single part of the book because it is utterly made of wrong.<br /> <br /> In this short section an Anarch with a mortal child posts to Anarch Reddit, asking if it is alright to feed vitae to the human baby. You know, to settle them down if they are fussy or something and you are out of the whiskey you normally use. A bunch of other Anarchs jump in to say yes, or no, and even discuss moderate feeding from their own human children. Assuming that the respondents are not utterly full of crap, then a striking number of Anarchs have mortal children. It is worth considering if those children are actually their own (as in ones they had in the normal way while still human), or ones they picked up somewhere along the way. The Anarchs arguably are taking the children of others - possibly their murder victims - and then raising and grooming the children to be ghouls. At which point the Anarchs have children in the same way humans have cats and dogs. In any case, one or more of the children's actual parents may be out and about looking for them, putting posters up on telephone poles and the like.<br /> <br /> Vampires are not good people. Vampires cannot be good people. The Camarilla is simply Control, and the Anarchs are simply Chaos.<br /> <br /> This section was also sadly cut when the book was reworked, following the issues with the <i>Camarilla </i>book. It is disappointing this section was removed as it clearly depicts the Anarchs as monsters in a way almost nothing can.</div> </div> </div> </div>But IS it healthy?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-11T05:26:42-07:00","id":1412991,"title":"","content":"[deadpan] Probably not. I mean, Anarch parents are probably anti-vaccers. [/deadpan]<br /> <br /> And I doubt the children of the couple in <i>Delusions </i>are better off left in the care of a single vampire parent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1208,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","user":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","date":". 09-11-2020, 09:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-11T10:04:55-07:00","id":1413051,"title":"","content":"That might be right actually. The baby thread is more sensationally taboo, which was validated by its removal from the new edition, but Freya (I assume) only said what she knew. The two of them hark to some sort of kindred <i>Jeremy Kyle Show</i>.<br /> <br /> The more I think about it, the more I like the idea of the dysfunctional relationship issues of young kindred being used a form of public entertainment, ending with executions or the occasional enslavement to resolve the matters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-11T13:55:31-07:00","id":1413095,"title":"","content":"Giving your child Vitae and discussing it online is so comically fucking stupid. <br /> <br /> -Parent is such a moron that they need to ask the question<br /> -Parent can't be that much of a moron because they can find a website to discuss this. <br /> -Vampires are such morons that such a chatroom would exist. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-11T14:00:08-07:00","id":1413097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1413095#post1413095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Giving your child Vitae and discussing it online is so comically fucking stupid.<br /> <br /> -Parent is such a moron that they need to ask the question<br /> -Parent can't be that much of a moron because they can find a website to discuss this.<br /> -Vampires are such morons that such a chatroom would exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. One of the chief advantages of the Anarchs is their access to the web and ability to share information that Elders would otherwise deprive them.<br /> 2. Secure communication among Anarchs is something they hopefully pass among one anothers.<br /> 3. Better the alternative than self-experimentation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-11T14:09:12-07:00","id":1413101,"title":"","content":"That a parent visits a forum to ask questions and discuss issue is not a surprise, nor is it stupid. It's a real life that people do. Vampires, being vampires, poison and ruin everything they touch. Of course hey are going to asking about ghouling children. Some fool probably also goes on line to talk about diablre.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-11T17:50:13-07:00","id":1413137,"title":"","content":"<b>Los Nueves</b><br /> <br /> For a good time the Acapulco Anarch\u2019s shoot each other in the face.<br /> <br /> Adeyemi reports on another subculture \u2013 but this one probably doesn\u2019t have a mortal counterpart. But it probably has a Sabbat origin. While vampires can survive getting shot most anywhere \u2013 chest, groin, face, etc. \u2013 that is not the same thing as saying it is enjoyable. The level of violence of this sport, the abasement of the participants, the way it sets the participants apart from the human, and it being in a formally Sabbat city\u2026 all goes to suggest the Anarchs adapted it from the former Big Bag Sect of the WoD.<br /> <br /> This section does most to a potential plot for a game session; the Pcs go and hang around with NPcs in some forlorn place and shot the hell out of each other.<br /> <br /> Adeyemi also possess a strong character voice.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-11T18:18:28-07:00","id":1413142,"title":"","content":"<b>Anarch Cities</b> <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Acapulco, Mexico</li> <li>Berlin, Germanu</li> <li>Indianapolis, IN USA</li> <li>Joliet, Il USA</li> <li>Las Vegas, NV USA</li> <li>Los Angeles, CA USA</li> <li>Madison, WI USA</li> <li>Naples, Italy</li> <li>Reykjavik, Iceland</li> <li>San Diego, CA USA</li> <li>Toamasina, Madagascar</li> <li>Washington D.C. , USA</li> <li>Tbilisi, Georgia</li> </ol><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1208,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","user":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","date":". 10-18-2020, 11:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-11T18:30:58-07:00","id":1413145,"title":"","content":"The game they were playing, Nines, was originally from Revised's Guide to the Anarchs. It had a bunch of other really fun ones:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You know about most of the Anarch popular games that have been devised in addition to Nines, such as Sixty-Nines, an unpleasant variant of Nines in which one participant doesn't know it's a game; Bear-Baiting, the delicate art of goading elders to Frenzy in Elysium while adhering to the rules; LA Roulette, in which two Anarchs duke it out by hitting one another with a bat until one concedes; and Gotcha, wherein you try to convince a mortal that he's accidentally killed you. (GttA: 69-70) </div> </div> </div>Gotcha is absolutely hilarious and I'd love to have seen a section on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-11T18:43:30-07:00","id":1413146,"title":"","content":"I guess I was wrong about Nines then. But I would not cross a busy road to play Gotcha.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-11T23:04:39-07:00","id":1413170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1413137#post1413137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Los Nueves</b><br /> <br /> For a good time the Acapulco Anarch\u2019s shoot each other in the face.<br /> <br /> Adeyemi reports on another subculture \u2013 but this one probably doesn\u2019t have a mortal counterpart. But it probably has a Sabbat origin. While vampires can survive getting shot most anywhere \u2013 chest, groin, face, etc. \u2013 that is not the same thing as saying it is enjoyable. The level of violence of this sport, the abasement of the participants, the way it sets the participants apart from the human, and it being in a formally Sabbat city\u2026 all goes to suggest the Anarchs adapted it from the former Big Bag Sect of the WoD.<br /> <br /> This section does most to a potential plot for a game session; the Pcs go and hang around with NPcs in some forlorn place and shot the hell out of each other.<br /> <br /> Adeyemi also possess a strong character voice.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd argue that it's probably something from the Sabbat and Anarch's shared heritage. While the Anarchs and Sabbat separated at the Treaty of Thorns, the ones who surrendered did NOT actually cease to exist or cease to be Anarchs as much as some vampires like to portray their actions as. They were perfectly able to pass down the lessons of the original Anarch Movement to the next generation and keep some continuity as we see with Tyler.<br /> <br /> I imagine the original form of the game was probably shooting each other with arrows, crossbow bolts, swords, and so on. It's a very easy game to get the hang of and easily fits both of them.<br /> <br /> It's also one I suspect, like beer pong, that has been independently &quot;created&quot; many times over by sufficiently bloodthirsty Anarchs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-14T20:25:23-07:00","id":1413695,"title":"","content":"<b>24 Hour Party Bloodsuckers</b><br /> <br /> \u201cParty all night. Sleep all day. It\u2019s fun to be a vampire.\u201d<br /> <br /> That quote from the film Lost Boys more or less sums up this section. It is a first person account of a pair of vampires, in a toxic friendship, and their feeding habits in Reykjavik. There is not much else to say about it, except it is a little dull after all the preceding sections of vampires going through their nights with no cares about the jyhad.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-14T20:34:48-07:00","id":1413698,"title":"","content":"Oh, FYI, this thread compelled me to finish CHICAGO FOLIOS' WIR. I'm really plowing through the NPC section.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-14T20:38:09-07:00","id":1413699,"title":"","content":"<b>Roll Call of the Revolution</b><br /> <br /> Rudi returns to reiterate a statement from Garcia back in <i>No Prince, No Caine</i>. Basically, there a many types of Anarchs and a lot of them do not care about the jyhad.<br /> <br /> Anarchs is a catch all term used by the Camarilla for all the vampires than are not Camarilla (I wonder if they use it for the Hecata?). By and large only the really politically active Anarchs bother to call themselves Anarchs \u2013 the rest of them are preoccupied anything other than the endless revolution and politics are simply the Unbound. What the Unbound and the Anarchs have in common is a desire for a better existence than the one possible under the rule of the Ivory Tower.<br /> <br /> Interestingly, Rudi writes that\u2026<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2026the worst enemy of Anarch cohesion is simple geography. We\u2019re all connected to the mortal communities that spawned us, much more than the Camarilla is. </div> </div> </div>I would have thought the reverse to be the case. A nomadic existence is far more common among the Anarchs than it is among the Camarilla. And the Camarilla seems temperamentally the type to encourage staying in a home city for decades, or even centuries at a time. Further, the \u201cconservatism\u201d (big air quotes) of the Camarilla would suggest they are the ones to nurse hate boners from their living days, more so than the dynamic Anarchs.<br /> <br /> Still, this section is repetitious in specifics and themes \u2013 something that has dogged the last few sections.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-15T01:55:35-07:00","id":1413736,"title":"","content":"Excellent as always.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1413699#post1413699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would have thought the reverse to be the case. A nomadic existence is far more common among the Anarchs than it is among the Camarilla. And the Camarilla seems temperamentally the type to encourage staying in a home city for decades, or even centuries at a time. Further, the \u201cconservatism\u201d (big air quotes) of the Camarilla would suggest they are the ones to nurse hate boners from their living days, more so than the dynamic Anarchs.<br /> <br /> Still, this section is repetitious in specifics and themes \u2013 something that has dogged the last few sections.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree because I think the implications are that Camarilla communities SUBSTITUTE for human interactions.<br /> <br /> One of the things that came up in my 90s V:TM games was the fact player characters almost ignored the existence of humans entirely. All the NPCs they dealt with were vampires and even ghouls were more like furniture. In a Camarilla city, you can easily never deal with humans save as slaves and have your entire social circle be undead. In TRUE BLOOD, they said this was one of the ways that vampires could become monstrous. If you were part of a &quot;nest&quot; then all your worst attributes would be magnified by each other normalizing them.<br /> <br /> Anarchs, by contrast, must deal directly with humans on a regular basis due to their lack of a formalized society and that will have result in them having more difficulty dismissing them as just food.<br /> <br /> <b>Re: The Morality of the Anarchs in V5</b><br /> <br /> I think one of the things that V5 suffers from a bit is the fact that it is trying a bit too hard to be dark and edgy. It wants to capture that 90s era zeitgeist of being grimdark before we had a word for it. This is a post-Game of Thrones and HBO's Watchmen world, though. What passes for dark and edgy, especially among geek media, is a great deal different.<br /> <br /> Still, I think this could have definitely used some nicer vampires as putting everyone in a moral event horizon doesn't actually benefit the story. The Lannisters are shocking because their behavior contrasts against the Starks. Part of what made V:TM interesting is that it made vampires into creatures with consciences (or at least popularized them among gamers) instead of making them Always Chaotic Evil creatures.<br /> <br /> So this is actually a step back from the more nuanced portrayals of previous editions. After all, there's nothing &quot;new&quot; about a vampire preying on a bunch of innocent hikers or metal fans. That's the most classic vampire depiction there is. The monster who portrays itself as a nice person and then murders people that consider it a friend.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 09-15-2020, 06:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-15T04:15:22-07:00","id":1413749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1413736#post1413736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the things that came up in my 90s V:TM games was the fact player characters almost ignored the existence of humans entirely.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is more the fault of storytellers and players and somewhat a learned thing from the books that could've done a little better with the emphasis. I've never had a problem with humans being marginalized, but that's largely due to either small table sizes where we can afford to develop characters or because we had good storytellers. I do think 'pff, mortals are beneath us' is an attitude that can come up, but I think if you're playing a large game much of that 'dealing with the humans, fostering close relations and staying close to humanity' needs to stay in the downtime, not where there's five of you and you need to get stuff done. They've definetly overcorrected this in V5 with 'Look how scary the SI are!1!1! humans are terrifying!.' thing. If anything the SI make hunters more alien to me: There's something a lot more human about a bunch of small time crooks, yokels and 'soccer mom's' trying to get their shit together in taking down a vampire in comparison to a highly profesional paramilitary.<br /> <br /> The Camarilla and anarchs are about the same when it comes to human social interaction. The Camarilla has more secluded elders, but the Anarchs have more vampire x vampire ties, and they also have more vampires on paths of enlightenment (So the Anarchs are probably a bit worse really, but they're younger and that's a plus). most vampires from both sects spend most of their time entertaining themselves, hunting, managing their domains and the mortals who they're close to, not galavanting around completing the prince's quests, not hanging in elysium, just doing their own thing in their own domains with the company of mortals and retainers.<br /> <br /> (unless they're the half the Tremere who are happily cloistered and are more likely to 'order room service' than go out and hunt.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 09-15-2020, 07:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-15T08:21:49-07:00","id":1413782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1413749#post1413749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is more the fault of storytellers and players and somewhat a learned thing from the books that could've done a little better with the emphasis. I've never had a problem with humans being marginalized, but that's largely due to either small table sizes where we can afford to develop characters or because we had good storytellers. I do think 'pff, mortals are beneath us' is an attitude that can come up, but I think if you're playing a large game much of that 'dealing with the humans, fostering close relations and staying close to humanity' needs to stay in the downtime, not where there's five of you and you need to get stuff done. They've definetly overcorrected this in V5 with 'Look how scary the SI are!1!1! humans are terrifying!.' thing. If anything the SI make hunters more alien to me: There's something a lot more human about a bunch of small time crooks, yokels and 'soccer mom's' trying to get their shit together in taking down a vampire in comparison to a highly profesional paramilitary.<br /> <br /> The Camarilla and anarchs are about the same when it comes to human social interaction. The Camarilla has more secluded elders, but the Anarchs have more vampire x vampire ties, and they also have more vampires on paths of enlightenment (So the Anarchs are probably a bit worse really, but they're younger and that's a plus). most vampires from both sects spend most of their time entertaining themselves, hunting, managing their domains and the mortals who they're close to, not galavanting around completing the prince's quests, not hanging in elysium, just doing their own thing in their own domains with the company of mortals and retainers.<br /> <br /> (unless they're the half the Tremere who are happily cloistered and are more likely to 'order room service' than go out and hunt.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, wait how coming is draining a person die type of feeding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-15T20:37:20-07:00","id":1413898,"title":"","content":"<b>Lasciami</b><br /> <br /> The book finally provides something a bit bloodier than vampires hanging around night clubs in Iceland or climbing mountains.<br /> <br /> It gives us the Anarch Mafia. Who probably operate a lot like this\u2026<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/nqSIVSaT__U?t=25\" data-code=\"nqSIVSaT__U\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/nqSIVSaT__U/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> Lasciami is Italian for \u201cleave me alone,\u201d or \u201cget off of me,\u201d more or less. Such as might be the final words of an Italian speaker being attacked by a vampire.<br /> <br /> The section presents as the transcript of a recording between people speaking Italian about murders are public relations statements, while in the city of Naples. The recording was probably made by Italian law enforcement pursuing organized crime, and it probably eventually ended up in the hands of the SI.<br /> <br /> Classically in the World of Darkness, vampires and crime in Northern Italy were dominated to a large extent by the Giovanni and the Mala del Brenta, with crime and vampires in Southern Italy dominated by the La Cosa Nostra and the Brujah. Given its position, I would guess Naples fell under the dominion of the La Cosa Maybestra.<br /> <br /> Yes, I know it would actually be the Camorra, but La Cosa Maybestra is funnier.<br /> <br /> In any case, some assassins with apparently little respect for subtly, law or good taste are scaring the mortals and performing notable murders in Naples. A pair of hoodlums are talking about their fear of these assassins \u2013 who they do not realize are vampires \u2013 but the two are willing to do business with the killers anyway.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Bo7zkd0kRS4\" data-code=\"Bo7zkd0kRS4\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/Bo7zkd0kRS4/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> The hoods ask the assassins why they want blood as payment, and why they drain blood from victims. The assassins flatly state they are vampires \u2013 taking refuge in audacity. The hoods are not very bright but are pretty determined. They are making a deal with the Devil, one they will not be able to control. The entire sections reads like an early scene in a horror story involving the mafia and vampires, and it is great.<br /> <br /> The section does pose a lot of questions, but ones which should provide a lot of fodder for Storytellers and PCs. Such as, how does the local Prince respond to the theatrical and Masquerade breaking murders committed by the Anarch mafia? How would any vampires involved with the Camorra respond to Anarchs poaching on their territory?<br /> <br /> The section presents vampires who are again probably not worried about the jyhad, but are more engaging that pretty much any of the others in the last six sections.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-16T08:08:25-07:00","id":1413970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1413898#post1413898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The section does pose a lot of questions, but ones which should provide a lot of fodder for Storytellers and PCs. Such as, how does the local Prince respond to the theatrical and Masquerade breaking murders committed by the Anarch mafia? How would any vampires involved with the Camorra respond to Anarchs poaching on their territory?</div> </div> </div> </div>Naples has a baron, named Carlotta Rossellini in <i>Cults of the Blood Gods</i>. The vampires in this scene might even be Hecata. It's one way to get blood without biting after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-16T08:24:29-07:00","id":1413973,"title":"","content":"I will take your word for it about CotBG - I don't have the book. And the assassins being Hecata is a good, and disturbing, twist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-16T18:08:27-07:00","id":1414108,"title":"","content":"<b>Soy Cuba</b><br /> <br /> I enjoy research and chasing down references. I mention this because I usually try to catch and check out the references in these WIR, in this <i>Anarch</i> book, in the <i>Camarilla</i> book and in the <i>Beckett\u2019s Jyhad Diary</i> book.<br /> <br /> Soy Cuba, as a term, led down an interesting rabbit hole.<br /> <br /> \u201cSoy Cuba\u201d is Spanish for \u201cI am Cuba.\u201d <i>Soy Cuba</i> is also the name of a movie. According to Wikipedia;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>I Am Cuba</i> (Spanish: <i>Soy Cuba</i>; Russian: \u042f \u041a\u0443\u0431\u0430, <i>Ya Kuba</i>) is a 1964 film directed by Mikhail Kalatozov at Mosfilm. An international co-production between the Soviet Union and Cuba, it was not received well by either the Russian or Cuban public and was almost completely forgotten until it was re-discovered by filmmakers in the United States thirty years later. The acrobatic tracking shots and idiosyncratic mise en scene prompted Hollywood directors like Martin Scorsese to begin a campaign to restore the film in the early 1990s.<br /> <br /> The film is shot in black and white, sometimes using infrared film obtained from the Soviet military to exaggerate contrast (making trees and sugar cane almost white, and skies very dark but still obviously sunny). Most shots are in extreme wide-angle and the camera passes very close to its subjects, whilst still largely avoiding having those subjects ever look directly at the camera. </div> </div> </div>Mise en scene is the arrangement of scenery and stage properties in a play, including the costumes, the selection of actors, sets, props and so forth. Mise en scene can also be understood as a single scene, or even a single image, that arguable serves as a symbol of the entire play or movie. Jack and the ghostly bartender in Kubrick\u2019s version of the <i>Shining</i> is a representative mise en scene for that movie, for example.<br /> <br /> <i>Soy Cuba</i> the movie is noted for its odd mise en scene, or odd staging, costumes and so forth. It presented a deeply distorted view of Cuba, which did not accurately represent the Cubans. The Cubans had little use for it.<br /> <br /> <i>Soy Cuba</i> the section in this book might serve as a representative mise en scene for all the problems and failures of the entire Anarch movement.<br /> <br /> <i>Soy Cuba</i> the section tells the story of a Cuba vampire reaching out to the Camarilla, asking for their intervention to depose a Russian survivor of the Brujah Council who has lately set himself up in Havanna as a strong man. This particular Cuban vampire resents the decisions of this strong man, how he is inviting Anarchs from across the world to come and set up shop in Cuba.<br /> <br /> History doesn\u2019t repeat, but it does rhyme.<br /> <br /> There are some humorous bits in the section as well, such as when the Cuban vampires says parties thrown by Russian blowhards suck, and when he worries about CIA involvement in Cuba.<br /> <br /> In any case, this is a solid section and one of the best in the book.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-16T18:09:52-07:00","id":1414109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=BwEabZrGFfI\" data-code=\"BwEabZrGFfI\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/BwEabZrGFfI/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-16T18:57:52-07:00","id":1414120,"title":"","content":"<b>The Brujah Council</b><br /> <br /> One thing I've noticed about V5 is the fact that it often takes concepts that were forgotten or discarded and then proceeds to make them integral parts of the setting. I'm not saying that's all on Matthew Dawkins but has a lot to do with his particular ethos. He loves taking throw away characters and concepts then reviving them to importance they never had in their previous embodiments.<br /> <br /> For example, the Brujah Council that's alluded to in this Cuban section. The Brujah Council was extinct from the start of V:TM. The Cold War was over by the time the ink was dry on the original green marble book. Instead, the Brujah Council was just a throwaway line about what Baba Yaga had killed to take over Russia. Except it turned out to be WEREWOLVES who ended up making the most of Baba Yaga (and then Baba Yaga was killed by a Niktuku in an unrelated V:TM adventure--pleasing no one).<br /> <br /> However, with the rise of the Russian Federation and Putin 2.0, the Brujah Council is suddenly back in business and communist Anarchs are now something interesting to explore in the Modern Era. The Soviet Union had a history of, like the CIA, arming insurgent and revolutionary groups worldwide. Many of which were the kind of firebrand anti-capitalists that inspire anarchists and communists alike among the undead. Or get co-opted by white middle class college kids with too much free time on their hands.<br /> <br /> Seeing the Brujah Council as potentially funding the Anarch Revolution worldwide is an interesting twist--albeit the kinds of governments it funds today might not be the same ones that Salvador thinks it will.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-16T19:37:35-07:00","id":1414127,"title":"","content":"It is a good use of resources in the lore, and the writers put it to good use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-17T09:50:46-07:00","id":1414222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1414120#post1414120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>The Brujah Council</b><br /> Seeing the Brujah Council as potentially funding the Anarch Revolution worldwide is an interesting twist--albeit the kinds of governments it funds today might not be the same ones that Salvador thinks it will.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is, uhh... painful to read.<br /> <br /> There's no incentive or ability for Russian Brujah to finance anarch movements. Idealism in the Soviet union died with Lenin and the union forgot about an international communist revolution and went for socialism in one state, IE Stalin wanted the USSR under his control and allied buffer states around him to protect... himself. During Lenin's rule one single type of housing was built for everyone. During Stalin's rule there were two, one for the people and one for 'the communist elite', if that's any indication of how much the USSR degenerated. Modern Russia is known by the populace to be ruled by Oligarchs. They're not under dellusions of fair democracy like the US, they know they're being ruled by Oligarchs.<br /> <br /> So with all that in mind, why would the Brujah council be making international moves? What would be the point? Modern communists aren't pining for a repeat of the USSR disaster, and russian information warfare isn't at all in favour of the left wing. If the BC had grudges with elders outside of russia (and why would they? They're all relatively young right?) how would they find foreign vampires and organize campaigns against them? Vampires don't benefit from left wing policies. What do the BC get out of doing... whatever it is they're doing?<br /> <br /> The important thing is that Information warfare is <i>good </i>for vampires. Patisanship and fascism and all that lovely stuff is great for vampires, Camarilla and anarchs alike. Maybe it's some long distance favour trading, but that's not really something that needs the mystery of &quot;The Brujah Council&quot;. They're not exactly avenging Carthage here and they're not likely to restore a USSR-type system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-17T10:36:09-07:00","id":1414229,"title":"","content":"I think you are forgetting<br /> (a) in the real world the cold war continued until the Soviet Union collapsed, and it did not end when Stalin died.<br /> (b) Vampires can create their own justifications to fight each other when those reasons would not otherwise exist, and this is a large part of the jyhad.<br /> <br /> Which is to say, the Brujah Council would have been fucking with the Camarilla, and the Camarilla would have been fucking with the Council, because<br /> (a) the Cold War went on for about 80 years,<br /> (b) vampires are assholes,<br /> (c) it makes for good stories.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-17T11:14:48-07:00","id":1414232,"title":"","content":"The support of the liberal Anarch Movement wouldn't necessarily be intended to make Californian style Anarchs the end goal or to protect kine in any way. The Brujah Council in this book is idealistic, but their ideals concern kindred, to the exclusion of kine. I assume that they don't want mortal communism per se, but police states, public or private, where kine don't ask questions when other kine disappear, which means that kindred have plenty of food and the masquerade is secure. They're probably looking at cities falling to the Second Inquisition and blaming all surviving sects for not controlling the intelligence services.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-17T17:28:52-07:00","id":1414299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1414222#post1414222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is, uhh... painful to read.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry to ruin what was obviously a very well thought out and interesting post but it falls apart very quickly at one observation: &quot;Why would you think the Brujah Council do something out of idealism?&quot;<br /> <br /> They would support world wide Anarch revolution for the explicit purpose of expanding their global power base and attacking the Camarilla's power base. The idea that Brujah would stop the expansion of their power base at the Soviet Union's borders is ludicrous when they have the apparatus of a global superpower at their beck and call. The elimination of other vampires only benefits their goal of expanding their power base and privilege globally. The idea that any vampire would be &quot;content&quot; at a mere Princedom when they could rule nations is silly.<br /> <br /> Also, some Anarchs seek more freedom. Other Anarchs seek far more draconian rulership that makes the Camarilla look like a party. The Anarchs are united by their hatred of the Camarilla--nothing more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 09-17-2020, 08:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-17T19:45:35-07:00","id":1414316,"title":"","content":"I've been partially fascinated by the Brujah Council when the game came out because it was never clear what it was about. So I think it's great that it's been finally addressed.<br /> <br /> However, I think they made a mistake by tying the Brujah Council in with the Anarchs because there was zero connection between the Brujah Council and the Anarchs in the original games. I don't remember it mentioned in any of the By Night books or the Anarch's Cookbook. Furthermore, what little we knew about the Brujah Council indicated it was antithetical to the ideals of the Anarchs. Anarchs were about trying to establish some kind of freedom from the elders. The Brujah Council was never about that. It was about the Brujah dominating the other clans. And while that obviously appeals to Brujah who make up a lot of the Anarchs, I don't see any of the other clans (or Caitiff) among Anarchs being enthusiastic about it.<br /> <br /> &quot;Council&quot; translated into Russian is &quot;Soviet&quot;. So Brujah Council is a just an English speaking way of saying Brujah Soviet. That makes the connection between human Communism and the Brujah Council which makes complete sense given the history we were given about the Council - both its origins and its demise were tied to the existence of Communist rule in Russia.<br /> <br /> While there had to be something different about the rule of the Brujah Council than the standard Camarilla, it didn't seem like it was a different sect. And certainly not a part of the Anarch movement.<br /> <br /> Therefore, I imagined that the Brujah Council was just a means for the Brujah clan to dominate local and regional Camarilla politics inside the Soviet Union. Unlike everywhere else where the Brujah clan was split into different factions, this group of Brujah were united in a council... just like how the Bolsheviks dominated the original Petrograd Soviet. And probably equally tyrannical. I imagined that this united group of Brujah exploited the Bolsehvik takeover to destroy the power bases of the other clans, and probably slaughtered a lot of the other vampires from those clans. I got the impression that the Brujah Justicars used the Soviet Union as their base of operations just like Petrodon and Xavier operated in North America. Probably because all the Brujah Justicars of that era already had Slavic names. Furthermore, the Camarilla already had an institution similar to a council - the Conclaves. And if the Brujah Council was a counterpart to the Bolsheviks, than the Conclaves could be used by them like the Bolsheviks used the soviets - as a means to entrench themselves in power. A semi-perpetual Conclave, dominated by the Brujah Council and lead by a Brujah Justicar could do just that. Until the entire leadership of the clan was gobbled up.<br /> <br /> Now all of this was in my head instead of detailed in the game. But it made sense. It explained how the Brujah could dominate the cities of the Soviet Union, by a very different thing from the rest of the Camarilla, yet not be an actual opposing sect.<br /> <br /> I don't know how accurate my suppositions were, but I think it'd be closer than this new revelation that these were supposed to be Anarchs. But I'd be very interested in hearing from any of the original developers and writers of the Vampire game line what they intended when they created the Brujah Council in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-17T20:02:31-07:00","id":1414319,"title":"","content":"For me, the Brujah Council being an Anarch revolt makes perfect sense.<br /> <br /> What else would the &quot;vampire politics reflecting real life&quot; be other than Brujah Anarchs overthrowing Ventrue and Toreador Royalists, only to prove to be EVEN WORSE dictators?<br /> <br /> I mean, that seems a perfectly plausible Anarch revolution result.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-17T21:42:03-07:00","id":1414329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1414316#post1414316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, I think they made a mistake by tying the Brujah Council in with the Anarchs.....</div> </div> </div> </div>We don't know if the Soviet Brujah considered themselves Anarchs, or as a part of the supposed Anarch movement. We do know they did not consider themselves to be part of the Anarch Free States. The label of Anarch was stuck on them by the Camarilla, and it might only have been applied out of spite and after the collapse of the USSR and the disappearance of the ruling Soviet Brujah.<br /> <br /> And lately the Camarilla calls everything aside from themselves &quot;Anarch.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-18T02:45:21-07:00","id":1414341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1414329#post1414329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We don't know if the Soviet Brujah considered themselves Anarchs, or as a part of the supposed Anarch movement. We do know they did not consider themselves to be part of the Anarch Free States. The label of Anarch was stuck on them by the Camarilla, and it might only have been applied out of spite and after the collapse of the USSR and the disappearance of the ruling Soviet Brujah.<br /> <br /> And lately the Camarilla calls everything aside from themselves &quot;Anarch.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>A note that the term Anarch seems synonamous among Kindred with revolutionary as well. My take on the Brujah Council they're Anarchs the same way the Sabbat are. An organization born from the original Anarch movement.<br /> <br /> I think the Brujah Council would support Anarch movements around the world as &quot;useful fools&quot; who undermined Camarilla power.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-18T04:50:07-07:00","id":1414355,"title":"","content":"Why would they be useful at all? I'm living in the former soviet union now; if i was a vampire, how could I possibly mess with kindred outside my region and what motivation would i have to do that? I have problems far closer to home, why would I engage in conflict with externals? There's points to be made among the mortal populace: An intolerant and devisive society who fears the Other is a maleable one, but how does one get offensive here? <br /> <br /> The Camarilla is 'us', the anarchs are 'me'. The Camarilla might see everyone else as Anarchs but the Anarchs hardly see each other as brethren because anarchs have multiple opposing ideas.. <br /> This 'Brujah council' is likely to inspire it's own 'anarchs'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-18T04:58:20-07:00","id":1414357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1414355#post1414355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would they be useful at all? I'm living in the former soviet union now; if i was a vampire, how could I possibly mess with kindred outside my region and what motivation would i have to do that?</div> </div> </div> </div>1. Paying for other Kindred's activities.<br /> <br /> 2. Money, power. It's an international economy now and wasn't far from it in the years before. The Kindred being all restricted to one single city is something that I've never much cared for. A Ventrue's business interests should be able to affect Saudi Arabia, Venezuela, Cuba, and the entirety of national interests.<br /> <br /> [quote]I have problems far closer to home, why would I engage in conflict with externals? There's points to be made among the mortal populace: An intolerant and devisive society who fears the Other is a maleable one, but how does one get offensive here?[/iquote]<br /> <br /> It's established with the Sabbat vs. Camarilla to start. The simple fact is that vampires are all rivals and the Brujah Council represents a third sect that threatens the other two with their own groups. Like the Kuei Jin, they are an existential threat to the Camarilla and need to be destroyed. Just like the Brujah Council know the Camarilla is the same. Otherwise, they will expand out and consume the other.<br /> <br /> Territory, domain, money.<br /> <br /> Vampires do not share power.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Camarilla is 'us', the anarchs are 'me'. The Camarilla might see everyone else as Anarchs but the Anarchs hardly see each other as brethren because anarchs have multiple opposing ideas.. </div> </div> </div>Yes, exactly, and the Brujah Council undoubtedly cares little about their ideologies beyond, &quot;I want to blow up the Prince.&quot; The Brujah Council will give you the semtex. It doesn't need to know why you do it and honestly doesn't care.<br /> <br /> They just want to place their own guy in his place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-18T06:20:12-07:00","id":1414370,"title":"","content":"Before I move on to the next section of the book, there is no longer a Brujah Council or Soviet Brujah, as a real group. There are some survivors, but they are scattered about. However, prior to 1990, the Council existed. And it would have been screwing with the West to disrupt the Camarilla. Now it will just come down to how bored Princes are, and how much power they possess.So its not what they Soviet Brujah would do as what they did do, back in the day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-18T06:33:36-07:00","id":1414374,"title":"","content":"Changing topics and actually okay with conceding to <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25794_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25794\" data-vbnamecard=\"25794\">MyWifeIsScary</a> (he has local knowledge), I'm going to say that I think it is interesting to see what cities have fallen to the Anarchs. There's some fairly big names this time around and they no longer are just jokes.<br /> <br /> Cities we know have fallen:<br /> <br /> * <b>Washington DC</b>: Vitel may be an AINO but you don't have to follow the system when you're one of the most famous powerful vampires in the world.<br /> <br /> * <b>Berlin</b>: Because the Camarilla thought the previous Prince was too soft, they put in a hardliner and lost the city. I imagine they blame the previous Prince.<br /> <br /> * <b>Las Vegas</b>: I actually think it would be best to make Therese the Baron of Vegas because she's able to embody both sides of the city.<br /> <br /> * <b>Indianpolis</b>: Both an Anarch city AND a Ministry city.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-18T06:43:13-07:00","id":1414376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1414374#post1414374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* <b>Indianapolis</b>: Both an Anarch city AND a Ministry city.</div> </div> </div> </div>thought the ministry were anarchs...what went wrong?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-18T06:45:14-07:00","id":1414378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1414376#post1414376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> thought the ministry were anarchs...what went wrong?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm saying its specifically an Anarch city but predominantly Ministry, just like Los Angeles is an Anarch city and predominately Brujah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-18T07:51:47-07:00","id":1414400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1414374#post1414374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cities we know have fallen:</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1413142#post1413142\">I've updating the list of Anarch cities. </a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-20T19:22:21-07:00","id":1414862,"title":"","content":"<b>Ni Dieu Ni Maitre</b><br /> <br /> This is another section that feels like the back ground of a PC, or possibly a pair of PCs. It is not bad, but there are so many of these types of sections in the book it begins to feel repetitive.<br /> <br /> Specifically, an Anarch vampire falls for a Camarilla vampire and plays a role in the Camarilla neonate\u2019s defection from the Ivory Tower. Some details along the way include both characters being female, and the Anarch being black. The two become lovers under the proverbial nose of the Camarilla neonate\u2019s sire. His pettiness and control freak nature do as much to drive her to the Anarchs and her Anarch lover does to draw her away.<br /> <br /> This is not bad section and I\u2019m not dismayed by the lesbian aspect or the interracial aspect. However, this is another section of the book which provides little useful game material but works better (as I said) as the background of either one or two PCs. It more or less treads the same ground as four previous sections in those terms. However, it is engagingly written.<br /> <br /> The title of the section comes from the French slogan &quot;<i>Ni dieu ni ma\u00eetre</i>!&quot; (literally 'Neither god nor master') coined by the socialist Louis Auguste Blanqui in 1880. This is a suitably Anarch philosophy.<br /> <br /> As an aside, I have a hunch most Camarilla elders are bad in bed and bad at most social interactions \u2013 they rely too much on disciplines like Presence and Dominate, so much so their actual skill sets atrophy. After a while, when the powers wear off and the blood bonds break, the victims remember the elder as a petty jackass and selfish lover.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-20T20:08:07-07:00","id":1414867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1414862#post1414862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As an aside, I have a hunch most Camarilla elders are bad in bed and bad at most social interactions \u2013 they rely too much on disciplines like Presence and Dominate, so much so their actual skill sets atrophy. After a while, when the powers wear off and the blood bonds break, the victims remember the elder as a petty jackass and selfish lover.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, most Toreador don't bother with Seduction rolls at the Elder stage because why should you? The end result is the same.<br /> <br /> According to Outstar, who sticks closer to the rules than most Storytellers I know, its important to remember that most Kindred derive no pleasure from the sexual act at Humanity 7 or below. However, the Blush of Life is something all Kindred can do now and it seems far broader than previous editions in giving you the ability to feel as well as give pleasure. Elders I suspect don't bother with the Blush of Life versus simple feeding as the material is quite clear that the Kiss is more pleasurable than sex or drugs both.<br /> <br /> No need to bother to play with your food.<br /> <br /> Interestingly, I think we're after this point but since this is a romance section, one thing I noticed in the ANARCH book was that we get an update on E and Lilly. You know, the Thin Bloods from Bloodlines. Apparently, canonically, they're broken up because E managed to get a human woman knocked up.<br /> <br /> After all the crap I went through to get them back together too!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-21T15:56:34-07:00","id":1414979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1414341#post1414341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A note that the term Anarch seems synonamous among Kindred with revolutionary as well. My take on the Brujah Council they're Anarchs the same way the Sabbat are. An organization born from the original Anarch movement.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought the Brujah Council was less about being similar to Anarchs than simply another Brujah controlled attempt to recreate their &quot;utopia&quot; at Carthage which predated the Anarch Revolt by a long time.<br /> <br /> The sense I got from the original description 30 years ago was that just like Carthage was supposed to be a blend of &quot;harmonious&quot; relations between vampire and kine; that Brujah vampire control of human Communism was supposed to create a similar &quot;utopia&quot;. Except in the first the vampires at Carthage fed on discarded human babies left for human sacrifice, and the vampires in the Soviet Union fed on the political prisoners of the Gulag and other prison camps.<br /> <br /> Not all conflicts about vampire society in the Camarilla fits the dynamics of elder versus anarch. Sometimes these different elements can blend together, but that doesn't transform one into the other.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1414341#post1414341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the Brujah Council would support Anarch movements around the world as &quot;useful fools&quot; who undermined Camarilla power.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure the Brujah Council would support Anarchs for the same reason why Brujah elders (and sometimes others) in the Camarilla support the anarchs on occasion - they're useful tools that can be used to put pressure on their rivals and then discarded. Critias' temporary support for Maldavis didn't make him an Anarch.<br /> <br /> Again, because the books never indicated the Brujah Council and the Anarchs were ever tied, I always assumed it was some strange thing either part of the Camarilla, or something entirely new. But there was enough circumstantial evidence that indicated it was somehow part of the Camarilla.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-21T16:03:03-07:00","id":1414980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1414979#post1414979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Again, because the books never indicated the Brujah Council and the Anarchs were ever tied, I always assumed it was some strange thing either part of the Camarilla, or something entirely new. But there was enough circumstantial evidence that indicated it was somehow part of the Camarilla.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is not the case in ANARCHS UNBOUND.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1356870-wir-anarchs-unbound-anarchy-in-the-wod?p=1356946#post1356946\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1356870-wir-anarchs-unbound-anarchy-in-the-wod?p=1356946#post1356946\"> [WIR] Anarchs Unbound - Anarchy in the WOD - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1356870-wir-anarchs-unbound-anarchy-in-the-wod?p=1356946#post1356946\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1356870-wir-anarchs-unbound-anarchy-in-the-wod?p=1356946#post1356946 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> https://www.drivethrurpg.com/images/4261/127247.jpg I love Anarchs. I love Anarchs to an unhealthy degree. This is something that everyone who reads my posts </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The French Revolution and Soviet Union are identified as Anarch in nature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-21T16:12:57-07:00","id":1414984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1414374#post1414374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cities we know have fallen:<br /> <br /> * <b>Washington DC</b>: Vitel may be an AINO but you don't have to follow the system when you're one of the most famous powerful vampires in the world.<br /> <br /> * <b>Berlin</b>: Because the Camarilla thought the previous Prince was too soft, they put in a hardliner and lost the city. I imagine they blame the previous Prince.<br /> <br /> * <b>Las Vegas</b>: I actually think it would be best to make Therese the Baron of Vegas because she's able to embody both sides of the city.<br /> <br /> * <b>Indianpolis</b>: Both an Anarch city AND a Ministry city.</div> </div> </div> </div>One major problem I have with metaplot, is that originally the cities that were Camarilla, Anarch, and Sabbat made certain sense. But metaplot is determined to make the game stupid.<br /> <br /> Cities that retained a good economy and manageable crime, like Chicago in the 80s and early 90s, were Camarilla. Cities that had a good economy, but high crime like LA with its gang wars, were Anarch. Cities that were in decline economically and had high crime like Detroit, were Sabbat. Cities that had mixed elements tended to be contested which is why New York was predominantly Sabbat, but Manhattan was still controlled by the Camarilla. Miami, with its drug cartel wars but drug fueled economic boom, was likewise another city that could be a contested field.<br /> <br /> I think this early attitude of &quot;what makes sense given how these cities are in real life&quot; was a major strength of the initial setting. They created their history and sect strongholds based on the real world and worked their way back to explain it.<br /> <br /> However, metaplot destroys that strength because metaplot isn't concerned with any kind of connection with the real world. It's only concern is &quot;what can I do now to create the plot I want.&quot; It's why the Revised metaplot of the Sabbat Crusade didn't make sense in the late 1990s which was an era of decreasing crime and economic prosperity. It's like when watching a movie or TV and you see characters do things they absolutely would never do except that the plot requires them to do so.<br /> <br /> This list of cities seems similarly strange to me. Indianapolis as a stronghold of the Anarchs and Setites? Has anyone ever been to Indianapolis?<br /> <br /> To me, this clearly puts the WoD into a fantasy mode with little basis in reality.<br /> <br /> Now, I don't mind it when an individual ST decides something is different in their chronicle, because local chronicles have their own history and plots. But I think the published setting needs to make sense. If you say City X is ruled by sect Z, then I should go, &quot;Yes, that makes sense.&quot; Not &quot;these people don't seem to know what they are doing.&quot;<br /> <br /> There are plenty of cities I could see being new strongholds of the Anarchs. But this list doesn't seem to be it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-21T16:23:54-07:00","id":1414986,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a> <br /> <br /> I dunno, it depends on how close you see the WORLD OF DARKNESS to our world. I don't tend to think of the WoD as resembling our world + vampires alone. I feel that was the premise of the NuWoD. Requiem was just Earth+vampires. V:TM I feel is more, &quot;You know Tim Burton's Gotham City? A city with a bunch of art deco skyscrapers, literally insane levels of crime, and gargoyles everywhere? That is Chicago, New York, and Los Angeles.&quot;<br /> <br /> Mind you, I never actually took the idea of &quot;What actually reflects the Camarilla, Sabbat, and Anarchs&quot; very seriously because I honestly didn't think they did a very good job to begin with. The Sabbat's strongholds were Canada, Sweden, Norway, and other locations that generally did not have massive crime rates.<br /> <br /> <i>Montreal by Night</i> flat out admitted that the Montreal of the book had NO relationship to the actual Milwaukee of the real world and was all the better for it. I think this has been the case from the very beginning because of Milwaukee. <i>Milwaukee by Night</i> has a city that is home of the Vampire and Werewolf Vietnam. Presumably hundreds of casualties, daily battles of the undead, and a place where the strongest go to die.<br /> <br /> Milwaukee.<br /> <br /> The World of Darkness Halifax in Nova Scotia is more like this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/oz88kJSdT6Y\" data-code=\"oz88kJSdT6Y\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/oz88kJSdT6Y/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> So a bit GRAND THEFT AUTO versus reality.<br /> <br /> But that's just me and YMMV.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-21T16:31:44-07:00","id":1414989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1414980#post1414980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is not the case in ANARCHS UNBOUND.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I understand the current developers are saying this is the case. I'm pointing out that this was not the case originally, and introducing this at this late date is overturning what some people have been doing for 25 years or so. I also don't think the decision was well supported with the bits of canon we did have. It's effectively retroactive continuity or an alternate reality.<br /> <br /> It's why I don't support V5 and why I ultimately stopped buying books in the Revised era.<br /> <br /> The French Revolution is a little different, because I think it was always implied - and perhaps even stated - that this was one of those failed neo-Anarch uprisings before the LA Anarch Free State. Whatever the Anarchs may have achieved for a time during Paris ultimately did not have any impact on how things were governed. That's in contrast to the decades long rule of the Brujah Council.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-21T16:33:36-07:00","id":1414990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1414989#post1414989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, I understand the current developers are saying this is the case. I'm pointing out that this was not the case originally, and introducing this at this late date is overturning what some people have been doing for 25 years or so. I also don't think the decision was well supported with the bits of canon we did have. It's effectively retroactive continuity or an alternate reality.<br /> <br /> It's why I don't support V5 and why I ultimately stopped buying books in the Revised era.<br /> <br /> The French Revolution is a little different, because I think it was always implied - and perhaps even stated - that this was one of those failed neo-Anarch uprisings before the LA Anarch Free State. Whatever the Anarchs may have achieved for a time during Paris ultimately did not have any impact on how things were governed. That's in contrast to the decades long rule of the Brujah Council.</div> </div> </div> </div>Anarchs Unbound is a V20 product by Justin Achilli.<br /> <br /> We also had literally about 2 or 3 sentences about the Brujah Council in 1st Edition to Revised.<br /> <br /> I admit, I like this because I don't think the War of Ages would go away with the Treaty of Thorns. WHAT HAVE THE ANARCHS BEEN DOING FOR 600 YEARS? Basically, that's my question. The Sabbat are fundamentally not a revolutionary organization so I think the Anarchs should be behind pretty much every peasant revolt and revolution, no matter the actual cause. For example, I expect there to be Anarchs on both sides of the Civil War (Brujah John Brown fighting against racist Brujah separatists would be particularly sweet).<br /> <br /> But I don't see any reason that Brujah Communists can't fight Brujah Anarchists, Brujah fascists, and Brujah Democrats. Its the clan of extremism, not freedom.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 09-21-2020, 07:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-21T23:01:51-07:00","id":1415019,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the correction on Anarchs Unbound. But since I don't like Revised metaplot which was the brainchild of Justin Achilli, I'm not surprised he has a hand in yet another thing I don't like. He's an imaginative man with some good ideas, but he has a tendency to ignore things when they get in the way of the story he wants to tell (and force on everyone else by making it the new canon).<br /> <br /> Yes, there was very little mentioned about what precisely the Brujah Council was. I said that multiple times already. I made it clear that much of what I was saying based on my own interpretations. At the same time, I've had almost 30 years of developing my own ideas about the setting. And those big empty spots Developers are trying to fill in 20+ years later of the setting, well, many old fans have already done that. Because we weren't going to wait 20+ years until someone did so. Just explaining why I don't think retroactively making the Brujah Council some kind of Anarch group was the right decision.<br /> <br /> I also don't react as you do with interest on the question of what the Anarchs been doing the past 600 years because I think it's like Marxists trying to link the Spartacus Revolt or Medieval German Peasant Rebellions into a common Communist history. There's actually no link between them.<br /> <br /> The Anarchs ceased being a movement after the Treaty of Thorns. Any surviving Anarchs became the Sabbat (like Tyler originally). The pardoned Anarchs who joined the Camarilla probably spent the next few hundred years trying to make it work. And some became happy with the new status quo. Others sold our completely. Others were dissatisfied, but ultimately remained loyal to the Camarilla as the least bad option. It took some time before some of those pardoned decided to rebel against this new system. The neo-Anarchs are merely inspired by the original Anarchs. There's no institutional link between them. Of course, there were some former Anarchs who weren't very happy with the Camarilla, and eventually they started causing trouble again - probably a few centuries later and after the first Camarilla-Sabbat Wars were over. Because vampires can live hundred of years, some of these people also became neo-Anarchs. But the Anarchs as an organized group didn't exist after the Treaty of Thorns. And once the neo-Anarchs creeped in (as a result of new embraces mostly, not the old Anarchs coming back and taking the lead) they were fighting a different war than the original Anarchs because the Camarilla is a different organization than the elder society that existed prior to the Revolt. Altered Traditions, revised mores and customs, Conclaves. and other reforms made that so. I see the two movements linked only by one being the inspiration for the other. Not any actual institutional connection. Any such claims are just propaganda.<br /> <br /> The neo-Anarchs went through a series of failed revolts. And as such, lost most of their numbers and any organizational cohesion before the next one flared. Although there may have been a few old timers involved in multiple risings. It wasn't until the LA Free State was established that finally one could say there was now a distinct group, as opposed to loosely affiliated groups scattered over the centuries which shared the same name.<br /> <br /> The Brujah Council was never mentioned as being part of this legacy though. That's why they weren't considered to be Anarchs. Brujah &quot;revolutionaries&quot; of course. But that isn't the same as Anarchs. Not every Brujah who doesn't like the Ventrue or Toreador is an Anarch.<br /> <br /> I agree that Brujah Communists should fight Brujah Anarchists, Brujah fascists, and Brujah democrats. Not sure why you think that is a matter of dispute. The clan has never been united and intraclan fights are the norm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-23T10:36:09-07:00","id":1415206,"title":"","content":"<b>I:IV:XV</b><br /> <br /> There is nothing like a Masquerade breach in the form of a heretical confession of a Caine worshipping vampire to make an abusive sire sound like a dangerous cultist.<br /> <br /> This section takes the form of a letter written from a sire \u2013 V \u2013 to their childre. V discusses the workings, under moral and spiritual philosophy, of the Church of Caine. This group is also known as the Cainite Heresy.<br /> <br /> The Cainite Heresy is a kind of inverted Gnosticism. In standard Gnostic belief and practice the spiritual world, and spiritual creatures were created by a good deity while the physical world and physical forms were created to imprison divine spirits. In the Cainite Heresy version, vampires are except from the standard belief and are taken as perfect angels because of their nominally incorruptible forms.<br /> <br /> The Cainite Heresy presents a spiritual, or at least religious organization, for the Anarchs in addition to the Ministry of Love, or the rebranded Followers of Set.<br /> <br /> The sire writing the letter admits to a forcible conversion of their childre. This included a ghastly ritual transformation into a vampire. The childre in question is probably a fanatic devotee now, or an enemy who hates their sire and the church.<br /> <br /> Joliet is apparently home to a branch of the Cainite Heresy, according to Chicago by Night 5<sup>th</sup>. They are apparently brazen in their activates, almost to a Sabbat level.<br /> <br /> Edit: I think the section title is a reference to a Bible verse; 1 John 4:15, If anyone acknowledges that Jesus is the Son of God, God lives in them and they in God.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1208,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","user":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","date":". 09-23-2020, 01:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-23T15:54:00-07:00","id":1415242,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a><br /> <br /> That's a very valid way of looking at it but not the way I run the Anarchs through the ages. Basically, for me, the Movement never died but merely changed forms across the centuries. Mostly because &quot;Anarch&quot; is just what anyone who is against the Elders and the Elder system is in a city. It is a fluid title and one that is often applied to people who are not really Anarchs in any meaningful sense. It's a bit like saying &quot;terrorist&quot; or &quot;guerila.&quot; Anarch really describes a methodology of gathering the dsicontented in a city and using them to overthrow the Prince or organized opposition to the heirarchy than a significant movement.<br /> <br /> At least until the Camarilla banished the Brujah and the Gangrel. Combined with the Followers of Set's Civil War and the resulting divide into the Ministry/Church of Set, the Anarchs were truly disorganized even with massive successes like the French Revolution and Russian Revolution or whatever they were doing in South America versus the Sabbat and Camarilla.<br /> <br /> So, the Movement is now an organization post 5E but it was many smaller revolutions and people being called &quot;Anarchs&quot; for awhile.<br /> <br /> <b>Re: The Church of Caine</b><br /> <br /> I really like the idea of the Church of Caine being something that is thriving among the Anarchs. I like the idea that it provides a sense of meaning and strength to the people who would otherwise be lacking any kind of unifying identity. The Camarilla may have many Gehenna Cults and no longer actively persecuting Noddists but I choose to believe they still do their best to discourage those who spread the legends of the Antedluvians as well as Caine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-24T18:38:13-07:00","id":1415350,"title":"","content":"<b>The Legend of Bloody Qhawe</b><br /> <br /> In this section a vampire discusses how he sought justice for wrong done but in dealing with vampires he could only have bloody vengeance.<br /> <br /> This is pretty standard, but here these aspects rise above base tropes because the story in South Africa, somewhere near Johannesburg. The narrator is a probably one of the Zulu \u2013 Qhawe is apparently a Zulu word meaning warrior. He discusses the abuses his friends and family, and himself, suffered at the hands of a private security force working for a mining company. The narrator, and the still living people essentially enslaved by the mining company, is freed. These people are freed by vampire, some of whom the narrator recognizes.<br /> <br /> The section is well written. It is good to be reminded that Africa, and African vampires, exist. As with a number of vampires outside the Camarilla, they probably do not worry about titles or the jyhad. They are simply labeled Anarchs by the Ivory Tower. The Bloody Qhawe are one such group.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-24T19:01:17-07:00","id":1415351,"title":"","content":"<b>The O</b><br /> <br /> I\u2019ve decided Agata Starek looks and sounds a great deal like Outstar. It\u2019s in her eyes, the merriness, the capacity of homicidal violence\u2026<br /> <br /> Anyway, in this section Starek shows up and harasses a supposed friend who is dwelling in Milwaukee. Louis (the Anarch Starek is visiting) and Starek herself have both terminally offended a group of vampires called the Oswobodziciele. The O themselves are opposed to blood bonding people, which Louis did to some of them. Starek is all about punching up against bosses and forms of power, which suggests she and the O should have common ground. But they also take exception to people using them as target practice, which Starek apparently did sometimes before the story.<br /> <br /> Louis shows Starek a member of the O, his former servant, he has recaptured and is keeping chained up in his basement. She decides to embrace the fellow just because.<br /> <br /> Several things stand out about the story. For one, unlike most sections in the book, this one is presented as a traditional bit of fiction, with a third person omniscient point of view. For another, the neighborhood in which Louis dwells is oddly normal \u2013 humans feel safe enough for a girl to ride up the street after dark. Even so, Louis is an utter monster. He murdered the family of his former ghoul, and keeps prisoners chained to a wall in his basement (albeit with SnM gear because Louis is bad at planning). Starek herself compares the setup to that of a serial killer. Further, the Anarchs are just another set of tyrants to the people the enslave with the blood bond.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-24T19:27:22-07:00","id":1415353,"title":"","content":"Hey, is this Louis Fortier? The former Baron of Santa Monica? If so, I'm genuinely surprised he's still alive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-24T19:32:33-07:00","id":1415354,"title":"","content":"<b>The Ministry of Love</b><br /> <br /> The Anarchs have always been at war with East Asia. The Anarchs have no law, only crimes, says Lynskey. Nothing is illegal; social pressure is used to exert control, in place of law.<br /> <br /> (clears throat)<br /> <br /> Right. So this section is a transcript of surveillance the SI is performing on vampires of the Ministry of Love, first a pair discussing the name, an induction which goes wrong (or right, depending on your point of view), and then the ministry vampires determining they had been bugged and the bug was in a bit of decorative statuary. The SI provides analysis of the Minsitry, but like their action the SI are a day late and a dollar short.<br /> <br /> The section has some humor to it and perhaps even some irony. The vampiric Ministry of Love is not as powerful or frightening as the Ministry of Love in 1984, but I think the rebranded Settites were named for the group in Orwell\u2019s book. <br /> <br /> Unfortunately the section is too brief to really provide much insight into how the Ministry of Love operates, except when they are barely ahead of the SI.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-24T19:33:09-07:00","id":1415355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1415353#post1415353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, is this Louis Fortier? The former Baron of Santa Monica? If so, I'm genuinely surprised he's still alive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably not - the text describe him as coming from Europe, not Southern California.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-25T16:38:34-07:00","id":1415474,"title":"","content":"I actually like the idea of the Ministry being THE MINISTRY OF LOVE and not just &quot;The Ministry&quot; because it's just cheesy enough to be entertaining.<br /> <br /> Mind you, they could have been The Ministry of Darkness.<br /> <br /> I totally believe the Undertaker could be a Follower of Set.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1415351#post1415351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>The O</b><br /> <br /> I\u2019ve decided Agata Starek looks and sounds a great deal like Outstar. It\u2019s in her eyes, the merriness, the capacity of homicidal violence\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see it. Someone should tell her she should be the model for future Agata Starek appearances.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-25T18:06:19-07:00","id":1415487,"title":"","content":"The title &quot;Ministry of Love&quot; possesses a greater sense of irony and doublethink, than something like &quot;Ministry of Darkness&quot; or &quot;Ministry of Shifty Bastard what as you should not trust.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-25T18:08:18-07:00","id":1415488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1415487#post1415487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The title &quot;Ministry of Love&quot; possesses a greater sense of irony and doublethink, than something like &quot;Ministry of Darkness&quot; or &quot;Ministry of Shifty Bastard what as you should not trust.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Mind you, the whole reason they renamed themselves was that people were reacting to the Followers of Set as &quot;obviously evil.&quot; Which, obviously, they are.<br /> <br /> The Ministry of Love means that hopefully people will give them a bit more of a listen.<br /> <br /> &quot;WORSHIP SATA....I mean, worship our non-traditional god of EV...Freedom!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-25T18:35:38-07:00","id":1415491,"title":"","content":"Anarch: So is this Ministry of yours\u2026. Evil?<br /> <br /> Settite: What? No. I don\u2019t know why you would say that.<br /> <br /> Anarchs: You fellows wear black robes all the time, follow people about and say \u201cDo it\u201d everyone time one has a negative impulse, you are constantly surrounded by snakes and scorpions, and people who you take into your temples come out with radically different personalities.<br /> <br /> Settite: Pft. Sounds like you are a bigot.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-27T03:59:36-07:00","id":1415668,"title":"","content":"I got the overwhelming sense that the writers of V5 don't understand the Setites. I mean there's the church of Caine that gets the sobrequiet of 'gnostics' and they act like they've got nothing but enmity for the Setites who're apparently aimless mustache twirling villains, who've been gnostic from the very begining, but downplayed to just a chaotic-evil corruption cult in V5. (I really dig that preacher posted earlier in this thread, but that's a later addition in v5) <br /> <br /> They have a super-cool, totally legit religion. They've got Presence and obfuscate as in-clans; So they're charismatic and can be subtle about it. They've always been portrayed as everyone's BFF, And yet V5 gives them a super hammy Fuck-this-Clan weakness of being at a higher social difficulty to do anything other than be a sleaze? Imagine a real life cult leader who socially falls apart every time he interacts with people beyond 'do the gross thing'; Imagine if Tom Cruise just started to struggle getting people to like him every time he wasn't doing scientology shit. <i>it just wouldn't fucking work</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-27T09:13:50-07:00","id":1415693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1415668#post1415668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I got the overwhelming sense that the writers of V5 don't understand the Setites. I mean there's the church of Caine that gets the sobrequiet of 'gnostics' and they act like they've got nothing but enmity for the Setites who're apparently aimless mustache twirling villains, who've been gnostic from the very begining, but downplayed to just a chaotic-evil corruption cult in V5. (I really dig that preacher posted earlier in this thread, but that's a later addition in v5)</div> </div> </div> </div>The Church of Set is a lawful evil corruption cult in V5, the Ministry is the heroic plucky freedom fighters who worship a variety of gods.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They have a super-cool, totally legit religion. They've got Presence and obfuscate as in-clans; So they're charismatic and can be subtle about it. They've always been portrayed as everyone's BFF, And yet V5 gives them a super hammy Fuck-this-Clan weakness of being at a higher social difficulty to do anything other than be a sleaze? Imagine a real life cult leader who socially falls apart every time he interacts with people beyond 'do the gross thing'; Imagine if Tom Cruise just started to struggle getting people to like him every time he wasn't doing scientology shit. <i>it just wouldn't fucking work</i>. </div> </div> </div>I think that the Setites are fundamentally running headfirst into the fundamentals of their concept. The Clan was based on the John Milinus version of Set worship that, itself, was a rough bastadization of Robert E. Howard's Conan the Barbarian. It was originally just supposed to be a cult of evil, corruption, and darkness for player characters to go, &quot;Yeah, I'm a vampire and evil but not THAT evil.&quot;<br /> <br /> Which got people wondering why we needed the Setites and Baali both. Now, I loved the way that the Followers of Set were expanded upon by adding a Paradise Lost variant to it. &quot;Set is Lucifer and Lucifer is waging war against an unjust system by the Aeons to free us all.&quot; However, it's still pretty one note.<br /> <br /> I like the fact the Setites are having a doctrinal schism since as a fan of religious history in general, you aren't doing it right if people aren't fighting over doctrine. The Church of Set being a bunch of fundamentalists who feel that the other pagans have wandered too much off the, &quot;We are a cult of EVIL, Set dammit!&quot; feels appropriate. It also gives Ministry PCs a lot more options to construct their characters and some enemies off the bat.<br /> <br /> I admit, I love Noddism and the Church of Caine but I do think they stole a bit of the Setites schtick.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 09-27-2020, 12:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-27T11:55:49-07:00","id":1415711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1415668#post1415668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I got the overwhelming sense that the writers of V5 don't understand the Setites. I mean there's the church of Caine that gets the sobrequiet of 'gnostics' and they act like they've got nothing but enmity for the Setites who're apparently aimless mustache twirling villains, who've been gnostic from the very begining, but downplayed to just a chaotic-evil corruption cult in V5. (I really dig that preacher posted earlier in this thread, but that's a later addition in v5)</div> </div> </div> </div>I have a hard time picturing the church of caine getting along with the Typhonists<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1415693#post1415693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I admit, I love Noddism and the Church of Caine but I do think they stole a bit of the Setites schtick.</div> </div> </div> </div>you love noddism, you hate sabbat, you love the church of caine which have an even more messed up version of noddist lore, and you would rather they were championing &quot;Maltheism instead (Caine replacing Lucifer for standing up against God)&quot; instead of gnosticism, when the sabbat noddists do champion a &quot;Caine standing up against God&quot; approach to noddism...I am so confused","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-27T12:05:45-07:00","id":1415713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1415711#post1415711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a hard time picturing the church of caine getting along with the Typhonists</div> </div> </div> </div>I briefly studied to be a minister and it makes perfect sense to me. They hate each other because their religion is 90% identical but it's that little tiny bit, &quot;Caine vs. Set&quot; that trips them up. So they hate each other MORE than they would if their belief systems were totally antithetical.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> you love noddism, you hate sabbat, you love the church of caine which have an even more messed up version of noddist lore, and you would rather they were championing &quot;Maltheism instead (Caine replacing Lucifer for standing up against God)&quot; instead of gnosticism, when the sabbat noddists do champion a &quot;Caine standing up against God&quot; approach to noddism...I am so confused </div> </div> </div>I think it's an interesting case where my opinion on the Sabbat has been misrepresented. I love the Sabbat. I think they're completely awesome. I think that they are also best used as utterly messed up. I think the Sabbat lose a lot of their interesting elements if you make them a functional sect versus a mass of contradictions and people who don't &quot;get it.&quot; Part of this is nostalgia on my part because one of my longest-running characters was a Serpent of Light (former Dark Ages Follower of Set) Setite on the Path of Caine.<br /> <br /> Said character believed that the Sabbat was meant to be a posthuman bunch of philosopher kings who rose above the weaknesses of humanity and embraced a higher virtue than Humanity (which did not work for vampires at all). He believed in fighting the Elders, fighting the Antediluvians, fighting the oppressive Church, and a bunch of other idealistic things that the Sword of Caine would embody.<br /> <br /> The campaign climaxed in the Modern Nights with the character practically broken by the fact the Sabbat of the Modern Age were a bunch of complete assholes. He wanted to create Nieztschean Superman but the majority of Sabbat were the equivalent of Alt-Right trolls as well as thugs. It was a really effective roleplaying experience about the death of idealism as well as the realization that utopian dreams often fail.<br /> <br /> <b>How he wanted the Sabbat</b><br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/mWUxsUxMZ0E\" data-code=\"mWUxsUxMZ0E\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/mWUxsUxMZ0E/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> <b>How the Sabbat actually are</b><br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/2j3adcbEwSM\" data-code=\"2j3adcbEwSM\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/2j3adcbEwSM/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-28T02:48:35-07:00","id":1415791,"title":"","content":"From my reading it felt less a diegetic -We think the Setites are trash- and more an external -the setites are actually trash- . The &quot;church of caine&quot; having a narrow view is fine, but not even the setites are making a good cause for themselves. One should also consider that for most everybody the Setites are the OG fellows and the 'church of caine' are the new kids on the block who aren't so established. The Setites haven't actually been all that shy on the matter of sharing their religion. <br /> <br /> But maybe I'm biased since V5 has otherwise tried to put the hammer down on clans that have otherwise skirted away from humanity (lasombra, corpse fuckers, the Tzmisce still somehow lack a writeup and I'm assuming the Ravnos aren't coming back) and I can only lump in the setites with that behaviour.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-28T04:23:08-07:00","id":1415797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1415693#post1415693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which got people wondering why we needed the Setites and Baali both.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really, the people were wondering about that as soon as the Baali were introduced. Because when you say that preying on the innocents for personal gain is \ud83d\udc4c, vampire business as usual, but preying on the innocents FOR THE GLORY OF SATAN is irredeemable evil, that raises a lot of questions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-28T06:25:13-07:00","id":1415811,"title":"","content":"It's worth noting the views of the Ministry the book has presented so far are not thorough examinations of the Ministry's ideology or methodology. In the first section on the Ministry, Hesha talks about how it came to join the Anarchs. The second section on the group just follows a pair of its members as they barely stay one step ahead of the SI. By comparison, the sections on the Church of Caine and the Cult of Lilith, and even the crazy vampire Southern preacher, are provide a discussion of beliefs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-28T07:13:12-07:00","id":1415821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1415713#post1415713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The campaign climaxed in the Modern Nights with the character practically broken by the fact the Sabbat of the Modern Age were a bunch of complete assholes. He wanted to create Nieztschean Superman but the majority of Sabbat were the equivalent of Alt-Right trolls as well as thugs. It was a really effective roleplaying experience about the death of idealism as well as the realization that utopian dreams often fail.</div> </div> </div> </div>would you say the Sith are alt-right trolls?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I briefly studied to be a minister and it makes perfect sense to me. They hate each other because their religion is 90% identical but it's that little tiny bit, &quot;Caine vs. Set&quot; that trips them up. So they hate each other MORE than they would if their belief systems were totally antithetical. </div> </div> </div>90%...are you sure? how are they identical?<br /> I thought Typhonists were about being chained and breaking the chains of society,<br /> the cainite heresy was about vampires being divine spiritual beings and mortals material trash","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-28T07:24:33-07:00","id":1415822,"title":"","content":"The different groups in all the vampire sects (cults, factions, clans, etc) all have different ways to justify ways to justify the supposed superiority of vampires over humans. The Church of Caine asserts they are anointed by God, and thus backed by Divine Rules, to justify that dominance. The Ministry rejects pretty much as rules (divine and otherwise) and says &quot;do it&quot; because they can (which might make them the least hypocritical if not the most honest). They all differ in how their justification works, and will fight to the death over that justification, even if what they all really want is the power to hurt each other and eat people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-28T07:32:31-07:00","id":1415824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1415821#post1415821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> would you say the Sith are alt-right trolls?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 90%...are you sure? how are they identical?<br /> I thought Typhonists were about being chained and breaking the chains of society,<br /> the cainite heresy was about vampires being divine spiritual beings and mortals material trash</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Setites believe we're all divine spiritual beings (Mortals included) and that the embrace is a gift to help us break free of the world's chains.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-28T08:11:19-07:00","id":1415828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1415821#post1415821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> would you say the Sith are alt-right trolls?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you see the typical Sabbat of the Modern Nights like the SIth then I would say that we have a completely different view of them. The tragedy is how the Sabbat of the Modern Nights are completely controlled by the Beast and failing as a sect. This is notably prior to V5 and circa 2004 that the campaign reached its conclusion. It was pretty much a view of the Sabbat as established in Revised, which was two editions ago.<br /> <br /> The thing is that failing as a sect DIDNT MEAN THEY WEREN'T INTERESTING. Because dealing with that failure as a Sith-like Sabbat Elder was really interesting to roleplay.<br /> <br /> It's also not a belief that I am alone in as the Sabbat Civil War as described in Beckett's Jyhad Diary included a section about the Sabbat Elders wanting desperately to make Lucita their leader because they felt the organization was completely falling apart. Later, V5 confirmed that quite a few Lasombra defected because the Sabbat were just utterly given over to the Beast. I was just ahead of the curve by 15 years.<br /> <br /> Some Sabbat are genius philosopher Kings.<br /> <br /> Most Sabbat are guys eating babies.<br /> <br /> I mean, I like the occasional baby myself but it's not a lifestyle.<br /> <br /> <b>Star Wars: Old Republic Sith</b><br /> <br /> What's kind of bizarre is that this is actually the same plotline in Star Wars: The Old Republic if you're a Light Side Sith (or even a Dark Side Sith). One of the running themes of the Sith Warrior and Sith Acolyte (with Imperial Agent having a view from the outside) is the majority of Sith are fucking morons. Not just morons. FUCKING morons. They relentlessly abuse their allies and engage in petty cruelties to prove how hardcore they are. This engenders no loyalty in their troops as well as undermines any alliances they make. It also leads to infighting that ends up destroying dozens if not hundreds of competent Sith that would otherwise be allies against the Republic.<br /> <br /> It actually is the focus of the KNIGHTS OF THE ETERNAL EMPIRE expansion as you find out that the Sith Emperor, the guy everyone thought was a Darth Nihilus wannabe who wanted to destroy the universe, actually agreed with the LS Sith and Darth Malgus that the Sith Empire was doomed unless it went dramatic reforms. Hence he created a SECOND force-using Empire and then trained all of his servants to be loyal, happy, and patriotic with a fanatical desire to protect him personally.<br /> <br /> <b>The Sabbat are inverted in the War of Ages</b><br /> <br /> The funny thing about, &quot;The Sabbat are shooting themselves in the foot&quot; is that its the only time I side with the Elders rather than the Neonates in vampire. If you own a copy of <i>New York by Night</i>, one of the last supplements of &quot;Classic Vampire&quot; then you get more or less my argument in its entirety from the life of Katherine Wiese a.k.a Ecaterina the Wise. She's pretty much the ideal philosophical Sabbat. She rebelled for good reason against the Elders during the Dark Ages and wanted to build a New CarthageTM with the Sword of Caine.<br /> <br /> By the 20th century, she thinks they're all a bunch of violent thugs that want to kill her because she's lasted longer than most.<br /> <br /> I've admittedly met plenty of Sabbat fans who HATE this interpretation of the Sabbat and blame Justin Achilli for making the sect into a bunch of screaming morons but I feel like it's something that there's plenty of textual support for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 09-28-2020, 11:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-28T10:11:51-07:00","id":1415846,"title":"","content":"I think the Sabbat works <i>because </i>it's such a contrived clusterfucked entity. <br /> <br /> Some guy did a study and found that, with religious groups, the more severe and restrictive demands made of it's members, the more successful and long lasting the group will last. So the more moderate the sabbat gets, the weaker it'd become You've got a long list of -they're out to get us- enemies that keep everyone together, and you've got the viniculum. Because you're always at war you've always got a target for your aggression and no-time to go for the higher ups. Any time someone starts to be a problem (In spite of the viniculum) you can just kill em off and replace them. <br /> <br /> As for killing babies like... what's the point? Like it might have a use when you're trying to intimidate your enemies (Or to prove a point when YOUR FUCKING GHOUL THINKS SHE CAN EXIST AND HAVE A NORMAL LIFE OUTSIDE OF YOUR CONTROL, wait sorry that's a Camarilla reason to kill babies... nevermind) but doing it for the sake of doing it... like... you're just going to alienate yourself. Most Sabbat are embraced from fairly neurotypical stock. It might be fun to powertrip and kill a few people for fun but you're just gonna alienate packmates, create enemies, and necessitate a clean-up if you're killing kids. That's across the line for a lot of kindred. There aren't actually any paths that would support the activity. Chivalry doesn't forbid it but it's pretty darn dishonourable, Bones might have you watch a child starve but you're not going to kill the child yourself with that. <br /> <br /> <b>Honestly I imagine the worst excesses of the Sabbat (especially in sabbat domains) usually lead to monomancies (if not wassail).</b> Imagine you're Max, once a single parent of three, and your new back mate Andy thinks it's cool to dash the heads of kids on concrete: You're certainly going to want to dash Andy's head on concrete, or at the very least stop him. Andy's just made an enemy for the rest of his unlife. <br /> <br /> It's probably something you'd see more among anarchs, since the viniculum isn't around to keep you with people who aren't of the same mind, you can find coterie members with more in common (as if you could trust such psychopaths) <br /> <br /> <b>Food for thought: <br /> Tzmisce are exceptionally polite for two reasons:</b><br /> Firstly; So they don't wear out their welcome with other clans. <br /> Second: when they bring someone back for horrific vicissitude practice they can justify it with 'this person offended me/broke the rules/did something wrong' <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-28T11:12:55-07:00","id":1415857,"title":"","content":"I think the Sabbat ritae and games are actually designed to deliberately lower the Humanity of its members. They want to bring you into the fold of the Sabbat and in order to do that, they basically do the SS/Kingsman thing where they give you a puppy and tell you to kill it. This proves you're willing to do what the group tells you to do and alienates you further from your old life. Killing a baby is an extreme example but it shows that human is fully divorced from their old life as a human being.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/5VHVms6sVxQ\" data-code=\"5VHVms6sVxQ\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/5VHVms6sVxQ/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> Which is part of why I also think most Sabbat don't bother with Paths of Enlightenment because they eagerly embrace freedom from morality not attempt to impose a new one over their old view.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat are the negative Crime Syndicate/Justice Lords inverse of the Anarchs.<br /> <br /> They're a group who embraced the worst of the Anarchs until they became a funhouse mirror distortion of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-28T11:43:53-07:00","id":1415864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1415828#post1415828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you see the typical Sabbat of the Modern Nights like the SIth then I would say that we have a completely different view of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>they're the same in every way, except for the vinculum,<br /> the Sith are what the sabbat would be if they were allowed to hold dominion over mortals<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Later, V5 confirmed that quite a few Lasombra defected because the Sabbat were just utterly given over to the Beast. </div> </div> </div>V5 is the last edition to have any tell on what is and what isn't given to the beast,<br /> they have flexible tenets, meaning there isn't a single common morality to judge them with,<br /> and if it's the lack of touchestones that hurt them, then there's more than just the sabbat that should have been given to the beast<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It actually is the focus of the KNIGHTS OF THE ETERNAL EMPIRE expansion as you find out that the Sith Emperor, the guy everyone thought was a Darth Nihilus wannabe who wanted to destroy the universe, actually agreed with the LS Sith and Darth Malgus that the Sith Empire was doomed unless it went dramatic reforms. Hence he created a SECOND force-using Empire and then trained all of his servants to be loyal, happy, and patriotic with a fanatical desire to protect him personally. </div> </div> </div>the sabbat's whole history is reform,<br /> the sabbat's founding was itself a reform,<br /> getting more extreme and demanding with each reform,<br /> <br /> even since 2e, with montreal by night where 2/3rds of the dioceses and the archbishop were trying to break the trads,<br /> half of Mexico by Night was about comparing the traditional and modern structures and individuals and how they establish themselves and were trying to push for changes,<br /> even the Lasombra/Tzimisce had realised how much they'd screwed up and changed their attitudes,<br /> the lasombra eleminating clan members who abused their status to abuse the antitribu and even sending elders to join and help young packs,<br /> the Tzimisce starting teaching koldunism after the death of the Tremere antitribu had caused alot of damage...<br /> <br /> now v20 and v5 are tossing everything and saying &quot;hey, you know what would be better than the Sith? Ed Gein murder hobos&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The funny thing about, &quot;The Sabbat are shooting themselves in the foot&quot; is that its the only time I side with the Elders rather than the Neonates in vampire. If you own a copy of <i>New York by Night</i>, one of the last supplements of &quot;Classic Vampire&quot; then you get more or less my argument in its entirety from the life of Katherine Wiese a.k.a Ecaterina the Wise. She's pretty much the ideal philosophical Sabbat. She rebelled for good reason against the Elders during the Dark Ages and wanted to build a New CarthageTM with the Sword of Caine. </div> </div> </div>actually, New York by Night is a great exemple of how the sabbat had changed in their methods after their previous approaches failed,<br /> and, ironically, a funny illustration of how the Camarilla were starting to resort to Sabbat tactics after THEIR failures (yet somehow didn't pay the price for it, because it's not the sabbat amiright?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":10998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","user":"Pleiades","date":". 09-28-2020, 02:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-28T12:35:25-07:00","id":1415870,"title":"","content":"No, the modern Sabbat are a bunch of philosophy-less losers and have been since Revised. Which is a good campaign starter if you're a Sabbat Path of Enlightenment follower. How do you deal with the fact the Sabbat have just decided to throw in the towel on posthuman morality and just be assholes?<br /> <br /> When the only goal is diablerie and mayhem?<br /> <br /> Then again, some people don't like going against the crowd in their sect. This is, notably, a direct contrast to 2nd Edition Sabbat and very much a Revised version of the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> But like the Anarchs, you should play the version of the Sabbat YOU like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 09-28-2020, 03:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-28T12:56:03-07:00","id":1415873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1415870#post1415870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, the modern Sabbat are a bunch of philosophy-less losers and have been since Revised. Which is a good campaign starter if you're a Sabbat Path of Enlightenment follower.<br /> <br /> How do you deal with the fact the Sabbat have just decided to throw in the towel on posthuman morality and just be assholes?<br /> <br /> When the only goal is diablerie and mayhem?</div> </div> </div> </div>first, how is any sabbat (or camarilla for that matter) to reach any posthuman morality or any position of power without diablerie?<br /> why do you think the Camarilla was offered when they raided New York?<br /> they were offered free diablerie (just like in sabbat raids), and the ghouls were offered embrace (just like shovelheads being made true sabbat)<br /> <br /> second, &quot;most&quot; sabbat are worthless, of course they are, &quot;most&quot; are weak and can't do anything equaling the Lasombra luminaries or Tzimisce fire spitting dragon shamans (partly because both regularly eliminate or boycot the competition),<br /> <br /> but so what?<br /> the Sith aren't all Sith lords Beacons of the force, the majority are just drones, rapist soldiers and force leeches hunting down jedi to leech their force (diablerie),<br /> and you as a Sith decide if you're to stay a rapist drone, or want to aim higher<br /> <br /> still, when people talk about the sith, they always talk about the examplars, the Revans, the emperors and Gods who have their statues in Korriban,<br /> that's what DEFINES the Sith<br /> <br /> but whenever we talk about the sabbat, &quot;nah they're just street thugs that want to cause mayhem&quot; and we ignore the examplars","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-28T13:04:31-07:00","id":1415874,"title":"","content":"I'll play the version of the Sabbat that makes sense, and I'll encourage others to play a version of the sabbat that makes sense, thank you very much! I didn't go through three years of -ology just to be told the most naive approaches to the Sabbat are just as good as the ones that actually make sense. Also we're on a forum where we're supposed to vehemently disagree with one another. How are we to learn about anything if we just go 'You do you!' <br /> <br /> The Sabbat is a militant fascist theocracy. By it's very nature each initiate (True Sabbat, at least) are versed in a dogma and philosophy, even if they remain on the path of humanity. The Sabbat have goals beyond themselves, they are to serve their elders, unlike the Camarilla/Anarchs (I mean, obviously you do serve your elders in those sects, but that's not explicitly -the rules- of those sects, where it is in the Sabbat). The Sabbat are all bound by the viniculum. Though they may have personal goals, they all adhere to the sect's goals, whilist the Camarilla doesn't set any goals for neonates beyond the preservation of rules. <br /> <br /> The Sabbat doesn't want Wights, it wants effective soldiers. There's a big leap between killing a dog under orders and torturing babies for fun. The former is reasonable, Encouraging the latter makes for less effective (and obedient) soldiers. It's just stupid. <br /> <br /> If you want your organization to not-work-whatsoever- could you pick something that hasn't lasted half a millennium without changing all that much? <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-28T13:04:54-07:00","id":1415875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1415873#post1415873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> first, how is any sabbat (or camarilla for that matter) to reach any posthuman morality or any position of power without diablerie?<br /> why do you think the Camarilla was offered when they raided New York?<br /> they were offered free diablerie (just like in sabbat raids), and the ghouls were offered embrace (just like shovelheads being made true sabbat)<br /> <br /> second, &quot;most&quot; sabbat are worthless, of course they are, &quot;most&quot; are weak and can't do anything equaling the Lasombra luminaries or Tzimisce fire spitting dragon shamans (partly because both regularly eliminate or boycot the competition),<br /> <br /> but so what?<br /> the Sith aren't all Sith lords Beacons of the force, the majority are just drones, rapist soldiers and force leeches hunting down jedi to leech their force (diablerie),<br /> and you as a Sith decide if you're to stay a rapist drone, or want to aim higher<br /> <br /> still, when people talk about the sith, they always talk about the examplars, the Revans, the emperors and Gods who have their statues in Korriban,<br /> that's what DEFINES the Sith<br /> <br /> but whenever we talk about the sabbat, &quot;nah they're just street thugs that want to cause mayhem&quot; and we ignore the examplars</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, the Rule of Two actually addresses this.<br /> <br /> If you have 2 incredibly potent genius Sith Lords like Vykos and Moncada and 2000 street thug Sith then the 2000 street thugs Sith will team up on the geniuses rather than follow them.<br /> <br /> Which is exactly what happened to the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> So you need to get rid of the street thugs to have the posthuman Sabbat. Ironically, we know a posthuman vampire sect is POSSIBLE because we have the Assamites and Followers of Set Pre-Revised who embody that kind of &quot;alien inhuman morality&quot; that the Sabbat claims to.<br /> <br /> The Tzimisce and Lasombra were halfway there but they've fallen to street thuggery. Same for the Ravnos pre-Week of Nightmares. They're clans that degenerated.<br /> <br /> The Brujah are another good example of a Clan that began as awesome and have since become rabble.<br /> <br /> We're a bit off topic, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-28T13:08:10-07:00","id":1415876,"title":"","content":"BTW, this book can be summarized in one Pooh meme.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/hNja3r0.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-28T18:08:28-07:00","id":1415913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1415797#post1415797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Really, the people were wondering about that as soon as the Baali were introduced. Because when you say that preying on the innocents for personal gain is \ud83d\udc4c, vampire business as usual, but preying on the innocents FOR THE GLORY OF SATAN is irredeemable evil, that raises a lot of questions.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair the BaIi usually do even more vicious things for no reason,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-28T18:22:57-07:00","id":1415915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1415913#post1415913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be fair the BaIi usually do even more vicious things for no reason,</div> </div> </div> </div>1. One third of the Baali believe they're in Call of Cthulhu and doing horrifying infant sacrifices keeps Cthulhu asleep.<br /> <br /> 2. One third of the Baali believe they're in Call of Cthulhu and doing horrifying infant sacrifices will wake Cthulhu up.<br /> <br /> 3. One third of the Baali believe they're in KULT and making horrifying infant sacrifices will make them rich.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-28T21:17:20-07:00","id":1415932,"title":"","content":"I found the greatest explanation of the Anarchs was in one of my earliest games by a much better player than me.<br /> <br /> Anarch NPC: &quot;The problem is you think the Anarchs vs. the Camarilla is Star Wars. No, it's the Godfather. Why do we fight the Camarilla? Because they got the shit like land, blood, and money we want. They'll kill us to keep us from it. We'll kill them to get it.&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 09-29-2020, 12:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-29T00:17:35-07:00","id":1415947,"title":"","content":"I initially approach the Sabbat from a meta perspective. What's their purpose in the game? I think it's to serve as the home for the evil vampires in pop culture depictions pre-Anne Rice. They're the Satan worshipping vampires from Hammer Horror; Kurt Barlow causing the entire town of Salem's Lot to become vampires; the heartless vampires who turn a variety of victims when they appear and torment their friends and family like in Count Yorga. But they do it without the traditional cape and evening wear that had been cliche since Bela Lugosi. They're the boogey men. But they're updated for the modern age like the Camarilla was.<br /> <br /> They originally lost to the Camarilla because they're already obsolete, but they can thrive when society becomes decadent.<br /> <br /> As an ST, I think they're a great tool. I liked early edition Sabbat which introduced the various Paths of Enlightenment (though I think the Revised rewrites are better) and depicted the sect divided by a variety of means (the various Paths of Enlightenment; Loyalists versus Centralizers; Inquisition versus Infernalists; various clan feuds (Panders, Tremere AT, Tzimisce, etc.); and even Nomadic packs versus Founded Covens. I found them very compelling.<br /> <br /> I didn't like the Revised metaplot which tossed all of that aside just so there could be a Crusade and the introduction of even more bloodlines just because. It became less interesting, and I didn't find the handwave explanations compelling. But there were some good ideas even in all this dreck.<br /> <br /> I like the Sabbat as a glorious mess because it gives me lots of tools as an ST, and if I wanted, I could run very different Sabbat games depending on what elements I wanted to focus on the local city. I could have fairly high humanity (for Sabbat) Loyalist Nomad packs; murderous founded covens ruling the ruins of Detroit; or devotees of the Path of Night terrifying mortals, but never quite killing them because that'd miss the point.<br /> <br /> I never ran Sabbat games, but as the occasional NPCs in my chronicles, they really caused a lot of problems and introduced confusion to the PCs because they were never consistent. And uncertainty produces fear.<br /> <br /> I like that within the Sabbat, the various factions prevent unity - at least in its original depiction. For every Lasombra ultra-conservative wanting a centralized structure and soldiers that obey orders without question; there's a charismatic ductus of a Nomad Loyalist pack undermining that archbishop's authority. Whatever is true, is only true locally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-29T06:41:15-07:00","id":1415963,"title":"","content":"<b>What Ever Happened to the Red Question</b><br /> <br /> Adeyemi returns with a profile of the Red Question, the collection of Anarch hackers who targeted Camarilla vampires. The name of Red Question as a group itself is a reference to what they hoped to be an armor piercing question, asking young Camarilla vampires why they believed in and obeyed Camarilla elders.<br /> <br /> Adeyemi discusses some of the things the Red Question did (including revealing secrets and gutting elder finances) but also spends a lot of time on the titular question; where did they go and what happened to them?<br /> <br /> This is a section that disappoints me on a meta level, or out of character level. It is not necessarily badly written but it should have been thought through better. Every section of the book should provide fodder for games and opportunities for players. Saying the Red Question, an Anarch vampire version of something like Anonymous, is simply gone ends too many game possibilities (it is suggested they were wiped out by the SI). <a href=\"https://www.theatlantic.com/technology/archive/2020/08/hacker-group-anonymous-returns/615058/\" target=\"_blank\">Anonymous has returned, and so of course can the Red Question</a> \u2013 but that is beyond the scope of this section.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-29T07:18:46-07:00","id":1415969,"title":"","content":"<b>Revelations of the Dark Mother</b><br /> <br /> This is a good section in the book, as it provides insights into the beliefs and methods of the cults of Lilith, the Bahari. The short version is pain, in all its forms, is central to what they believe and how they operate. This section of the book includes statements from three vampires, including Agata \u201cOutstar\u201d Starek and Rachel Dolium, who compiled the \u201cRevelations of the Dark Mother\u201d book. The Bahari are usually vampires so it is terrifying, if you are paying attention.<br /> <br /> Pain is a teacher, and arguably everything we learn is related to pain on some level. Maybe it is physical pain (don\u2019t stick your hand in a fire) or maybe it is social pain (you should be embarrassed by the \u201cF\u201d you got on the test), but pain plays a role in learning, and learning plays a role in growth, development, and evolution. The relative power of vampires means it is harder for them to experience pain, so it is arguably harder for them to grow, develop, and evolve. Likewise, pain can teach empathy \u2013 so the same relative power of vampires means it is hard for them to experience empathy.<br /> <br /> On a related note I doubt Tzimisce (a clan almost synonymous with the infliction of pain) are often members of the Bahari \u2013 pain is for other creatures, not for the Tzimisce. It\u2019s been a thousand years and the Fiends are still pretty salty about the Tremere inflicting pain on them, after all.<br /> <br /> It is also interesting to compare the Bahari with the Church of Caine. The Bahari are considered a group of cults, while the Church of Caine gets to call itself a church. The term \u201cchurch\u201d carries social clout and respect, while the term \u201ccult\u201d conjures suspicious and a lack of respectability. As described in the texts, the Church of Caine is a structured organization providing rhetoric to justify its members\u2019 behavior and structural methodology. By comparison, the Bahari have little formal structure and little formal rhetoric. The Bahari would be uncomfortable to be a member of while the Church of Caine would be a comfortable one to be a member of \u2013 and what does comfort teach?<br /> <br /> In the <i>Chicago Folio</i> members of the Cult of Lilith catch an interloper and potential spy and saboteur. They stake him, step him up in front of a mirror and then skin him \u2013 noting he gets to watch as his skin gradually grows back. If they had been really angry with him they would have set him up in front of a wide-screen TV and made him watch the 2015 Fantastic Four movie.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-29T12:43:59-07:00","id":1416020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1415969#post1415969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On a related note I doubt Tzimisce (a clan almost synonymous with the infliction of pain) are often members of the Bahari \u2013 pain is for other creatures, not for the Tzimisce. It\u2019s been a thousand years and the Fiends are still pretty salty about the Tremere inflicting pain on them, after all.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Bahari do inflict pain on others, that's part of their duty<br /> <br /> and contrary to popular belief, while they do welcome pain, they are not expected to enjoy it,<br /> to feel bad, salty, bitter about it is part of the process (Lilith is still salty about what Caine did to her),<br /> pain is not pleasure, it's not entertainment, it's a teacher,<br /> and the Tzimisce have learned their lesson well<br /> <br /> the Tzimisce would actually be the most suited clan for the path of lilith if it weren't for the bahari's rejection of wealth and temporal power","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-29T15:27:31-07:00","id":1416035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1415963#post1415963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>What Ever Happened to the Red Question</b><br /> <br /> Adeyemi returns with a profile of the Red Question, the collection of Anarch hackers who targeted Camarilla vampires. The name of Red Question as a group itself is a reference to what they hoped to be an armor piercing question, asking young Camarilla vampires why they believed in and obeyed Camarilla elders.<br /> <br /> Adeyemi discusses some of the things the Red Question did (including revealing secrets and gutting elder finances) but also spends a lot of time on the titular question; where did they go and what happened to them?<br /> <br /> This is a section that disappoints me on a meta level, or out of character level. It is not necessarily badly written but it should have been thought through better. Every section of the book should provide fodder for games and opportunities for players. Saying the Red Question, an Anarch vampire version of something like Anonymous, is simply gone ends too many game possibilities (it is suggested they were wiped out by the SI). <a href=\"https://www.theatlantic.com/technology/archive/2020/08/hacker-group-anonymous-returns/615058/\" target=\"_blank\">Anonymous has returned, and so of course can the Red Question</a> \u2013 but that is beyond the scope of this section.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, this is one of the most frustrating entries in the book for me.<br /> <br /> I feel like the Red Question was somewhat overplayed in ANARCHS UNBOUND as the hot new thing in the Anarchs. They supposedly caused the 2008 Financial Crash and that may have wiped out Horatio Ballard's personal finances but we all know that the real victims of that weren't the billionaires due to the bailouts.<br /> <br /> This chapter actually feels a bit like an &quot;apology&quot; for the Red Question and I honestly wonder why they bothered. The Red Question wasn't a BAD idea. We've had hacker Brujah since Bobby Weatherbottom and they're not a bad concept. They may not be all that relevant to Anarchs in the more international movement (which this section notes) but they still fit into the larger pattern.<br /> <br /> I also feel like that if they wanted to get rid of the Red Question they could have come up with a number of interesting ways to do it. Have the Second Inquisition crack down on them, have them taken out by the Virtual Adepts or Glass Walkers [Which would be a nice nod], have them all sell out before being hired by the Camarilla, or just have them break up. Its not like Anonymous vanished as you say.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-29T18:41:57-07:00","id":1416048,"title":"","content":"Also, PCs can be a part of the Red Question without too much trouble, so dropping it limits play options.<br /> <br /> Hrm. I'll make a lore sheet for it tomorrow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-29T23:51:49-07:00","id":1416063,"title":"","content":"Wait Anonymous still exists, like they are part of the Geroge Floyd protests.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-30T00:09:06-07:00","id":1416066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1416063#post1416063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait Anonymous still exists, like they are part of the Geroge Floyd protests.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well... A twitter account named &quot;Anonymous&quot; has appeared this year. But the original Anonymous has infamously been taken over by the FBI and used for a number of cyberattacks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-30T00:17:32-07:00","id":1416069,"title":"","content":"a financial crash is good for vampires though?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-30T00:26:59-07:00","id":1416070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1416069#post1416069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">a financial crash is good for vampires though?</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe a financial crash is terrible for vampires. Which is why the Red Question (supposedly) triggered it in order to hurt (other) vampires. However, even when the book first came out, it strikes me that it was the result of &quot;natural&quot; market forces (i.e. unchecked greed and stupidity) and the Red Question just took credit for it. Unless you were Alan Sovereign or watched THE BIG SHORT movie, then the vast majority of Ventrue would probably believe them. Very few Elder vampires know what is or is not possible with modern technology.<br /> <br /> Even then, I don't think it's a very good example for Anarch &quot;resistance&quot; because in real life, a huge amount of ordinary people lost their homes while the mega-rich were bailed out by the government in order to return the economy to normal. If anything, it would be the Ventrue showing why they're at the top of the predator list because they managed to survive what the rest of the country were rocked by.<br /> <br /> Or, to quote Sir Terry Pratchett (RIP), &quot;When banks collapse, it is rarely bankers who starve.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1416066#post1416066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well... A twitter account named &quot;Anonymous&quot; has appeared this year. But the original Anonymous has infamously been taken over by the FBI and used for a number of cyberattacks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Anonymous never really existed as an organized group, though, which is kind of the point. It was just the name under which a bunch of hackers played around with assholes (and backed down when the cartels started threatening to kill random people). Anyone could claim membership because it wasn't meant to be a traditional organization but a cover for any hacker who wanted to use it.<br /> <br /> Fun fact: Bobby Weatherbottom was/is a member. It's possible that he was the ONLY member in fact and could have been behind all of it. He might have stopped because putting his girlfriend into a coma to drink from constantly is occupying his thoughts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 09-30-2020, 03:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-30T00:37:45-07:00","id":1416071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1416070#post1416070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anonymous never really existed as an organized group, though, which is kind of the point. It was just the name under which a bunch of hackers played around with assholes (and backed down when the cartels started threatening to kill random people). Anyone could claim membership because it wasn't meant to be a traditional organization but a cover for any hacker who wanted to use it.</div> </div> </div> </div>While anyone could claim membership, there were distinct hacker groups within anonymous that executed actual organized cyberattacks and committed cybercrimes, instead of just walking around with the Guy Fawkes masks and posting on 4chan. Because weirdly enough, it turned out you need planning and leadership and organization for this sort of thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-30T01:19:31-07:00","id":1416076,"title":"","content":"But the red question had technomagic and were distributing it among the anarchs... Maybe house ipssimus or whatever got em... <br /> Rites of the blood was a good book and it's a shame V5 has undone it. <br /> <br /> <br /> Anyhow, All vampires fundamentally benefit from 'hard times' <br /> <br /> A huge wealth gap is great for them. The poor being in the desperate shitter makes them easier to feed from; The more people in the gutter, the more people driven to commiting crimes, more people walled off in their homes afraid of crime. The more people distrust others, blame other races for their issues, and don't speak to police (who've been coming down on them of late) the easier it is for vampires to feed without getting caught. Vampires themselves have money, they can laugh off a mugging, but they can't laugh off a clean orderly society where the slightest infraction is taken seriously. They need a place where their activities are unnoticed and everyone has bigger problems on their plate. <br /> <br /> Causing economic hard times is good for Camarilla, Sabbat the independents and anarchs alike. The only problem with hard times is that it becomes a little easier for vampires to build up power and criminal elements and send them at eachother; it actually benefits the young a little bit more than the old.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-30T01:35:39-07:00","id":1416080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1416066#post1416066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well... A twitter account named &amp;quot;Anonymous&amp;quot; has appeared this year. But the original Anonymous has infamously been taken over by the FBI and used for a number of cyberattacks.</div> </div> </div> </div> really? How did people discover this fact?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-30T01:36:34-07:00","id":1416081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1416076#post1416076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Causing economic hard times is good for Camarilla, Sabbat the independents and anarchs alike. The only problem with hard times is that it becomes a little easier for vampires to build up power and criminal elements and send them at eachother; it actually benefits the young a little bit more than the old.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the argument of the Camarilla in Revised. That they make cities nastier, uglier, and poorer.<br /> <br /> However, Anarchs live among the people and often times are hit with the exact same problems that their fellow poor people are. Anarchs can live in a dumpster as long as it's light proof but it's not a pleasant experience, even if you're a Nosferatu.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-30T02:01:34-07:00","id":1416084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1416081#post1416081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> However, Anarchs live among the people and often times are hit with the exact same problems that their fellow poor people are. Anarchs can live in a dumpster as long as it's light proof but it's not a pleasant experience, even if you're a Nosferatu.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bullshit. Anarchs are young, they don't get day jobs, but they can ghoul who they like, network with other anarchs, and their basic needs can be summed up with a place to stay; They don't need to buy groceries, get insurance, or pay for suprise medical bills. They need a safe place to sleep and good hunting grounds, and that is all. Just ghoul someone nice and mooch of them, or get an older vampire to sugar daddy for them. Whatever, the point being they're not the fucking 'working man' because they don't fucking <i>work</i>. <br /> <br /> But either way, for anarchs, what's better: To have the surroundings a shitter so that they have plenty of oppertunities to safely feed and perhaps build up a criminal power base without too much trouble, or to have their surroundings nice and clean so that they have to literally go an extra mile and then some to poach on another kindred's territory every time they want to feed? No drunks, no homeless, no junkies, a fast response time should they ever break into a house or assault someone? A high chance to appear on the news in a city where 90% of crime is reported and taken very seriously? <br /> <br /> <br /> Yeah, nah; Anarchs benefit from the city going to shit, far moreso than camarilla vampires. Camarilla vampires are at least going to own a lot of good stuff so they aren't going to need to do some street hunting, and as an elder centric sect they have more leeway in getting away with riskier kinds of hunting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-30T02:09:44-07:00","id":1416085,"title":"","content":"The sales pitch that Anarchs get Dominate and Presence and then don't abuse it because of their, uhhhh, superior moral fibre I guess, rings false to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-30T05:31:54-07:00","id":1416090,"title":"","content":"The Camarilla is evil. The Anarchs are also evil.<br /> <br /> Does anyone have thoughts on the Dark Mother section?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-30T11:01:12-07:00","id":1416134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1416084#post1416084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Bullshit. Anarchs are young, they don't get day jobs, but they can ghoul who they like, network with other anarchs, and their basic needs can be summed up with a place to stay; They don't need to buy groceries, get insurance, or pay for suprise medical bills. They need a safe place to sleep and good hunting grounds, and that is all. Just ghoul someone nice and mooch of them, or get an older vampire to sugar daddy for them. Whatever, the point being they're not the fucking 'working man' because they don't fucking <i>work</i>.<br /> <br /> But either way, for anarchs, what's better: To have the surroundings a shitter so that they have plenty of oppertunities to safely feed and perhaps build up a criminal power base without too much trouble, or to have their surroundings nice and clean so that they have to literally go an extra mile and then some to poach on another kindred's territory every time they want to feed? No drunks, no homeless, no junkies, a fast response time should they ever break into a house or assault someone? A high chance to appear on the news in a city where 90% of crime is reported and taken very seriously?<br /> <br /> Yeah, nah; Anarchs benefit from the city going to shit, far moreso than camarilla vampires. Camarilla vampires are at least going to own a lot of good stuff so they aren't going to need to do some street hunting, and as an elder centric sect they have more leeway in getting away with riskier kinds of hunting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Incorrect because you're running into the problem of assuming that vampires are going to be all into the &quot;snatch and grab&quot; predator type. The assumption that Anarchs are going to want to grab random people off the street and drain them. Plenty of Anarchs are going to be social drinkers who feed on herds they have cultivated and you don't want your herds to be subject to drug abuse [unless you are feeling in the mood], homelessness, sickness, or other thing. The Camarilla loves making sure there's lots of unguarded mortals ready and willing for draining but the Anarchs do tend to keep a closer relationship to their food.<br /> <br /> They want the same level of clubs, blood banks, and so on that will benefit them.<br /> <br /> Alleycats benefit from city degredation but what about Baggers, Sirens, Consensualists, Farmers, and more?<br /> <br /> Just saying.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1416090#post1416090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Camarilla is evil. The Anarchs are also evil.<br /> <br /> Does anyone have thoughts on the Dark Mother section?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry for the digression.<br /> <br /> Honestly, as much as I like the Church of Caine section, I'm not sure why either of them are inside THE ANARCH book because unless there's a major cult to both of them among the Anarchs, I don't know what they have to do with the Movement. I could buy a lot of Anarchs embracing (haha) Lilith worship because of the perception of freedom and rebellion but that actually got analyzed better in CULTS OF THE BLOOD GODS.<br /> <br /> I think both sections would have benefited from explaining how the Anarchs feel about the Church of Caine and Bahari more than just presenting them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-30T11:52:52-07:00","id":1416147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1416134#post1416134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, as much as I like the Church of Caine section, I'm not sure why either of them are inside THE ANARCH book because unless there's a major cult to both of them among the Anarchs, I don't know what they have to do with the Movement. I could buy a lot of Anarchs embracing (haha) Lilith worship because of the perception of freedom and rebellion but that actually got analyzed better in CULTS OF THE BLOOD GODS.<br /> <br /> I think both sections would have benefited from explaining how the Anarchs feel about the Church of Caine and Bahari more than just presenting them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't read the book, but I agree with you. Things like religious movements likely cross sects unless there are things very specific in their details that explain why it is located in that one sect. Is it something in its appeal? Is it somehow centrally controlled with its leaders in that sect (this explains many Sabbat spiritualism, and traditionally the Typhonist cult among Setites)? Something in its history?<br /> <br /> I can see Anarchs being adherents. But I can see the same thing for Camarilla loyalists, Autarchs, and other groups. This is much more of an individual decision for things separate from political sect adherents.<br /> <br /> I do see the Bahari as always being an underground movement because it is &quot;heretical&quot;. So the Bahari might thrive or spread more among Anarchs because they lack any central means to suppress it. But if the Camarilla has Gehenna Cults then certainly there would have secret Bahari cells as well.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-30T12:11:37-07:00","id":1416149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1416134#post1416134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Incorrect because you're running into the problem of assuming that vampires are going to be all into the &quot;snatch and grab&quot; predator type.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wrong<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> . Plenty of Anarchs are going to be social drinkers who feed on herds they have cultivated </div> </div> </div>And it's safer to cultivate herds in an environment where people don't ask or tell.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and you don't want your herds to be subject to drug abuse [unless you are feeling in the mood], homelessness, sickness, or other thing. </div> </div> </div>Most sicknesses do not effect the blood. Homelessness does not effect the blood. Drugs have very mild effects on the kindred. Also, like, i'm not saying we should replace all the good people with junkies, just that we should make more people available, and in doing so we increase the amount of junkies.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Camarilla loves making sure there's lots of unguarded mortals ready and willing for draining but the Anarchs do tend to keep a closer relationship to their food. </div> </div> </div>This sounds like an in-universe opinion a character has rather than something that's actually true<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They want the same level of clubs, blood banks, and so on that will benefit them. </div> </div> </div>You can have the city go to shit and still have clubs, blood banks and... did you use 'so on' because that's all you could think of? I used to live above a club district, it attracts the scum who yell past midnight and get far to melodramatic below my window. Clubs and shitty areas go hand-in-hand, and blood banks don't suffer when there's people who need the money.<br /> <br /> The Vampire ideal is a city with both extreme poverty and extreme wealth and a small middle-class (it says so in <i>Midnight Seige, </i>an excellent book)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Alleycats benefit from city degredation but what about Baggers, Sirens, Consensualists, Farmers, and more?<br /> <br /> . </div> </div> </div>Sandmen benefit immensely.<br /> Cassanovas are not really effected. Well, if people drink more, that's gonna be helpful amrite?<br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Consensualists benefit from a run-down population that are going to be more accepting of consensualist bullshit when they've got more going on in their lives. Think how it's easy to pull people towards religion when times are tough. </span></span></span><br /> It doesn't effect farmers at all, except maybe if the city is a difficult hunting ground more people are going to compete/poach with farmers.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> But also you gotta remember that V5 hit itself with a hammer when it did the whole predator types thing; They're just preferences, they shouldn't sum up your character's every meal. Nobody should be a full-time alleycat, it's just too much of a problem. Vampires are more opportunistic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-30T13:50:57-07:00","id":1416157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1416081#post1416081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is the argument of the Camarilla in Revised. That they make cities nastier, uglier, and poorer.<br /> <br /> However, Anarchs live among the people and often times are hit with the exact same problems that their fellow poor people are. Anarchs can live in a dumpster as long as it's light proof but it's not a pleasant experience, even if you're a Nosferatu.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait why do Anarch owned cities tend to go to shit? I mean the Camarilla loves corruption in basically everything, so they can cover up bloodless corpses and an epidemic of Anemia","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-30T13:56:19-07:00","id":1416158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1416157#post1416157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wait why do Anarch owned cities tend to go to shit? I mean the Camarilla loves corruption in basically everything, so they can cover up bloodless corpses and an epidemic of Anemia</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I don't think we have enough examples to go by. The only one we know they ruled for almost a century is Los Angeles.<br /> <br /> The others include Paris during the Revolution where they degenerated into infighting and lost it to Francois Villon again....and the Soviet Union.<br /> <br /> Where the Anarchs were either along for the ride or were authoritarian communists 1000x worse than the Camarilla feudalists.<br /> <br /> Which isn't to say they WERN'T Anarchs, it's just that Anarchs can rapidly go the opposite direction of freedom. See the Sabbat for another example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-30T15:00:22-07:00","id":1416166,"title":"","content":"The Anarchs want more freedom for vampires<br /> <br /> Which means more oppression for humans.<br /> <br /> There was some quote i heard about the ancient greeks which comes to mind, something like &quot;Never is a man more free than in Sparta, and never is a slave more a slave than in Sparta'<br /> <br /> <br /> The more opressed the people at the bottom are the more freedom the ruling class have, and Vampires by their very nature are ruling class. Some more than others, but the blood bond isn't an innate gift for no reason.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 09-30-2020, 06:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-30T15:26:33-07:00","id":1416168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1416166#post1416166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Anarchs want more freedom for vampires<br /> <br /> Which means more oppression for humans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or they want freedom for humans.<br /> <br /> Or they want freedom for both.<br /> <br /> Maldavis and Gordon Keaton are both Anarchs.<br /> <br /> Even in this book, we have Agata Starek who is a psychotic diablerist terrorist alongside Rudi who is a champion of minorities and the oppressed among Kine.<br /> <br /> Rudi uses his powers to fight against THE MAN for Kine too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-30T15:37:08-07:00","id":1416170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1416168#post1416168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or they want freedom for humans.<br /> <br /> Or they want freedom for both.<br /> <br /> Maldavis and Gordon Keaton are both Anarchs.<br /> <br /> Even in this book, we have Agata Starek who is a psychotic diablerist terrorist alongside Rudi who is a champion of minorities and the oppressed among Kine.<br /> <br /> Rudi uses his powers to fight against THE MAN for Kine too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Clearly he's an idiot and you're using outliers or liars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-30T15:42:58-07:00","id":1416174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1416170#post1416170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Clearly he's an idiot and you're using outliers or liars.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just one of the Signature characters of the setting?<br /> <br /> Maldavis was active in Civil Rights<br /> <br /> Anita Wainwright is involved in Black Rights<br /> <br /> Gengis is an organizer of Antifa<br /> <br /> Annabelle is heavily involved in community activism<br /> <br /> Rudi is involved in the plight of Syrian refugees and homosexuals in Europe.<br /> <br /> Jenna Cross is a maybe because she's fighting for the rights of Thin Bloods and they're ghouls+.<br /> <br /> I mean, Brujah have ALWAYS been involved in the fight for the rights of mortals.<br /> <br /> I mean, they MAKE THINGS WORSE but that's not deliberate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 09-30-2020, 06:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-30T19:11:18-07:00","id":1416198,"title":"","content":"The Anarchs are everything the Camarilla is not - and that is how the Camarilla defines them, rather than how the Anarchs define themselves. Given that, it is interesting that <i>both </i>the Church of Caine and the Lilith cult's are considered Anarch. The Bahari, with their rejection of social norms and the patriarchy, would not be included in the Camarilla so they are Anarch by definition. And the Anarchs themselves are too divided for enough of those opposed to the Bahari to really do anything about the Lilins, because the rest don't care or are preoccupied by their own affairs or support that cult on some level. The odder inclusion among the Anarchs, or possibly the odder exclusion by the Camarilla, is the Church of Caine. Maybe too many Camarilla elders hold grudges from when it was an issue during the Dark Ages. Maybe the elder worshiping cults inside the Camarilla these days are worried about competition.<br /> <br /> In any case, I've no issue with both the Church of Caine and the Bahari as part of the Anarchs. The Anarchs are so unstructured almost anything could credibly be said to be Anarch, so long as it is not Camarilla. Also, the Church of Caine and the Bahari are polar opposites and so will appeal to different personality types.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-01T11:25:06-07:00","id":1416311,"title":"","content":"<b>Luzern Kommune / Lucerne Commune</b><br /> <br /> This section is set in Lucerne, Switzerland. A local vampire is pitching the Castle for vampires new to the area, like a salesman pitching a timeshare who is really itching for a commission. The \u201ccastle\u201d is a former sanatorium, or an establishment for the medical treatment of people who are convalescing or have a chronic illness, near the city of Lucerne.<br /> <br /> As stated (repeatedly) before, the anarchs are defined as everything the Camarilla is not. And in this case that include a semi-libiterian set up in Lucerne which does not acknowledge the superiority of the Camarilla \u2013 but which also does not give a fig about the struggles of the Anarch Free State or the (former) Soviet Brujah. They are doing their own thing and everyone else can piss off\u2026 unless you are here looking to invest in capital. In that case, come on inI<br /> <br /> The film \u201cCure for Wellness\u201d came out in 2016, or two years before the release of this book. So it might have influenced the selection of a sanatorium as the place a bunch of evil immortals call home.<br /> <br /> A substantial investment is required before vampires may join the Commune. L\u00e9onie Langenstein narrates the section and he is pitching the Lucerne Commune so hard it becomes slightly funny. He does everything but take his guests to the gift shop.<br /> <br /> There is also a bit of Rapture, the setting for the 2007 game BioShock, to the idea of the Lucerne Commune. Whatever else may be said of Andrew Ryan, he would have never abided dwelling in the Camarilla (or the Sabbat for that matter) and judged anyone who did to be a slave.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-01T11:39:37-07:00","id":1416316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1416311#post1416311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Luzern Kommune / Lucerne Commune</b><br /> <br /> This section is set in Lucerne, Switzerland. A local vampire is pitching the Castle for vampires new to the area, like a salesman pitching a timeshare who is really itching for a commission. The \u201ccastle\u201d is a former sanatorium, or an establishment for the medical treatment of people who are convalescing or have a chronic illness, near the city of Lucerne.<br /> <br /> As stated (repeatedly) before, the anarchs are defined as everything the Camarilla is not. And in this case that include a semi-libiterian set up in Lucerne which does not acknowledge the superiority of the Camarilla \u2013 but which also does not give a fig about the struggles of the Anarch Free State or the (former) Soviet Brujah. They are doing their own thing and everyone else can piss off\u2026 unless you are here looking to invest in capital. In that case, come on inI<br /> <br /> The film \u201cCure for Wellness\u201d came out in 2016, or two years before the release of this book. So it might have influenced the selection of a sanatorium as the place a bunch of evil immortals call home.<br /> <br /> A substantial investment is required before vampires may join the Commune. L\u00e9onie Langenstein narrates the section and he is pitching the Lucerne Commune so hard it becomes slightly funny. He does everything but take his guests to the gift shop.<br /> <br /> There is also a bit of Rapture, the setting for the 2007 game BioShock, to the idea of the Lucerne Commune. Whatever else may be said of Andrew Ryan, he would have never abided dwelling in the Camarilla (or the Sabbat for that matter) and judged anyone who did to be a slave.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps it's because I'm from Kentucky but I saw this as a very transparent con. In Kentucky, we have a lot of doomsday preppers and one of the more successful, albeit niche, cons that we have people who market luxury survival shelters. Basically, it comes with the following view:<br /> <br /> Con Man: You afraid of black people/disease/nuclear war/Democrats, then when the fall of society comes, here's our luxury exclusive survival shelter that will allow you to ride out the apocalypse in luxury until society can be rebuilt. You have to reserve your ticket today for 100,000 dollars, though. There's only room for 10 families here.<br /> <br /> Rich White Dude: Are you sure it's safe?<br /> <br /> Con Man: Of course! *gives tour*<br /> <br /> Rich White Dude: This is amazing! *gives money and leaves*<br /> <br /> Con Man: Okay, guys, let's leave this abandoned basement we've decorated like a luxury apartment with empty cardboard boxes and soap cans.<br /> <br /> Henchman: How many suckers did we fool into buying into it?<br /> <br /> Con Man: 30.<br /> <br /> Presumably, the guys selling this investment intends to bilk a bunch of bunch of rich vampires of their fortune then leave them to fight it out with the other people who sold the place.<br /> <br /> I honestly think that you could pull this on Camarilla Elders to ride out Gehenna but the problem there is that they can just PRESENCE or DOMINATE you into telling the truth. They are very rich but very paranoid about being played for fools. I also think Marcus Vitel DID set up his own bunker with presumably its own underground city.<br /> <br /> Oddly, the audiobook recently released for V:TM *DID* have something similar to this with a farm of Anarchs raising humans in luxury until they're slaughtered at age 30 as an ethical alternative to just hunting them normally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 10-01-2020, 02:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-01T12:58:57-07:00","id":1416324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1416316#post1416316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I honestly think that you could pull this on Camarilla Elders to ride out Gehenna but the problem there is that they can just PRESENCE or DOMINATE you into telling the truth. They are very rich but very paranoid about being played for fools. I also think Marcus Vitel DID set up his own bunker with presumably its own underground city.</div> </div> </div> </div>just to make sure,<br /> in V5, thought it was no longer possible to use Dominate to acquire information,<br /> a command like &quot;tell the truth&quot; would just result in the victim responding by saying: &quot;the truth&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-01T13:41:42-07:00","id":1416331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1416316#post1416316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps it's because I'm from Kentucky but I saw this as a very transparent con. In Kentucky, we have a lot of doomsday preppers and one of the more successful, albeit niche, cons that we have people who market luxury survival shelters. Basically, it comes with the following view:</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://risingsbunkers.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Honest to God, people who make a sell those things are located about a mile from my house</a>.<br /> <br /> In any case, either version can work for a game. It's all a vampire (and not under water) City of Rapture and the PCs are involved when everything goes to hell. Or it is all a massive con job and the PCs are involved when everything goes to hell.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-01T13:43:22-07:00","id":1416333,"title":"","content":"Next up is Theo Bell and some Rudi.<br /> <br /> Which is very good.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1416324#post1416324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> just to make sure,<br /> in V5, thought it was no longer possible to use Dominate to acquire information,<br /> a command like &quot;tell the truth&quot; would just result in the victim responding by saying: &quot;the truth&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on the Dominate level I suppose. Mesmerize and, &quot;Interrogate&quot; are probably different powers but I imagine some Elders would have both.<br /> <br /> Mind you, I have stated I don't like how Elder powers have been nerfed in V5 so I admit that this is a subject I'm not very familiarized with.<br /> <br /> Humanity, Hunger, Touchstones, Rouse checks, all good.<br /> <br /> Nerfing elders? No.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 10-01-2020, 04:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-01T14:29:27-07:00","id":1416345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps