}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-02T11:58:13-07:00","id":1416502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1416345#post1416345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> there's an &quot;Interrogate&quot; power in v5?</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://www.meme-arsenal.com/memes/faf02daa0f147f83ff19645fa2ed0e67.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> &quot;Where's the vitae Lebowski?!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-02T13:14:27-07:00","id":1416517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1416350#post1416350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm convinced CTphipps doesn't actually play and just sits around in forums all day</div> </div> </div> </div>that would be me actually,<br /> haven't played in ages, just sitting around in forums all day chewing sleeping pills<br /> <br /> that's why I'm grateful for these threads offering feedback on real experience with the game and different perspectives<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1416502#post1416502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;Where's the vitae Lebowski?!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>my deadass toreador doesn't have potence,<br /> and my deadass ravnos...well, ravnos don't exist anymore, not that they would have potence if they did<br /> <br /> ...guess it's time to switch to Lasombra<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-02T17:52:26-07:00","id":1416557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1416501#post1416501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>I Believe in Theo Bell / Fuck Theo Bell</b><br /> Mr. Salvador Garcia and Madam Agata Sterek engage in a lucid conversation about one Mr. Theodor Bell, specifically engaging in a meaningful dialogue about their meaning when they use the phrase \u201cFuck Theo Bell.\u201d<br /> <br /> Garcia, at best doesn\u2019t like, Bell, or how a fan club has formed around the notoriety of the former Archon. He also asserts Bell, relative to most Anarchs and Garcia himself, was embraced into a lot of privilege and advantages. Lastly, Garcia points out Bell is only lately come to join the Anarch cause.<br /> <br /> Starek says she think Bell is hot and says she wants to bone him \u2013 but this is Starek we are talking about, and there is a good chance she says this just to provoke a reaction from Garcia.<br /> This is not a section which offers a lot of adventure possibilities, but it does provide some insight into the mind set of some Anarchs, which in turn provides some insight into how they operate.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am going to say this short little chapter, more like a vignette really, is probably my favorite part of the entire book. Part of this is just the nostalgia factor because I absolutely love Theo Bell. I think he's basically just Wesley Snipe's Blade with a thin coat of paint and working for the vampires instead of against them but that doesn't mean he's not awesome.<br /> <br /> I think this actually does a very good job of explaining a lot about the Anarchs and criticizing them at once. Their handling of Theo Bell and his &quot;defection&quot; is something that I was really fascinated by.<br /> <br /> Salvador, the Ancilla verging on Elder, is nursing decades-long grudges against Theo Bell who has probably personally murdered friends is someone who has no particular interest in welcoming him into the Movement. He cites the fact Theo Bell is a firm believer in the Traditions and just hates the corruption of the Camarilla versus hating the system itself. He also notes that Theo Bell may have lived a hellacious existence as a mortal but he became part of the ruling elite (while having a slave-owning master). He also cites that Theo Bell hasn't even been consistently anti-slavery but had a Darwinist view of his abolitionism.<br /> <br /> All of Salvador's arguments have a ring of truth to them but they're also very obviously motivated by the fact that he's been replaced as the Golden Boy of the AnarchsTM. Salvador killed the Prince of Los Angeles and probably some lesser cities' princes according to The Anarch Cookbook but none of that has the same impact as killing the FOUNDER of the Camarilla. It's a Tyler-level defining event (hehehe).<br /> <br /> Agata is, by contrast, charmed by the MYTHOLOGY of Theo Bell that is only tangentially related to the man himself. The idea of the slave who rises to the heights of the Camarilla, kills its tyrant, and then joins the Anarchs. It's something similar to GLADIATOR and really shows that style over substance is a powerful force in the Anarchs. It doesn't hurt that Theo Bell is a physically attractive and imposing man as she notes.<br /> <br /> I also loved the amusement that Theo Bell would almost certainly kill Agata Starek for being an unrepentant (or even repentant) diablerist but she doesn't care.<br /> <br /> I imagine Theo Bell will do his best to make the Anarchs as Camarilla-like as possible, right until they form their own breakaway sect like he and Jan did in the GEHENNA scenarios.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 10-02-2020, 08:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-02T22:54:24-07:00","id":1416576,"title":"","content":"Random aside, this inspired me to go buy the paperback copies of THE BRUJAH TRILOGY starring Theo Bell. Too bad the Victorian Era Beckett ones are too expensive.<br /> <br /> I tried to make the PDF versions work on Kindle but failed miserably.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-03T19:36:54-07:00","id":1416668,"title":"","content":"<b>Blood of Patriots</b><br /> <br /> This is middle section, in that there are better sections and worse sections.<br /> <br /> Here a vampire pretending to be a perennial student at Harvard is writing the minutes of a meeting with other vampires pretending to be perennial students at the old Ivy League school. Parts of the section have a real bro tone, in that it is one frat boy vampire writing to another frat boy vampire, and ridiculing the second one for getting too wasted at a party. It also has all the pretension of college student fans of Ayn Rand righteously discussing their plans and ethics. Those two tones do not work together very well. The frat boy parts have a tone of dark comedy. The writer might want the Ayn Rand fan club to be funny, but if so it lands with a thud (It\u2019s not offensive, it\u2019s just kind of there).<br /> <br /> That vampires are crawling all over colleges (hunting in college parties and eyeball deep in college groups and social life) is old news, but it is nice to see a reminder here. However, it probably would have been better by just making it about frat boy vampires, or just making it about sophomore level vampire objectivists. Trying to be both undermines the impact.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-04T05:23:01-07:00","id":1416712,"title":"","content":"This, along with the Lucerne section, represents the (overt) ancap side of the Anarch Movement. Even though some readers looked straight to Rudi and decided that his group were what Anarchs, if not V5 kindred in general, were about anyway, this section is essential for the demonstration of the movement's political breadth. <br /> <br /> Maybe similar ideals could have been attributed to the Red Question, but I don't know what their agenda was in V20.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","user":"Spencer from The Hills","date":". 10-04-2020, 08:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-04T10:19:34-07:00","id":1416739,"title":"","content":"Left wing vampires who champion mortal causes are fools who are sabotaging themselves. You are the 0.01%, you survive because you feed on everyone else. it is in your best interests to push mortals to the right, or if you're gonna be a lefty you at least need the regime to be more authoritarian than left. <br /> <br /> Left wing among vampires? Sure, that makes a lot of sense. But for kine? No. <br /> <br /> If you've got a specific issue that plagues you (you're a minority in a racist land) and you think the advantage of that (your tasty ethnic ghetto rack that is firmly yours, not upsetting the cities other cainites) isn't worth the persecution, you might have a good rational to push for a little liberalism. But Rudi is a fucking joke caricature. Only the Camarilla would want to suggest that the Anarchs are 'people like Rudi'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-04T11:57:45-07:00","id":1416746,"title":"","content":"I don't think &quot;Vampire not fully onboard the vampire train&quot; is a viable concept. With the focus on humanity and golconda, tending to mortal issues is valid. A problem I have with the way V5 tackles it is that this is a fairly protagonist-y thing to do. PCs should champion the mortal causes among vampires and challenge the status quo, because PCs are the focal point of the story. Saying &quot;yeah, everyone's already doing it, we've got a Gangrel elder pushing the charge&quot; steals the thunder. Fall into the line, do what the big man Rudi says.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/GNbTvpi.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12892,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","user":"Kammerer","date":". 10-04-2020, 03:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-04T13:21:19-07:00","id":1416753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1416739#post1416739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Left wing vampires who champion mortal causes are fools who are sabotaging themselves. You are the 0.01%, you survive because you feed on everyone else. it is in your best interests to push mortals to the right, or if you're gonna be a lefty you at least need the regime to be more authoritarian than left.<br /> <br /> Left wing among vampires? Sure, that makes a lot of sense. But for kine? No.<br /> <br /> If you've got a specific issue that plagues you (you're a minority in a racist land) and you think the advantage of that (your tasty ethnic ghetto rack that is firmly yours, not upsetting the cities other cainites) isn't worth the persecution, you might have a good rational to push for a little liberalism. But Rudi is a fucking joke caricature. Only the Camarilla would want to suggest that the Anarchs are 'people like Rudi'</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see why vampires have to suddenly only care about their own needs as soon as they get embraced. The paths of previous editions had tenets about helping others or at least shunning sin and even not having &quot;selfish thoughts&quot; was the pinnacle of the Path of Humanity. That doesn't mean they're much good at it or that the majority even want to be, but the aspiration clearly exists for some of them.<br /> I think it's reasonable for kindred on the whole to be intolerant of vampires who try to make the world safer for kine or more aware of their problems, to the point that no <i>institution</i> that does so persists and that many respond to it with a reactionary fervour comparable to McCarthyism, but that doesn't mean that it shouldn't exist at all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1416746#post1416746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think &quot;Vampire not fully onboard the vampire train&quot; is a viable concept. With the focus on humanity and golconda, tending to mortal issues is valid. A problem I have with the way V5 tackles it is that this is a fairly protagonist-y thing to do. PCs should champion the mortal causes among vampires and challenge the status quo, because PCs are the focal point of the story. Saying &quot;yeah, everyone's already doing it, we've got a Gangrel elder pushing the charge&quot; steals the thunder. Fall into the line, do what the big man Rudi says.<br /> [/IMG]</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds far too gamey for my taste, as if the PCs are a different type of vampire to the NPCs. There should be NPCs as good as PCs and PCs as bad as NPCs. Plus having sympathetic NPCs gives the idealistic PCs at least a sliver of hope of accomplishing anything beyond their own domain. Doom is a theme of Werewolf: The Apocalypse and even they have some people, like other werewolves, with common goals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-04T13:24:17-07:00","id":1416754,"title":"","content":"I like my World of Darkness Dark.<br /> <br /> So, Ideally, if my players are going to play 'champions of the people' I'll begin by having NPCs asking them politely to stop, and that they're interfering, and maybe they'll even provide compelling arguments. If players continue, the court turns against them and things will deteriorate from there unless they 'fall in line'.<br /> <br /> The prince begins to send them on less-than-desirable tasks for chump change, With V5 their enemies are taking advantages of resonances that they aren't/can't. Their rivals are getting more resources thanks to both having more allies and having less ethical qualms about the money. Their mentors cut ties. Prestation seems to be biased against them. Hunters seem to be directed towards the players. I'll give the coterie a good mortal friend who exists just to be cut up and sent to the players as hate mail, The prince is pressured to find an excuse to blood hunt or execute the players. (This should actually be quite fun if done well; the players wanted an uphill battle, and having RIGHTEOUS FURY is fun)<br /> <br /> If players are somehow successful in fighting corruption and injustice, it'll bite them in the ass: It's harder to hunt, it's harder to find easy meals, and it's easier to get in trouble with the law, who are now competent and aren't so corruptible. Pretty soon people'll pass drinking laws and other such things the players didn't account for, and the clubs scene deadens. The ghouls they relied on are on the run from the law. Their little movement has snowballed. They can either restore the disorder to make their lives easier, be totally unprepared for a foreign attack, or they can crusade themselves into the next city where their righteousness is needed (their current city likely infiltrated and corrupted behind them)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 10-04-2020, 04:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-04T13:41:49-07:00","id":1416756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1416754#post1416754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like my World of Darkness Dark.<br /> <br /> So, Ideally, if my players are going to play 'champions of the people' I'll begin by having NPCs asking them politely to stop, and that they're interfering, and maybe they'll even provide compelling arguments. If players continue, the court turns against them and things will deteriorate from there unless they 'fall in line'.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I totally agree.<br /> <br /> And these PCs would then be forced to strike back at the Prince, strike back hard, and perhaps organize other like-minded or hard nosed vampires to fight back against the Prince. Some of them would be fellow idealists. Others of them would be people with an ax to grind against the Prince. A few of them would just be people who wanted to cause mayhem for no reason. Others would be seeking power.<br /> <br /> However, this would undoubtedly be...Anarchy.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> Oh wait.<br /> <br /> You just described how the Anarchs function and why.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-04T14:00:58-07:00","id":1416761,"title":"","content":"<b>Anarchs and Charity</b><br /> <br /> Ultimately, I find myself once more disagreeing with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25794_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25794\" data-vbnamecard=\"25794\">MyWifeIsScary</a>. Ironically, it's because we're actually on the same page but use different math to reach the same conclusion. It's not 1+1=3 versus 1+1=2 but 2-2=0 and 0+0=0. Both of us like incredibly dark and unforgiving World of Darknesses. MWIS believes that this is achieved by thinking that the majority of Princes and Anarchs are going to be solely pro-vampire selfish dirtbags who are only focused on their own survival. A lot of vampires are like that in my games, yes. However, no, those guys mean shit in the end. No, the scary ones are the ones who BELIEVE. Those are the really dangerous ones in the World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> This is actually something that comes up in <i>Vampire: The Masquerade: Winter's Teeth</i> if you haven't checked out that awesome comic by Tim Seeley. It's only had two issues out but they've already woven a pretty complicated character arc and discussed how Humanity affects the vampires involved.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/ComicBook/VampireTheMasqueradeVault\" target=\"_blank\">https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.p...asqueradeVault</a><br /> <br /> The primary protagonist of the books is <b>Cecily Bain</b>, a former Anarch turned Camarilla Stooge Brujah. Cecily was an Anarch in the 70s to late 90s fighting against the system. Cecily believes she's &quot;grown up&quot; and that the Anarch cause was stupid. She thinks the only way to survive is to selfishly pursue her own interests at all costs. She only works for herself, her sister (who is now dying of old age), and disdaining any emotional attachments as impediments.<br /> <br /> Cecily is, in a word, fucked.<br /> <br /> Her lack of emotional attachments and causes is seriously screwing with her Humanity. It's also resulting in her lashing out at everyone around her in a way that has made her numerous enemies. She kills another Kindred's Touchstone to show her contempt for caring for mortals and instead of him breaking, he's gained a life goal of destroying her. She's tried to teach her childe that killing &quot;evil&quot; people doesn't help because they have loved ones and it's only made her childe hate her. Her attitude of, &quot;We're parasites, why care?&quot; pisses off everyone.<br /> <br /> Cecily isn't WRONG. Vampires ARE awful but they need a kind of anchor to keep them sane. A self-delusion that they're not purely evil parasites. At least if they're not completely alien monsters like the Sabbat. This is actually baked into the fundamentals of the setting, IMHO.<br /> <br /> 1. Brujah have their causes and every Brujah cares about one cause or another.<br /> 2. Toreador justify their existence by cultivating art and beauty.<br /> 3. Nosferatu have their bands of the homeless, runaways, and lost.<br /> 4. Ventrue build their kingdoms that they feel an obligation to even if the health of Amazon.com comes before its workers or Chicago before its citizens.<br /> 5. Tremere justify their existence by pushing the boundaries of knowledge, science, and magic<br /> 6. Gangrel are the only ones who actially are purley survival focused and live like animals from night to night.<br /> 7. Malkavians? Okay, fuck if I know what motivates the Malkavians, but they DO have a motivation.<br /> <br /> Every vampire needs something to get them through their immortal lives and make them feel.<br /> <br /> However, the trick to make it truly dark is that their attempts to help the cause will almost always make it worse. Michael Corleone wanst to protect his family by getting them out of the Mob life? Well, watch the bodies pile up and the horrors he perpetuates get bigger as he does more evil than his father to go legitimate. Scarface wants to be a big man? Well, watch his sister become addicted to cocaine and her husband get murdered because Tony wants her to be a virginal pure Touchstone for his family image.<br /> <br /> The Banu Haqim are a perfect example of this as they are totally 100% convinced of their righteousness and are among the most alien psychos of all. Ditto the Followers of Set who have reversed good and evil but will passionately die for the cause of selfishness. Vampires will almost always have a cause but they will almost certainly make it worse. Annabelle, Lodin, and other Elders almost certainly have &quot;pet causes&quot; they're involved in (like mobsters and corrupt corporate executives) but these things are salves on the wound of their humanity. It allows them to do worse.<br /> <br /> But don't take my word for it, take the Doctor's.<br /> <br /> <b>The Doctor on Vampire Morality</b><br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/VLZOFZggG4w\" data-code=\"VLZOFZggG4w\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/VLZOFZggG4w/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-04T15:04:17-07:00","id":1416768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1416739#post1416739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Left wing vampires who champion mortal causes are fools who are sabotaging themselves. You are the 0.01%, you survive because you feed on everyone else. it is in your best interests to push mortals to the right, or if you're gonna be a lefty you at least need the regime to be more authoritarian than left.<br /> <br /> Left wing among vampires? Sure, that makes a lot of sense. But for kine? No.<br /> <br /> If you've got a specific issue that plagues you (you're a minority in a racist land) and you think the advantage of that (your tasty ethnic ghetto rack that is firmly yours, not upsetting the cities other cainites) isn't worth the persecution, you might have a good rational to push for a little liberalism. But Rudi is a fucking joke caricature. Only the Camarilla would want to suggest that the Anarchs are 'people like Rudi'</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine most vampires who have pet causes (that promote benefits to Humanity that would in turn hurt vampires in general) quickly turn from being true proponents of those changes, to simply looking at the people advocating their pet causes as being... their pets. So instead of truly wanting those changes that hurt the vampire's long term interests, it's just wanting to protect this small group of humans instead of actually helping them achieve anything. They make sure a select number of human advocates are rewarded financially, given social prestige, kept physically safe, etc. but the larger number of humanity gets nothing.<br /> <br /> There's a concept called &quot;pathological altruism&quot; which showcases how certain attempts to help people actually cause great harm to the people they are trying to benefit. And no matter how much evidence you show these people that they are harming the very people they are trying to help, the pathological altruists refuse to believe it and double down. It goes so much against their self image and humiliate them psychologically to admit they're wrong, that they're incapable of actually helping people. <br /> <br /> And of course, there are any number of con artists and social predators that are more than happy to use rhetoric as a cover for their own crimes.<br /> <br /> Those few vampires that continue on a course that would actually harm vampire society because of their naive beliefs are probably killed by their own side at some point.<br /> <br /> I believe these scenarios would afflict over 99.9% of such vampires. And the very, very few vampires who are truly concerned with justice end up dropping out of vampire society and politics entirely and devote themselves to retaining high Humanity, seeking Golconda, joining the Children of Osiris or following any of the other probably false promises of vampire redemption.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-04T15:10:25-07:00","id":1416770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1416761#post1416761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, the scary ones are the ones who BELIEVE. Those are the really dangerous ones in the World of Darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am currently listening to <i>The Looming Tower </i>as an audio book - it is about the events leading to the 9/11 attacks. The author discusses the concept of takfir, or Islamic concept of one Muslim declaring another Muslim to be apostate, and thus non-Muslim. In normal Muslim tradition this is a power limited to very few and cause for a lot of controversy. However, during the 1990s Islamic extremists took the power for themselves, ignoring traditional Islamic law on the subject and even the letter of the Koran. Takfiri played a roll in the Algerian Civil War of the 1990s, during which Islamic extremists killed 26,000, through combat operations, massacres, bombings and assassinations, alongside 18,000 people, 'disappeared' and presumed killed in secret.<br /> <br /> While I agree that belief is potentially dangerous, in my experience a belief system does not warp people. It is people that warp a belief system, to justify their behavior, to grant legitimacy to all the ugliness already inside them. The takfiri massacres in Algeria represent an inversion of Muslim morality, ethic, and tradition. But they do offer a clear show case of human cruelty given a paper thin justification.<br /> <br /> Vampires are inherently bad people. No matter their stated goals, they will poison whatever they touch. It does not matter much if they ascribed to conservatism, or progressivism, or Catholicism. They will ruin it. They will turn it into a toxic inversion of its purported ideals, morality, ethics, and tradition.<br /> <br /> That is what vampires do. That is what vampires are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-04T15:22:26-07:00","id":1416771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1416768#post1416768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe these scenarios would afflict over 99.9% of such vampires. And the very, very few vampires who are truly concerned with justice end up dropping out of vampire society and politics entirely and devote themselves to retaining high Humanity, seeking Golconda, joining the Children of Osiris or following any of the other probably false promises of vampire redemption.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://static.tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pub/images/paint_3.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Another good example is NIGHT ROAD where we have a couple of example this in practice.<br /> <br /> <b>Pattermuster</b> is a Brujah medical doctor who runs a free Catholic hospital that he does his very best to use to provide as much healthcare he can to the locals of Tuscon, Arizona. This is a lot of people because a lot of people cannot afford healthcare in the United States. Duh. However, Pattermuster's desire to help people also extends to the Thin Bloods and the local Caitiff in the area which he allows to feed at the hospital. The result of the two attempts to &quot;help&quot; have turned the hospital into a shit show as people who would recover from their injuries end up being killed. It becomes even more of a shit show because they can't afford to keep the place open on their current budget and thus one of the vampires (who doesn't want to lose her haven and safe feeding place), takes to using the place for a cover for a massive pill marketing scheme. The pills paying to keep the hospital open and free.<br /> <br /> I swear this is a GLORIOUS example of the Anarchs at work, IMHO.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-04T19:41:57-07:00","id":1416790,"title":"","content":"<b>Rudi\u2019s Army</b><br /> <br /> On a personal level I\u2019m alright with Nazi\u2019s appearing in an RPG for the same reason I\u2019m alright with zombies and evil cultists appearing in an RPG \u2013 my characters get to kill them.<br /> <br /> So anyway in this section Rudi appears and he is leading a well-organized circle discussion of antifa activists Anarchs. The members of the circle are generally polite to each other. One member expresses disappointment they were transformed into a vampire before their gender confirmation surgery(1). But they also say the ability to curb stomp, with the power of a vampire, a skin head helps make up for that disappointment.<br /> <br /> Interestingly here Rudi describes himself as a strict materialist, when elsewhere he is described as a Muslim. I\u2019m not sure if this is an error or a reflection of character development.<br /> <br /> I have a personal aphorism; \u201cReal life produces the best satire.\u201d Basically it is a reference to all the times life out does things like Saturday Night Live, for example. In real life antifa is not a singular thing or organization, it is a general social cause. It is also generally responsible for far less crime that the alt right. This despite how it is treated in some circles as some kind of fifth column. The alt right, for all its jingoist bravado, cannot help but create fantasies of vast enemy forces when mostly people are just sick of their bloody juvenile bullshit.<br /> <br /> However, in the World of Darkness at least parts of antifa are carefully organized, by inhumane monsters no less. The vampires involved will quickly escalate situations in which they are involved and will, as always, turn the cause into something toxic.<br /> <br /> In any case, this is another good section in that it provides a good insight into another aspect of the Anarchs and it provides potential plot hooks for an entire group.<br /> <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>I hope they do not express that sentiment around a Tzimisce, or if they do they are also highly skeptical of offers that sound too good to be true.</li> </ol><br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-04T20:50:01-07:00","id":1416794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1416790#post1416790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Rudi\u2019s Army</b></div> </div> </div> </div>I have thoughts on Rudi's Army.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> On a personal level I\u2019m alright with Nazi\u2019s appearing in an RPG for the same reason I\u2019m alright with zombies and evil cultists appearing in an RPG \u2013 my characters get to kill them. </div> </div> </div>One of the oddest fights I've ever gotten into on this forum was a guy who was angry that I kept talking about the Nazis in Kentucky in my posts about the state. He said that not everyone who disagrees with me politically was a Nazi. I then had to explain that I was not speaking metaphorically but was referring to the actual swasztica wearing white supremacist people who are the &quot;generic ethnic crime gang&quot; of Appallachia.<br /> <br /> There's a LOT of them here and if I played a Brujah, it would be a pretty big buffett for them if they wanted to solely feed on fascists. We only banned last year the sale of Nazi paraphenalia at the state fair: <a href=\"https://www.courier-journal.com/story/news/2018/11/15/sales-nazi-and-kkk-items-banned-kentucky-expo-center/2003010002/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.courier-journal.com/stor...er/2003010002/</a><br /> <br /> In other words, they may not enough to overthrow the government and install a Fifth Reich but there's a lot of Neo-Nazis criminals in the United States and plenty in Europe too if you know where to look. They also are perfect guilt-free eating as the TV show <i>Santa Clarita Diet</i> show. Those wacky yuppie California Nagaraja.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.buzzfeed.com/krystieyandoli/santa-clarita-diet-nazis\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.buzzfeed.com/krystieyand...ita-diet-nazis</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So anyway in this section Rudi appears and he is leading a well-organized circle discussion of antifa activists Anarchs. The members of the circle are generally polite to each other. One member expresses disappointment they were transformed into a vampire before their gender confirmation surgery(1). But they also say the ability to curb stomp, with the power of a vampire, a skin head helps make up for that disappointment. <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>I hope they do not express that sentiment around a Tzimisce, or if they do they are also highly skeptical of offers that sound too good to be true.</li> </ol> </div> </div> </div>While it's probably not a good idea to submit to the operating table of ANY Tzimisce, I am wondering if the Sabbat defections to the Anarchs and the Lasombra defection to the Camarilla has led to a proliferation of Vicissitude among the organizations. Besides, even if you don't trust the Tzimisce to do the job for you, a person who hasn't had gender confirming surgery could learn Protean/Vicissitude from one of these individuals in order to change their body themselves.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Interestingly here Rudi describes himself as a strict materialist, when elsewhere he is described as a Muslim. I\u2019m not sure if this is an error or a reflection of character development. </div> </div> </div>Some interesting possibilities:<br /> <br /> 1. Rudi is assumed to be a Muslim because he's an German-Arab immigrant and other vampires stereotype him.<br /> <br /> 2. Rudi is lying to his Antifa friends here and is a great believer in the supernatural. The same possibly for other vampires. Whatever works.<br /> <br /> 3. Rudi's opinions on the supernatural changed in the subsequent years since this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I have a personal aphorism; \u201cReal life produces the best satire.\u201d Basically it is a reference to all the times life out does things like Saturday Night Live, for example. In real life antifa is not a singular thing or organization, it is a general social cause. It is also generally responsible for far less crime that the alt right. This despite how it is treated in some circles as some kind of fifth column. The alt right, for all its jingoist bravado, cannot help but create fantasies of vast enemy forces when mostly people are just sick of their bloody juvenile bullshit.<br /> <br /> However, in the World of Darkness at least parts of antifa are carefully organized, by inhumane monsters no less. The vampires involved will quickly escalate situations in which they are involved and will, as always, turn the cause into something toxic. </div> </div> </div>Rudi's group is interesting because it's perfectly believable that a random group of vampires would be a gang of misfits because the undead tend to pick people from the margins of society to begin with. An atheist gay Arabic German immigrant, a trans vampire, a Swiss would-be ally, and a few other undead concerned with fighting fascism seems a bit ridiculous except you can find far stranger groups in typical player character coteries. Also, if you went to a RL group dedicated to fighting fascists, you'd find just as diverse a group (minus the vampires). Because RL is unrealistic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In any case, this is another good section in that it provides a good insight into another aspect of the Anarchs and it provides potential plot hooks for an entire group. </div> </div> </div>Agreed, Rudi and his kind want to use their powers to make the world a better place but are they worse monsters than the Nazis?<br /> <br /> I dunno, I'm kind of on their side here.<br /> <br /> Note: Damsel uses Tender to lure Nazis to their doom. So, it seems the Anarchs have made fascism a dangerous ideology.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-04T22:11:15-07:00","id":1416797,"title":"","content":"Random Aside: I have the weird idea that Jeanette Voerman and Therese are the two Avril Lavinges in the &quot;Girlfriend&quot; video AND the two Taylor Swifts in &quot;Belong&quot;. The boyfriends are confused because they keep switching personalities.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 10-05-2020, 02:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-05T00:03:31-07:00","id":1416807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1416771#post1416771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <img src=\"https://static.tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pub/images/paint_3.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Another good example is NIGHT ROAD where we have a couple of example this in practice.<br /> <br /> <b>Pattermuster</b> is a Brujah medical doctor who runs a free Catholic hospital that he does his very best to use to provide as much healthcare he can to the locals of Tuscon, Arizona. This is a lot of people because a lot of people cannot afford healthcare in the United States. Duh. However, Pattermuster's desire to help people also extends to the Thin Bloods and the local Caitiff in the area which he allows to feed at the hospital. The result of the two attempts to &quot;help&quot; have turned the hospital into a shit show as people who would recover from their injuries end up being killed. It becomes even more of a shit show because they can't afford to keep the place open on their current budget and thus one of the vampires (who doesn't want to lose her haven and safe feeding place), takes to using the place for a cover for a massive pill marketing scheme. The pills paying to keep the hospital open and free.<br /> <br /> I swear this is a GLORIOUS example of the Anarchs at work, IMHO.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh. That's a really different read on Pattermuster from what I've got.<br /> <br /> 1. Pattermuster doesn't run St.Basil. Yes, he's a vampire in charge of it, but he doesn't actually control it. Head of the hospital is a totally different person, Pattermuster doesn't have a grasp on the general affairs of the hospital, and it all comes back to bite him in the ass when the Second Inquisition takes over.<br /> 2. His desire and ability to help the mortals in St.Basil is questionable. The hospital is certainly run down, and Pattermuster's not really doing anything to fix it. There's a whole drug operation running through the place that he's unaware of.<br /> 3. Said drug operation isn't paying to keep the hospital open and free.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-05T00:11:58-07:00","id":1416808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1416807#post1416807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Huh. That's a really different read on Pattermuster from what I've got.<br /> <br /> 1. Pattermuster doesn't run St.Basil. Yes, he's a vampire in charge of it, but he doesn't actually control it. Head of the hospital is a totally different person, Pattermuster doesn't have a grasp on the general affairs of the hospital, and it all comes back to bite him in the ass when the Second Inquisition takes over.<br /> 2. His desire and ability to help the mortals in St.Basil is questionable. The hospital is certainly run down, and Pattermuster's not really doing anything to fix it. There's a whole drug operation running through the place that he's unaware of.<br /> 3. Said drug operation isn't paying to keep the hospital open and free.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. Eh, it's his domain and while he has the General Manager planning a bunch of reforms, they're rather easily thwarted.<br /> 2. My chief rememberace is his attempts to save a dying patient as a Brujah and being disgusted when he can't.<br /> 3. The drug operation is extremely interconnected with the hospital and used by the member of the hospital that he executes. I jumped the gun but you can convince Pattermuster to take over the drug operations to fund the hospital.<br /> <br /> He's not on the ball with all the issues but that's a reflection of attempting to serve two masters:<br /> <br /> 1. His vampire associates.<br /> 2. The mortals of the place.<br /> <br /> If he got rid of the vampires or stopped caring about the humans, things would work much better for him.<br /> <br /> But even if I did read it wrong, I think it's a good example of Anarch philosophy failing in the face of the realities of vampirism. Julian doesn't care about the humans of the city, only funding his vampire project and thus he actually is able to make accomplishments. However, it turns into the fact the vast majority of players refused to make the choice to run the labor camp as a blood farm.<br /> <br /> Most vampires have SOME standards.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 10-05-2020, 03:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-05T01:10:49-07:00","id":1416815,"title":"","content":"I think Vampires can have their pet causes without treading on the toes of every other vampire in the city and ruining the eco system.<br /> <br /> Say, some left wing organizations are filled with absolute clowns. A good deal of modern 'social justice' stuff has pushed centrists further to the right. A vampire needs to encourage the clowns on both sides. <br /> <br /> I'm living in a country right now with the most fucking batshit view on homoexuals are held by a significant portion of the populace (and there's an election in a week) and they all look at western movies shoving in token gays everywhere as some kind of insidious plan to make everyone gay and lower birthrates (No joke, they act like it's an infectious illness.) It is <i>the</i> partisan issue of politics right here and it overshadows anything economic.<br /> <br /> Left wing vampire champions should do the callow corperate thing and do a lot of fake progressivism. Like they should produce 2020's Mulan. Or more successfully; Star Wars: The last Jedi. Not only can you trick yourself into thinking you're doing good, but you're also aiding other vampires who trive off of close-knit partisan groups.<br /> <br /> The best way for Vampire to champions the LGBTQ community is to make it US vs THEM. They should bring LGBTQ people together, encourage activities that would drive them further from mainstream acceptance. Push the more controversial and divisive aspects of the movement to the front. Call everyone who doesn't agree with you as a mindless bigot. Have everyone wear flags to differentiate them from the normal populace. Raise awareness as much as possible. Demand representation in media even when in situations where it doesn't fit and where doing so would push more mainstream audiences further to the right...<br /> <br /> This all makes it easier for you, the vampire, to feed on the LGBTQ community. It makes it easier for your friend, another vampire, to feed on the Bigot community. It helps both of you make money. It helps people forget about economic issues when an election comes up. Everybody wins (except the poor mortals)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 10-05-2020, 04:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-05T01:18:43-07:00","id":1416817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1416815#post1416815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Vampires can have their pet causes without treading on the toes of every other vampire in the city and ruining the eco system.<br /> <br /> Say, some left wing organizations are filled with absolute clowns. A good deal of modern 'social justice' stuff has pushed centrists further to the right.<br /> <br /> I'm living in a country right now with the most fucking batshit view on homoexuals are held by a significant portion of the populace (and there's an election in a week) and they all look at western movies shoving in token gays everywhere as some kind of insidious plan to make everyone gay and lower birthrates (No joke, they act like it's an infectious illness.) It is <i>the</i> partisan issue of politics right here and it overshadows anything economic.<br /> <br /> Left wing vampire champions should do the callow corperate thing and do a lot of fake progressivism. Like they should produce 2020's Mulan. Or more successfully; Star Wars: The last Jedi. Not only can you trick yourself into thinking you're doing good, but you're also aiding other vampires who trive off of close-knit partisan groups.<br /> <br /> The best way for Vampire to champions the LGBTQ community is to make it US vs THEM. They should bring LGBTQ people together, encourage activities that would drive them further from mainstream acceptance. Push the more controversial and divisive aspects of the movement to the front. Call everyone who doesn't agree with you as a mindless bigot. Have everyone wear flags to differentiate them from the normal populace. Raise awareness as much as possible. Demand representation in media even when in situations where it doesn't fit and where doing so would push more mainstream audiences further to the right...<br /> <br /> This all makes it easier for you, the vampire, to feed on the LGBTQ community. It makes it easier for your friend, another vampire, to feed on the Bigot community. It helps both of you make money. It helps people forget about economic issues when an election comes up. Everybody wins (except the poor mortals)</div> </div> </div> </div>I think my best rebuttal here is essentially you're arguing vampires should work together to achieve a better environment for themselves.<br /> <br /> Which they won't.<br /> <br /> A Brujah will go in, murder the guys preying on LGBT people, then go back to feeding on bigots or he will then feed on the LGBT people safe in his hypocrisy that HE did them a favor. The Camarilla tries to get vampires to work together on these things but in the end, they won't.<br /> <br /> To use another example from Night Road, Elin Olivecrona is one of the great heroines of vampires.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://static.tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pub/images/paint_5.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Elin Olivecrona has set up a massive migrant camp where the locals are actively being fed on in en masse with the police, state police, ICE, and everyone turning a blind eye. The Second Inquisition EVENTUALLY gets around to it but with ample forewarning. Better still, she's already got OFFERS to resume the business of bleeding people like cows are milked in other immigrant holding facilities. So much so she's made a fortune in the Blood trade and single-handedly supplies most of Seattle.<br /> <br /> It's an incredibly lucrative business and helps the Kindred maintain a lower profile. It is even stated to be something that could be used to eventually create a Kindred paradise. Something like 96% of players go about freeing the migrants and sabotaging her plans according to stats, even in replay. The big picture just does not fit with at least some Kindred anymore than it does with regular humans.<br /> <br /> If they did, vampires would be better off.<br /> <br /> The Anarchs screw with the Kindred's business.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-05T01:26:25-07:00","id":1416819,"title":"","content":"So your argument is &quot;This all falls apart if someone MURDERS YOU&quot; (or otherwise has something against you)<br /> <br /> Well, yeah, I guess it does.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://www.dictionary.com/e/wp-content/uploads/2020/05/picard-facepalm.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <br /> But Elin Olivecrona sounds like a vampire hero. Finally some well written characters. Shame she's apart of a scenario with what sounds like poorly written protagonists with shitty motivations. They got stats for this? Storyteller probably lead the players into doing it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 10-05-2020, 04:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-05T01:34:34-07:00","id":1416822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1416819#post1416819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But Elin Olivecrona sounds like a vampire hero. Finally some well written characters. Shame she's apart of a scenario with what sounds like poorly written protagonists with shitty motivations. They got stats for this? Storyteller probably lead the players into doing it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Before you give me the Picard facepalm, maybe you should ask yourself, &quot;You are making a plan...involving vampires...that DOESN'T account for their natural tendency to infight as well as undermine each other at every turn?&quot;<br /> <br /> Am I getting that right?<br /> <br /> And yes, basically the Circulatory System of V5 is pretty much large scale human trafficking and slavery in the Modern Era. Don't ask where the blood you can buy in every city comes from. But vampires have finally organized to make sure all the humans are milked enough that blood is a ready commodity.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-05T05:33:37-07:00","id":1416845,"title":"","content":"Of course, that's obvious, but you seem to be conflating standard vampire dickery and righteous crusades.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-05T06:20:29-07:00","id":1416851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1416845#post1416845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...standard vampire dickery and righteous crusades.</div> </div> </div> </div>These are vampires - when they are involved its hard to tell the one from the other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-05T07:56:25-07:00","id":1416860,"title":"","content":"But Vampires do work together. Their society has functionality. They live under laws. They have leaders with mandates. Vampires support vampires when it's in their interest, they want good neighbours and they want stability. The vampires who break the social contract are shunned, and the vampires who break the rules are killed.<br /> <br /> Elin is a good neighbour. The Vampire warping the LGBTQ community is a good neighbour. A vampire who kills them off in the name of mortal morality is a fuckwit who is going to be destroyed; Tactically it's a mistake, strategically it's a mistake, socially it's a mistake, legally it's lethal. You don't get to say 'nah it's cool I'm an anarch'. Most of the anarchs think you're a dickhead who deserve whatever the Camarilla are going to do to you. If you'll do that to a Camarilla vampire, you'll do that to an Anarch vampire, and a lot of them are in deeper evil than Elin ever was.<br /> <br /> Vampires like that do not survive.<br /> Now, if you killed one of these vampires smartly; you came up with 'just cause' (actual just cause, like she broke a tradition or was an infernalist or something) then yeah, you can do it, but you're going to be under scrutiny. And when you start to be a bad neighbour (IE you heal the mortal community), people are going to be clamouring for you gone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-05T10:04:45-07:00","id":1416874,"title":"","content":"FYI - Good arguments, MWIS. I think you've got the Camarilla perspective down cold.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1416860#post1416860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But Vampires do work together. Their society has functionality. They live under laws. They have leaders with mandates. Vampires support vampires when it's in their interest, they want good neighbours and they want stability. The vampires who break the social contract are shunned, and the vampires who break the rules are killed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not trying to undermine your view but from Chicago by Night to New York by Night, every depiction of vampire-run cities has shown them to be in constant states of covert war with each other for assets, control, prestige, and resources. Their leaders either rule through tyranny or they rule as puppets of councils of powerful Elders. They have no mandates because they're feudal dictatorships where the strongest or cunningiest elder has risen to the top of the food chain.<br /> <br /> Mind you, depending on your Edition, the Camarilla might be lesser or greater in its dysfunction but it's always-always dysfunctional as fuck.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Vampires like that do not survive. </div> </div> </div>No vampire survives but the Antediluvians. Immortality, like the cake, is a lie.<br /> <br /> But your belief that Camarilla vampires have tighter bonds than Anarch ones is ridiculous. As is, &quot;If you do it to a Camarilla vampire, you'll do it to an Anarch.&quot; Which is nonsense. Anarchs regularly commit horrifying atrocities against Camarilla vampires and are accepted as &quot;heroes of the Revolution.&quot; Look at Salvador and Agata Starek.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Tactically it's a mistake, strategically it's a mistake, socially it's a mistake, legally it's lethal. </div> </div> </div>And yet plenty would do it and they'd get away with it too. Maybe not saying, &quot;I did it for morality!&quot; but certainly all you'd have to do was say, &quot;I did it because she's Ventrue.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 10-05-2020, 01:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-09T15:35:51-07:00","id":1417489,"title":"","content":"<b>What is to be done?</b><br /> <br /> Agatha \u201ccrazy little blonde Polish woman\u201d Sterek and Salvador Garcia have a verbal go at each other, with Garcia getting the best of Sterek for once. This bit mostly serves as a thematic transition from the last few sections into the next ones.<br /> <br /> <b>Educate, Agitate and Organize </b><br /> <br /> This section is a flier where in Garcia talks about how to foment dissent and revolution inside a Camarilla domain. It reads a bit like a shortened version of Saul Alinsky\u2019s <i>Rules for Radicals</i>, with the caveat that Garcia\u2019s take on it obviously includes a discussion of vampires, whereas Alinsky\u2019s neglected that demographic for some reason.<br /> <br /> Garcia expressly uses the terms educate, agitate and organize. These have been in use by political malcontents since the 1860 when they were apparently first used by (appropriately enough) real world anarchists. Notably, while Garcia might have a massive hate boner for the Camarilla, but he is not blind to the nature of the Anarchs. In the section he writes \u201cIf not in a Camarilla city, don\u2019t worry. There will still be enemies, from wannabe-tyrants who want to make the city their domain\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> In his flier he offers a great deal of solid advice, such as avoiding dealing with elders if at all possible and not getting too hung up on all Anarchs needing to speak in the right speech-code.<br /> <br /> This is a good section and provides a lot of potential, should a Storyteller and a group want to run a resistance and revolutionary style game. Even if they did not, dealing with Anarchs following Garcia\u2019s advice could provide a lot of fodder for stories.<br /> <br /> As an aside, it is interesting that Garcia thinks \u201cvampire\u201d is a vulgar term but \u201clicks\u201d is not offensive to him.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-09T15:41:58-07:00","id":1417490,"title":"","content":"I find lick offensive. We have reclaimed vampire, Caine dammit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1417489#post1417489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>What is to be done?</b><br /> <br /> Agatha \u201ccrazy little blonde Polish woman\u201d Sterek and Salvador Garcia have a verbal go at each other, with Garcia getting the best of Sterek for once. This bit mostly serves as a thematic transition from the last few sections into the next ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do kind of like how Starek and Salvador Garcia play off one another. He's 100% more interesting as, &quot;The Anarch who by dint of age has fallen behind the times and no longer gets the modern Movement&quot; than he is the &quot;veteran firebrand revolutionary.&quot;<br /> <br /> Also, you're right, she's just Outstar in my head now.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/youtube/images/0/0a/BRUJAH_EXPLAINED_-_First_playable_clan_in_Vampire_The_Masquerade_-_Bloodlines_2%21/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/340?cb=20200101132433\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 10-09-2020, 08:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-17T14:24:49-07:00","id":1418713,"title":"","content":"<b>Build a Better World (for You)</b><br /> <br /> Dalia Nakache provides this section which is about coopting mortal groups to serve as foot soldiers and cannon fodder in vampire fights.<br /> <br /> In any case, Nakache discusses using mortal groups for vampire goals. She discusses a vampire using their social circle, and friends, or even a group of people they despise. They are <i>all</i> simply mortals and thus expendable.<br /> <br /> Nakache is honest enough to write; \u201cMost of us feel intuitively that the presence of an undying monster doesn\u2019t make any political movement better. Our influence is toxic, yet we often continue to hang around with our old friends just because we like them.\u201d<br /> <br /> I cannot read this section without wincing. It is about vampire using mortal groups, in everything from creating riots to spawning urban violence, for the purposes of the vampires. The concerns and needs of the mortals are incidental. This is par for the course in the World of Darkness and in Vampire the Masquerade.<br /> <br /> This summer America has seen a kind of rioting, urban violence, and general malcontent it has not sense the civil rights movement and the protests against the Vietnam War. There are specious, but widely believed, conspiracy theories about some malign and singular group behind the protests and the riots. The \u201cBuild a Better World (for You)\u201d section is not bad. But reading it is uncomfortable.<br /> <br /> Aside from the arguable squeamishness, the section is pretty good. It provides some solid story ideas for an Anarch group.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-17T14:53:38-07:00","id":1418719,"title":"","content":"<b>Art</b><br /> <br /> This is not about a specific section but an observation about the art. I like the art in this book better than the art in the <i>Camarilla</i> book.<br /> <br /> The cover of the <i>Camarilla</i> is more memorable and striking than the cover of the <i>Anarch</i> book. But the interior art in the Anarch book is better. The Camarilla book is home to a lot of static art of buildings and things, such as on pages 11, 15, 17, 18, and so on. By comparison, the <i>Anarch</i> book is home to a lot of images of people, which are more interesting that just pictures of some skyscraper.<br /> <br /> The stylized images are interesting, like the ones of page 17 and 23. The image on page 30 is done in the style of Tom of Finland, which is fine but its placement at this point in the book feels a bit random. I think it is supposed to Sterek on pages 63, but in my head the character looks like Outstar.<br /> <br /> On page 114 in the original version of <i>Anarchs</i> is a picture of a Saulbri. In the edited version her third has been removed, which is a pity.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-17T14:56:30-07:00","id":1418721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1418713#post1418713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Build a Better World (for You)</b><br /> <br /> Dalia Nakache provides this section which is about coopting mortal groups to serve as foot soldiers and cannon fodder in vampire fights.<br /> <br /> In any case, Nakache discusses using mortal groups for vampire goals. She discusses a vampire using their social circle, and friends, or even a group of people they despise. They are <i>all</i> simply mortals and thus expendable.<br /> <br /> Nakache is honest enough to write; \u201cMost of us feel intuitively that the presence of an undying monster doesn\u2019t make any political movement better. Our influence is toxic, yet we often continue to hang around with our old friends just because we like them.\u201d<br /> <br /> I cannot read this section without wincing. It is about vampire using mortal groups, in everything from creating riots to spawning urban violence, for the purposes of the vampires. The concerns and needs of the mortals are incidental. This is par for the course in the World of Darkness and in Vampire the Masquerade.<br /> <br /> This summer America has seen a kind of rioting, urban violence, and general malcontent it has not sense the civil rights movement and the protests against the Vietnam War. There are specious, but widely believed, conspiracy theories about some malign and singular group behind the protests and the riots. The \u201cBuild a Better World (for You)\u201d section is not bad. But reading it is uncomfortable.<br /> <br /> Aside from the arguable squeamishness, the section is pretty good. It provides some solid story ideas for an Anarch group.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>One of the most interesting short term arguments I ever had on the internet was with Lindsay Ellis of Nostalgia Chick fame. I doubt she remembers it but she did a review of how Fox Mulder had aged badly due to the fact conspiracy theories have become a tool of the Alt-Right in particular and Far Right in general. Therefore, it's harder now to support a conspiracy theorist protagonist given we know they're probably a bunch of racist psychopaths who want to shoot brown people and democrats.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.tor.com/2015/03/03/fox-mulder-romantic-conspiracy-theorist/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.tor.com/2015/03/03/fox-m...racy-theorist/</a><br /> <br /> I pointed out the irony that while conspiracy theorists have never been grosser and more dangerous that conspiracies as we know them have never been more obvious as well as objectively true. Corporate cover-ups, election rigging, mass NSA surveillance, Russian election interference, data-manipulation, and sex trafficking by billionaires for billionaires (it just wasn't under a pizza joint with vampire Satanists). I made a tasteless joke about the Seventh Generation being real at my table once.<br /> <br /> She never responded.<br /> <br /> But yes, one of the interesting things about V:TM 5th Edition is that you have articles about this and they're not necessarily wrong. There are crisis actors and destabilizing agents inside a lot of protest movements working to either frame them for violence or just motivate them to it. I've seen plenty of people also infiltrate forums and groups to change the tone.<br /> <br /> One of the craziest things is the fact I was on 4chan when the whole Qanon thing was created. The whole meta-fiction AR game based around the fanfic of a fake leaker is no more realistic than 45 fighting the Slenderman but it has taken off and utterly transformed conversation in America. Would it be in poor taste to reveal a Malkavian was responsible (Son?) or some racist Brujah? I dunno, because reality has become a bit like Mike Tyson. You can't make up any stories about it that are weirder than the truth these days.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-18T05:06:18-07:00","id":1418807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1418721#post1418721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I pointed out the irony that while conspiracy theorists have never been grosser and more dangerous that conspiracies as we know them have never been more obvious as well as objectively true. Corporate cover-ups, election rigging, mass NSA surveillance, Russian election interference, data-manipulation, and sex trafficking by billionaires for billionaires (it just wasn't under a pizza joint with vampire Satanists). I made a tasteless joke about the Seventh Generation being real at my table once.</div> </div> </div> </div>More than this - conspiracy theorist circles are smaller now than ever before. At one point almost 90% of Americans believed that Kennedy Assassination is sketchy and can't be a lone gunman job. We see conspiracy theories as dangerous in the now because we live in the now. But much like with crime - conspiracy theories are on the downturn, but the fear of conspiracy theories is rising.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> One of the craziest things is the fact I was on 4chan when the whole Qanon thing was created. The whole meta-fiction AR game based around the fanfic of a fake leaker is no more realistic than 45 fighting the Slenderman but it has taken off and utterly transformed conversation in America. Would it be in poor taste to reveal a Malkavian was responsible (Son?) or some racist Brujah? I dunno, because reality has become a bit like Mike Tyson. You can't make up any stories about it that are weirder than the truth these days. </div> </div> </div>For the record - QAnon has long since left its birthplace at 4chan. For years now the main QAnon audience are 40+ folks on facebook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-18T05:25:02-07:00","id":1418809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1418719#post1418719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Art</b><br /> <br /> This is not about a specific section but an observation about the art. I like the art in this book better than the art in the <i>Camarilla</i> book.<br /> <br /> The cover of the <i>Camarilla</i> is more memorable and striking than the cover of the <i>Anarch</i> book. But the interior art in the Anarch book is better. The Camarilla book is home to a lot of static art of buildings and things, such as on pages 11, 15, 17, 18, and so on. By comparison, the <i>Anarch</i> book is home to a lot of images of people, which are more interesting that just pictures of some skyscraper.<br /> <br /> The stylized images are interesting, like the ones of page 17 and 23. The image on page 30 is done in the style of Tom of Finland, which is fine but its placement at this point in the book feels a bit random. I think it is supposed to Sterek on pages 63, but in my head the character looks like Outstar.<br /> <br /> On page 114 in the original version of <i>Anarchs</i> is a picture of a Saulbri. In the edited version her third has been removed, which is a pity.</div> </div> </div> </div>She's just winking at you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-18T07:13:31-07:00","id":1418813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1418809#post1418809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> She's just winking at you.</div> </div> </div> </div>(waggles my eyebrows back at her)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-18T07:35:27-07:00","id":1418816,"title":"","content":"<b>Keep Yo Turf</b><br /> <br /> One thing that struck me on reading this is that the Camarilla\u2019s ability to do background searches on employees is non-existent or completely rubbish.<br /> <br /> Here a mature Anarch guides a neonate through a night and provides some guidance on survival. One big element of this is hiding in plain sight, more or less. The group of Anarchs the pair belongs to is known to exist by mortals who think it is simply another human gang with its own urban territory. I hope at least one such group of Anarchs calls themselves the Bloods.<br /> <br /> The older Anarch also has a relatively high humanity score, to judge by her actions here. She engages in some showy self-harm to intimidate some human gang members, rather than just trashing or even killing the mortals. But it gets the point across.<br /> <br /> The younger one thinks about the Masquerade and decides to pretend to be a Camarilla vampire, so as to spy on the Ivory Tower. This apparently works and she eventually gets a job an Archon. Damn. You go girl.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-18T08:06:52-07:00","id":1418826,"title":"","content":"<b>The Prince Must Die</b><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1413142#post1413142\">So Tbilisi is an Anarch city. Tbilisi is the capital of the nation of Georgia. I will add that to the list of known Anarch territories</a>.<br /> <br /> In this section Natia Abakelia provides some guidance on subverting the Camarilla from within. She specifically advises infiltrating the Ivory Tower and turning its own methodologies and weaknesses against it.<br /> <br /> She says \u201c\u2026if you really want to fight like a vampire, you must abandon honor and principle. Burrow deep into the flesh of the enemy and poison them from within.\u201d<br /> <br /> Two sections which stood out to me include;<ul><li>\u201cMake it an offence to be insufficiently servile. When the Prince makes a joke, note who failed to laugh, then whisper to others about it. Your goal is to create a situation where the Prince makes a speech and nobody dares to stop applauding first because they\u2019re afraid to be seen as disloyal.\u201d</li> <li>\u201cA classic trick is to be a stickler for rules. Always demand that the proper protocol be followed, no matter the urgency of the situation. Argue for a strict interpretation of the Traditions, against local initiative.\u201d</li> </ul><br /> <br /> The Camarilla is vulnerable to strategies like this and such moves could leave it moribund and unable to respond to Anarch moves, if the Anarchs have some patients and finesse.<br /> <br /> There is a lot of good material here for Anarchs trying to divide and conquer a Camarilla domain, or even for Camarilla vampires trying to fight against such an effort.<br /> <br /> As an aside, Abakelia states that the Tbilisi Anarchs broke from the Soviet Brujah in the 1970s. That is interesting as Georgia itself remained a communist nation and part of the mortal soviet sphere until the collapses of communism in 1990s. Even so, the vampires at least in Tbilisi slipped out of the grasp of the vampires in Moscow and Russia. That would be an interesting historical campaign.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1208,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","user":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","date":". 10-18-2020, 11:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-18T08:48:30-07:00","id":1418832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1418826#post1418826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Camarilla is vulnerable to strategies like this and such moves could leave it moribund and unable to respond to Anarch moves</div> </div> </div> </div>I see two big issues with these ideas.<br /> <br /> 1. Nothing described is Camarilla specific. Sure, maybe this is some in-character hypocrisy, but the suggested approaches to corrupt the Camarilla are exactly applicable to the Anarchs. The Anarch structure is the same. There's also a Baron and enforcers and stuff.<br /> 2.How exactly is this supposed to work? &quot;Make it an offence to be insufficiently servile. Always demand that the proper protocol be followed. Argue for a strict interpretation of the Traditions&quot; - who are you and how did you end up in a position of power where you can meaningfully do that? You are Joe Newguy who just joined the local Camarilla and is now at the bottom of the pecking order. Or you are apparently powerful enough or scheming enough to kill an Archon and usurp their place, and can have way bigger impact operations than &quot;be really annoying&quot;.<br /> <br /> I get it, this is clearly inspired by IRL research. But the power structure and mobility ladders of the Nazis are way different from those of the Camarilla.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-18T10:17:32-07:00","id":1418852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1418832#post1418832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Nothing described is Camarilla specific.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually the term Prince is a Camarilla term. The Sabbat used Archbishop and the Anarchs (generally) use the term Baron. Further, the text in this section discusses using the Traditions, which are the Camarilla common law. No other sect uses the Traditions.<br /> <br /> As for your second point, I except any such effort to subvert Camarilla rule would take time, years at least and potentially decades.<br /> <br /> Edit: I suspect the Soviet Brujah used the term Chairman.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1208,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","user":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","date":". 10-18-2020, 01:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-18T10:27:36-07:00","id":1418856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1418826#post1418826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>The Prince Must Die</b><br /> <br /> <br /> Two sections which stood out to me include;<ul><li>\u201cMake it an offence to be insufficiently servile. When the Prince makes a joke, note who failed to laugh, then whisper to others about it. Your goal is to create a situation where the Prince makes a speech and nobody dares to stop applauding first because they\u2019re afraid to be seen as disloyal.\u201d</li> <li>\u201cA classic trick is to be a stickler for rules. Always demand that the proper protocol be followed, no matter the urgency of the situation. Argue for a strict interpretation of the Traditions, against local initiative.\u201d</li> </ul><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This sounds like how some old clan Tzimisce rule their enclaves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/769-chris-wilson","name":"Chris Wilson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-18T10:32:42-07:00","id":1418859,"title":"","content":"Points of order: prince was the term used pre-Camarilla. The Traditions are used pre-camarilla (with less emphasis on the masquerade) and presumably the Ashirra. <br /> <br /> Prince/Baron thing is... kinda just a thing players decided on. All leaders select their titles, and Baron seems appropriate to the leader of a large semi-autonomous domain, and these Domains are often the anarch areas of a Camarilla city. But the Baron could just as well be an influentual Camarilla elder or an Independent. 'Baron' has become synonymous with Anarch leader because of the setup of these domains. <br /> <br /> <i>Also Anarchs probably know that the Camarilla will more likely want to kick their teeth in if they name an Anarch &quot;Prince&quot;. </i><br /> <br /> <br /> In an Anarch-dominated city. They would likely adopt a different term. Like &quot;president&quot; or &quot;prime minister&quot; or &quot;Boss&quot; or &quot;The Leader&quot; or &quot;The Manager&quot; or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-18T11:57:06-07:00","id":1418869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1418816#post1418816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Keep Yo Turf</b><br /> <br /> One thing that struck me on reading this is that the Camarilla\u2019s ability to do background searches on employees is non-existent or completely rubbish.<br /> <br /> Here a mature Anarch guides a neonate through a night and provides some guidance on survival. One big element of this is hiding in plain sight, more or less. The group of Anarchs the pair belongs to is known to exist by mortals who think it is simply another human gang with its own urban territory. I hope at least one such group of Anarchs calls themselves the Bloods.<br /> <br /> The older Anarch also has a relatively high humanity score, to judge by her actions here. She engages in some showy self-harm to intimidate some human gang members, rather than just trashing or even killing the mortals. But it gets the point across.<br /> <br /> The younger one thinks about the Masquerade and decides to pretend to be a Camarilla vampire, so as to spy on the Ivory Tower. This apparently works and she eventually gets a job an Archon. Damn. You go girl.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It's funny because THE CHICAGO FOLIO flat out shows what a terrible idea that infiltrating the Camarilla is, at least if you don't have an exit strategy. Devin Boyes asks to argue for the player characters with the Prince and if they're dumb enough to let a teenager bargain for them, they effectively find the Camarilla wants more than just empty promises from their members regarding the Anarchs. They want you to PROVE your loyalty and that means burning bridges with the Anarchs permanently as Damien was forced to.<br /> <br /> Or to quite FLASH GORDON (DA DAaaa) the movie:<br /> <br /> <i>Chief: We have nothing to offer but our loyalty.<br /> <br /> Ming the Merciless: How deep is that loyalty?<br /> <br /> Chief: Without limit!<br /> <br /> Ming the Merciless: Excellent! Kill yourself.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-18T12:07:23-07:00","id":1418870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1418832#post1418832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I see two big issues with these ideas.<br /> <br /> 1. Nothing described is Camarilla specific. Sure, maybe this is some in-character hypocrisy, but the suggested approaches to corrupt the Camarilla are exactly applicable to the Anarchs. The Anarch structure is the same. There's also a Baron and enforcers and stuff.<br /> 2.How exactly is this supposed to work? &quot;Make it an offence to be insufficiently servile. Always demand that the proper protocol be followed. Argue for a strict interpretation of the Traditions&quot; - who are you and how did you end up in a position of power where you can meaningfully do that? You are Joe Newguy who just joined the local Camarilla and is now at the bottom of the pecking order. Or you are apparently powerful enough or scheming enough to kill an Archon and usurp their place, and can have way bigger impact operations than &quot;be really annoying&quot;.<br /> <br /> I get it, this is clearly inspired by IRL research. But the power structure and mobility ladders of the Nazis are way different from those of the Camarilla.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think they're going for ROYAL COURT vs. STREET GANG versus Nazis and Democracies.<br /> <br /> Essentially, the big difference between a Baron and a Prince is not their titles but their style of management. They're not AS different as the Anarchs like to believe. Being called a Baron is meant to be a joke and one that isn't particularly funny to old school Anarchs like Jeremy MacNeil. However, even that is a not insignificant difference, In a real sense the idea is, &quot;A Baron is the ruler but he is meant to be significantly closer to his knights.&quot;<br /> <br /> A Camarilla Prince depends on tradition, protocol, and respect for the system to provide them with their power. Status, intrigue, power games, and one-upmanship in Elysium is very much a part of the thing. A lot of Camarilla leaders come from times when the forms of showing respect were long and complicated rituals that if you didn't show them, you were being actively disloyal. George W. Bush kicked out his own staff at meetings who never wore ties and that was in the 21st century.<br /> <br /> The funny thing about Anarchs is the fact that their leaders must show they do NOT care about the trappings of power while still having the level of personal charisma to shut down challenges to said power. A Baron is not going to care about the dress code, cheering [though he may note it], or bad attitudes but he needs to kick the shit out of anyone who actively disobeys. There's still going to be some intrigue in Anarch domains but they attempt to go with the idea of Anarch domains having less overt bullshit and pretension.<br /> <br /> In the TV Show ROME there's a scene where Pompey accidentally starts his war with Caesar early due to the fact Marc Anthony is so bored out of his skull with procedure he fails to exercise his veto for declaring Caesar a renegade. The Camarilla-types in this scenario run around trying to find a legal justification for undoing what they did while Marc just assumes they all want war now because, &quot;Why would you make the vote unless you did?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-18T13:31:25-07:00","id":1418880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris Wilson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1418856#post1418856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This sounds like how some old clan Tzimisce rule their enclaves.</div> </div> </div> </div>The prince in her story actually was Tzimisce; perhaps they didn't need to actively make her court like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-18T13:36:10-07:00","id":1418883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1418852#post1418852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually the term Prince is a Camarilla term. The Sabbat used Archbishop and the Anarchs (generally) use the term Baron. Further, the text in this section discusses using the Traditions, which are the Camarilla common law. No other sect uses the Traditions.<br /> <br /> As for your second point, I except any such effort to subvert Camarilla rule would take time, years at least and potentially decades.<br /> <br /> Edit: I suspect the Soviet Brujah used the term Chairman.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well yes, I know that Anarchs call their Princes &quot;Barons&quot;. My point is that Barons still exist and Anarch clique politics are not particularly different from Camarilla clique politics. It's sort of a natural result of both being small scale might-makes-right structures.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1418870#post1418870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Camarilla Prince depends on tradition, protocol, and respect for the system to provide them with their power. Status, intrigue, power games, and one-upmanship in Elysium is very much a part of the thing. A lot of Camarilla leaders come from times when the forms of showing respect were long and complicated rituals that if you didn't show them, you were being actively disloyal.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno man. From the material I've seen - a Camarilla Prince depends on the Sheriff and personal connection to the Primogen. And usually comes to power not through status and tradition, but by kicking down the door and eating the previous Prince.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The funny thing about Anarchs is the fact that their leaders must show they do NOT care about the trappings of power while still having the level of personal charisma to shut down challenges to said power. A Baron is not going to care about the dress code, cheering [though he may note it], or bad attitudes but he needs to kick the shit out of anyone who actively disobeys. There's still going to be some intrigue in Anarch domains but they attempt to go with the idea of Anarch domains having less overt bullshit and pretension. </div> </div> </div>Dress code (not necessarily <i>high society dress code</i>), cheering/jeering and bad attitudes are &quot;active disobediance&quot; once you get authoritarian enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12892,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","user":"Kammerer","date":". 10-18-2020, 04:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-18T13:40:32-07:00","id":1418884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1418883#post1418883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well yes, I know that Anarchs call their Princes &quot;Barons&quot;. My point is that Barons still exist and Anarch clique politics are not particularly different from Camarilla clique politics. It's sort of a natural result of both being small scale might-makes-right structures.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah and I disagree.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I dunno man. From the material I've seen - a Camarilla Prince depends on the Sheriff and personal connection to the Primogen. And usually comes to power not through status and tradition, but by kicking down the door and eating the previous Prince. </div> </div> </div>Actually, it seems to be, &quot;The Primogen backs you instead of the previous guy&quot; as we see with Kevin Jackson and Joseph Peterson. But the Primogen is made of the Elders. So, it's really whoever the Elders support.<br /> <br /> In Anarchs, its who everyone supports.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-18T13:43:53-07:00","id":1418886,"title":"","content":"I'm really, really, really having a hard time not seeing V5's Anarch/Camarilla conflict as anything other than.... Democrat and republican. <br /> <br /> You've got vicious psychopathic warmongers deeply in the pockets of some terrible people, who espouse nice and agreeable ideas to look good to a younger demographic, and you've got vicious psychopathic war profiteers deeply in the pockets of terrible ideas who espouse conservative and now religious ideas, are slightly more less low-key about their clanism to appeal to an older and more established demographic. Also there's no serious third party option. <i>In any case your schools aren't getting more funding</i>. <br /> <br /> It genuinely feels like this is what they're actively going for, and I don't like it. But hey, I see the Camarilla as the &quot;good&quot; guys in the most conventional sense (In that they do their best to limit the population of blood sucking parasites and reign in their worst tendancies to make very little impact on the status quo) <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">(The Setites are the actual-good vampires) </span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-18T15:41:16-07:00","id":1418898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1418886#post1418886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm really, really, really having a hard time not seeing V5's Anarch/Camarilla conflict as anything other than.... Democrat and republican.<br /> <br /> You've got vicious psychopathic warmongers deeply in the pockets of some terrible people, who espouse nice and agreeable ideas to look good to a younger demographic, and you've got vicious psychopathic war profiteers deeply in the pockets of terrible ideas who espouse conservative and now religious ideas, are slightly more less low-key about their clanism to appeal to an older and more established demographic. Also there's no serious third party option. <i>In any case your schools aren't getting more funding</i>.<br /> <br /> It genuinely feels like this is what they're actively going for, and I don't like it. But hey, I see the Camarilla as the &quot;good&quot; guys in the most conventional sense (In that they do their best to limit the population of blood sucking parasites and reign in their worst tendancies to make very little impact on the status quo)<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">(The Setites are the actual-good vampires) </span></div> </div> </div> </div>I take it as the much more cynical (but is it?) cyberpunks vs. Corporates.<br /> <br /> The cyberpunks are composed of organized crime, street hustles, drug dealers, and mercenaries.<br /> <br /> The Corporates are neo-feudalists old money families who live in an entirely different world from the punks.<br /> <br /> The cyberpunks used to be employed by the corporates as a way to keep equilibrium.<br /> <br /> Now? Now it's open warfare where the cyberpunks want to rule themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-18T16:08:15-07:00","id":1418905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1418886#post1418886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...conflict as anything other than.... Democrat and republican.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's more about order and control v. chaos. Or CONTROL and KAOS.<br /> <br /> Also, the IP is written and produced to a large extent by people who are not American, so the Democrat and Republican metaphor would mean little to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1208,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","user":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","date":". 10-18-2020, 07:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-18T16:29:25-07:00","id":1418911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1418905#post1418905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's more about order and control v. chaos. Or CONTROL and KAOS.<br /> <br /> Also, the IP is written and produced to a large extent by people who are not American, so the Democrat and Republican metaphor would mean little to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>To make a not inconsiderable joke.<br /> <br /> &quot;Goth never died in Europe, which is what's confusing as hell to American readers where it died by Revised and everyone pretended it was gone. So V5 being SUPER-GOTH confuses them to no end.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-23T19:11:07-07:00","id":1419892,"title":"","content":"<b>A V\u00e9r Hanaja</b><br /> <br /> In the reedit of the book this section is titled \u201cA v\u00e9r hangja.\u201d The text reads that this means voice of the blood in Hungarian.<br /> <br /> As an aside, <i>A V\u00e9r Hangja</i><i> is also the title of a song by the heavy metal thrash Hungarian band </i>Jogos \u00d6nv\u00e9delem (this popped up when I did a google search of the term). According to <a href=\"https://www.metal-archives.com\" target=\"_blank\">www.metal-archives.com</a> the band is associated with \u201cWhite Pride, Antisemitism, Nazism\u2026\u201d and produces music described as \u201cpure anger through and through.\u201d<br /> <br /> Right. So I don\u2019t know if the band, or the title of the track, influenced this section but both this section and the band are more or less operating from the same song book.<br /> <br /> All that to say, in this section a bigoted vampire talks about the importance of good blood and how bad breeding has debased the quality of human blood, and that this is debasing vampires. While the narrator does not speak of any particular human race or group as inferior, it would be a surprise if the narrator did not have a lot of hang ups about race, and probably religion and sexuality as well. The narrator also espouses a lot of what sounds like Sabbat ideology about vampire superiority and listening to the will of vampire blood.<br /> <br /> Anarchs are vampires, and vampires cannot be good people so Anarchs cannot be good people. Some of them are worse than others, and this one is worse than Garcia or Sterek.<br /> <br /> It is useful, if not good, to be reminded, of the fact some Anarchs are going to be utter rubbish and that it will be fine if the PCs kill them. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-23T19:37:30-07:00","id":1419895,"title":"","content":"<b>Mask and Masquerade</b><br /> <br /> Near the beginning of this section is the following passage; \u201cThere were white kids who seemed to have learned their radical politics from old Rage Against the Machine lyrics and North Africans who could quote Frantz Fanon but had never heard of Salvador Garcia\u2019s Anarch Manifesto. I thought it was the foundational text of the Anarch movement, but it turns out I was the only person there who had read it!\u201d<br /> <br /> This is one of the single best passages in the entire book. The Anarchs are, by definition, are everything the Camarilla is not \u2013 which means they are not remotely unified and do not possess a coherent communication network.<br /> <br /> In this section a neonate vampire and aspiring Anarch is living in Paris while pretending to be a loyal member of the Camarilla. The Establishment forced the neonate to kill his sire and so he has no love or loyalty for the Ivory Tower. However, the Anarchs do not trust the neonate enough to include him in their plans, or help him flee the city if things go south for him.<br /> <br /> The Sheriff demands to speak the narrator of this section and the narrator expects to be harshly interrogated and exacted \u2013 only to be congratulated by the Establishment for his temperament, connections to mortal finance and then trusted with \u201croughly half a billion euros of Camarilla properties.\u201d That is almost $600 million.<br /> <br /> The narrator still hates the Camarilla but decides to play the system, and funnel Camarilla funds and assets into the hands of the Anarchs.<br /> <br /> This is a delightful section and should provide fodder and ideas for a lot of games.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-23T23:04:09-07:00","id":1419922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1419892#post1419892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>A V\u00e9r Hanaja</b><br /> <br /> In the reedit of the book this section is titled \u201cA v\u00e9r hangja.\u201d The text reads that this means voice of the blood in Hungarian.<br /> <br /> As an aside, <i>A V\u00e9r Hangja</i><i> is also the title of a song by the heavy metal thrash Hungarian band </i>Jogos \u00d6nv\u00e9delem (this popped up when I did a google search of the term). According to <a href=\"http://www.metal-archives.com\" target=\"_blank\">www.metal-archives.com</a> the band is associated with \u201cWhite Pride, Antisemitism, Nazism\u2026\u201d and produces music described as \u201cpure anger through and through.\u201d<br /> <br /> Right. So I don\u2019t know if the band, or the title of the track, influenced this section but both this section and the band are more or less operating from the same song book.<br /> <br /> All that to say, in this section a bigoted vampire talks about the importance of good blood and how bad breeding has debased the quality of human blood, and that this is debasing vampires. While the narrator does not speak of any particular human race or group as inferior, it would be a surprise if the narrator did not have a lot of hang ups about race, and probably religion and sexuality as well. The narrator also espouses a lot of what sounds like Sabbat ideology about vampire superiority and listening to the will of vampire blood.<br /> <br /> Anarchs are vampires, and vampires cannot be good people so Anarchs cannot be good people. Some of them are worse than others, and this one is worse than Garcia or Sterek.<br /> <br /> It is useful, if not good, to be reminded, of the fact some Anarchs are going to be utter rubbish and that it will be fine if the PCs kill them.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This seems like a perfect character article for Svein &quot;Azrael&quot; Fortinbras who is a character from CHILDREN OF THE REVOLUTION. He's a character who rejected the Sabbat, is a sincere Satanist, a religious terrorist, and a heavy metal Scandanavian Follower of Set.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Svein_Fortinbras\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Svein_Fortinbras</a><br /> <br /> <b>Racism and Anarchs</b><br /> <br /> He hasn't been affiliated with white supremacy because the books are usually coy about this (with the exception of Thomas Ewell due to the BLINDINGLY OBVIOUS fact that a Confederate soldier would be racist) but I could easily see him as one of those Alt-Right pagans that are yet another reason to be embarrassed by the movement. Not a dig at pagans, FYI, just racist misogynist ones.<br /> <br /> I've always had white supremacist Anarchs among my antagonists. This despite the fact I have many more black revolutionary, hippie pacifist, and antifa Anarchs. That's because, as you say, the Anarchs are everyone not Camarilla. So a bunch of Skinheads and Nazi Brujah have shown up over the years to ruin the Anarchs' day and make the Camarilla look better.<br /> <br /> It's funny because this WAS a V5 controversy that Brujah would include white supremacists when they were listed in the original V5 manual. I felt that that was overblown because as early as Berlin by Night, Dieter was an actual Nazi Brujah. Also, probably the only one that was actually usable among the Nazi characters in the book as he wasn't a member of Nazi High Command or tastelessly inserted.<br /> <br /> (I've used Dieter a few times as a villain in my campaigns, particularly as a Sabbat infiltrator of the Anarchs)<br /> <br /> Neo-Nazis, Confederates, white supremacist pagans, Old Nazis, and probably Brujah KKK members are all things that I can see among the Anarchs. Because they're the sect closest to mortals and their ills. I also see that they're the sort of people that if they ever show up at any place other than the areas they control, they will get their asses kicked or have a war with the other Anarchs. Theodore Dooley, Maldavis, and Carlyle aren't going to work with them against the Camarilla. They may even work with the Camarilla against the Nazis.<br /> <br /> And that's why the Anarchs weren't winning their war against the Feudalists until recently (but at least they kept the Nazis from winning).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 10-24-2020, 02:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-24T02:38:41-07:00","id":1419951,"title":"","content":"I recall an early version of V5 doing it's best to say 'good brujah are -left wing- bad brujah are camarilla. That seemed controversial. The idea that Brujah have nazis among them isn't controversial. That's just outrage culture spinning it's bullshit.<br /> <br /> Real world politic but genuinely left-wing activist vampires don't make sense. The fun of embracing someone from antifa would be to see them twist and writhe as their virtues work against them, to caste off their veneer, to see what kind of person they really are. In retrospect. I've not seen anyone from antifa who i think would make good vampire material. Most of em seem like they're just LARPing... (right wing groups are somewhat better for this... even with their Grand wizards)<br /> Vampires need their disenfranchised lower classes and gloriously fun elite class; it's just good for them. If a vampire has joined antifa, it's because they've got their own goals and intend to do very little or less for left-wing activism.<br /> <br /> Right wing groups make natural allies for vampires. Left wing groups make natural enemies. White supremacists, black supremacists, &quot;libertarian&quot; militias, corrupt elites, fascist cops, propaganda media outlets, lobbyists, career politicians, war hawks, everyone with at least 4 dots of resources... all make great friends. Someone who wants to end oppression, increase wages, give more rights and freedoms to workers, cripple the insurance industry and raise public spending and clean up your domain... Might as well be a vampire hunter.<br /> <br /> You want your country to look like the United States, not Sweden. A socialist country needs to be corrupted to have a class system with elites and oppressed masses to work for vampires. Scandinavian countries are left-wing and nice in the WoD because the all-day sun in summer keeps vampires from gaining a serious foothold in most cities.<br /> <br /> People like Rudi are exceptions to the norm that the anarchs leave alone for propaganda reasons. Any reasonable vampire is going to feel persecuted the moment you fight for someone else's rights. It's a &quot;Slippery slope&quot; that needs to be curbed in infancy, and Anarchs aren't supposed to be an infant-only sect. Left wing vampires aught to be the setting's antagonists. (from the relative, vampire perspective)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 10-24-2020, 09:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-24T03:19:06-07:00","id":1419955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1419951#post1419951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I recall an early version of V5 doing it's best to say 'good brujah are -left wing- bad brujah are camarilla. That seemed controversial. The idea that Brujah have nazis among them isn't controversial. That's just outrage culture spinning it's bullshit.<br /> <br /> Real world politic but genuinely left-wing activist vampires don't make sense. The fun of embracing someone from antifa would be to see them twist and writhe as their virtues work against them, to caste off their veneer, to see what kind of person they really are. In retrospect. I've not seen anyone from antifa who i think would make good vampire material. Most of em seem like they're just LARPing... (right wing groups are somewhat better for this... even with their Grand wizards)<br /> Vampires need their disenfranchised lower classes and gloriously fun elite class; it's just good for them. If a vampire has joined antifa, it's because they've got their own goals and intend to do very little or less for left-wing activism.<br /> <br /> Right wing groups make natural allies for vampires. Left wing groups make natural enemies. White supremecists, black supremecists, &quot;liberatrian&quot; militias, corrupt elites, fascist cops, propaganda media outlets, lobbyists, career politicians, war hawks, everyone with at least 4 dots of resources... all make great friends. Someone who wants to end opression, increase wages, give more rights and freedoms to workers, cripple the insurance industry and raise public spending and clean up your domain... Might as well be a vampire hunter.<br /> <br /> You want your country to look like the United States, not Sweden. A socialist country needs to be corrupted to have a class system with elites and oppressed masses to work for vampires. Scandinavian countries are left-wing and nice in the WoD because the all-day sun in summer keeps vampires from gaining a serious foothold in most cities.<br /> <br /> People like Rudi are exceptions to the norm that the anarchs leave alone for propaganda reasons. Any reasonable vampire is going to feel persecuted the moment you fight for someone else's rights. It's a &quot;Slippery slope&quot; that needs to be curbed in infancy, and Anarchs aren't supposed to be an infant-only sect. Left wing vampires aught to be the setting's antagonists. (from the relative, vampire perspective)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <b>Long and Boring Essay on Left Wing politics vs. Right Wing with vampires</b><br /> <br /> I think that's a somewhat overly optimistic view of Left wing counter-culture or how it would interact with vampires. I also feel like Ring wing ideologies are not going to fair much better among the undead either, surprisingly enough. A friend of mine said that he felt that V:TM &quot;cheated&quot; by having vampires seemingly evolve past the prejudices of their mortal days and that most should be incredibly racist, misogynist assholes. I disagree with that actually, even among the Camarilla [especially among the Camarilla], for reasons I will get into.<br /> <br /> I feel like lots of vampires would be tied to Left Wing groups because there's always going to be the fundamental desire by vampires to self-actualize by deluding themselves into doing something useful with their powers. Very few people are the villain in their own story and even vampires who are Humanity 4 are going to have their pet causes, IMHO. Kevin Jackson wants to help the black community, another vampire might support battered women, Theo Bell has issues with slavery [modern or otherwise], and Al Capone still believes he's a patron of the downtrodden. In fact, I actually had a very interesting idea that the Toreador's entire thing is that promoting art is their spiritual purpose in life and gives their unlife meaning. It justifies all sins that they create something LASTING more than mortal life and made the world more beautiful.<br /> <br /> The thing is that this is always going to backfire in some way. You're inevitably going to start feeding on the people who are important to you. Your mindset is also going to be warped by the Beast so every problem looks like a blood bag. Police brutality? Well, obviously the solution is to just straight up MURDER the cops who killed Breonna Taylor (plenty of my fellow Kentuckians would support that solution--but probably won't help race relations in the USA).<br /> <br /> Kevin Jackson in V5 is actually a really good example of this in that he wants to help the black community and become the &quot;Good&quot; ending of Lincoln Clay in Mafia III. Build schools, support STEM, patronize the community, and so on. However, KJ makes his money selling drugs and beating loans out of people. Mostly black people. He was a vampire in life and undeath hasn't made him any better. I like this because it's got poignancy and makes the horror even better, IMHO. I think Right Wing causes are actually harder to maintain too because vampires are going to have just as many problems as Leftists maintaining any connection to the causes they held in life.<br /> <br /> Thomas Ewell and the General of Atlanta may believe the South will rise again but for the most Kindred, they're going to have trouble remembering why they cared about a bunch of Kine and their lost war as time goes on. They might miss the easy feeding but everyone is a potential food bag now.<br /> <br /> White, black, European, gay, man, woman, or straight mean little versus the common bond of being an undead predator and rival for power. To quote Dirty Harry, the average vampire &quot;hates everyone equally.&quot; Then again, in my books all vampires are kind of omnisexual too because blood is sex and sex is blood so really all humans are the same in the end. I admit I stole this from Anne Rice who had Louis go through the epiphany that blacks and whites are equal--they're both prey animals to him.<br /> <br /> But that's my take on it.<br /> <br /> Lots of activist vampires will exist. They will just make things so much worse for the people they're trying to help. Likewise, you will have Neo-Nazis and Nazi-Nazi vampires but they will have to be REALLY dedicated to not drop the whole thing after a century or so.<br /> <br /> I totally do agree vampires will genuinely manipulate Right Wing groups and keep a populace divided, supsicious, poor, and terrorized because it's easier to hide. It's just I don't see them sharing much ideology with them. In Sons of Anarchy, there was a Neo-Nazi gang that was fighting the, themselves racist, titular gang because they sold weapons to minorities. Only at the end does the Neo-Nazi find out his boss just wanted the Sons out of the way so he could take over their business.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 10-24-2020, 06:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-24T04:36:57-07:00","id":1419957,"title":"","content":"And most vampires are the boss that just want to take that business<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">Sidenote: I started SoA because I wanted to understand biker culture for a vampire character. I also find bikes beautiful, but I'm broke. Anyhow. It started off great, but &quot;The Irish stole my baby&quot; has got to be the dumbest, no-fun hammiest dramatic turn I've seen. Half-black plotline really tested me too. Dropped it hard. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">white supremecists aren't a great example as they it hasn't really been around long enough for it to disappear. It has changed. But it's still a thing. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">That said, they say a good way to elminate prejudices is to travel, and vampires essentially travel through time whilst continuously living in a narrow, fast changing age bracket. Even if they stay in the same city all their unlives, they see people change, demographics change, language change, attitutes change, fashion change, and they have to adapt or be outed for a freak. I think it's rare that more in-touch clans are going to be inflexible with that; They might hold onto a few old values that have stood the test of time, but not anything that'll get them in trouble. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">The clans more likely to seriously cling to old values are the Gangrel and Ravnos, because they spend less time around people. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Still. I feel most vampires are just oppertunists. Some vampires have closeted beliefs, some vampires are opportunistic firebrands, and a bunch of camarilla vampires are 'against racism' because it's unfashionable. Very very few vampires are going to be actual radicals. But divisiveness is good for feeding. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">True-Believer Nazis aren't many, but they're way better for vampire society than True-Believer anything-left. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Honestly I imagine there are a lot of good friendships among vampires who set their servants into radicalizing their demographics against eachother. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">&quot;Sohpia, can you believe we got them to lynch one of yours?&quot; </span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">&quot;great, send me the pictures, I'll arrange for the 'peaceful protest' on thursday, and we'll firebomb a few houses to respond. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">&quot;His servants or hers?&quot;</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">&quot;His&quot;</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">&quot;Great, how big's the hardcore crowd? </span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">&quot;Depending on what you send me. I think I can get about sixty in. Your side best come prepared. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">*opens a box*</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">&quot;We got new T-shirts and signs, check out that slogan there&quot;</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">&quot;Sweet jesus, fuck, this city's gonna burn.&quot;</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">&quot;Bout time you invest in my security company then, eh?&quot; </span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">&quot;looks like it&quot; </span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-24T06:44:31-07:00","id":1419977,"title":"","content":"Examining the implicit racism of A V\u00e9r Hanaja feels a like like breaking open a turd to examine the contents.<br /> <br /> That said, the narrator in A V\u00e9r Hanaja never specifies any race, creed, religions, gender, sexuality, or other specific quality of people. He just asserts human blood is being debased and that this is something which may be determined by the taste of the blood. At a guess his standards are pretty random.<br /> <br /> Vampires keep all the bad traits they had as living people, and drop most of the good ones when they become undead. So it is easy to believe some of them will be racist, sexist, and so on. On the other hand, some might move past that into a more general sadistic sociopathy, which I am not certain in better. For the narrator of the section the implicit racism (sexism, ableism, etc) is directly linked to his hunger as a vampire, rather than something done in terms of mortal politics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1208,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","user":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","date":". 10-24-2020, 09:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-24T07:12:10-07:00","id":1419979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1419977#post1419977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Examining the implicit racism of A V\u00e9r Hanaja feels a like like breaking open a turd to examine the contents.<br /> <br /> That said, the narrator in A V\u00e9r Hanaja never specifies any race, creed, religions, gender, sexuality, or other specific quality of people. He just asserts human blood is being debased and that this is something which may be determined by the taste of the blood. At a guess his standards are pretty random.<br /> <br /> Vampires keep all the bad traits they had as living people, and drop most of the good ones when they become undead. So it is easy to believe some of them will be racist, sexist, and so on. On the other hand, some might move past that into a more general sadistic sociopathy, which I am not certain in better.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't get the impression that they were saying that any demographic that we recognise is a better than another. The narrator's issue is that modern civilisation allows weak people to survive and breed, which prevents humanity and the Blood from reaching its potential. It's not random, it's Darwinian.<br /> <br /> Perhaps it could be a radical Bahari idea, given that they're big in Budapest in <i>Cults of the Blood Gods.</i> The conditions that this narrator wants to inflict on humanity could be described as tribulation intended to make it stronger, like a garden where only the hardiest, healthiest crops can grow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-25T04:50:46-07:00","id":1420110,"title":"","content":"agreed, I don't see any impicit racism in that section","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-25T06:59:20-07:00","id":1420118,"title":"","content":"It is not expressed explicitly, but would anyone be surprised if the narrator started blaming all the problems of weak blood on a particular race or group? Would anyone be surprised if the narrator said the first thing to do was kill all of a particular group?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-25T11:38:38-07:00","id":1420152,"title":"","content":"It would consistent with their own proposal if they believed that the genocide of that group could at least contribute to the dissolution of civilisation. I can't imagine how that would work, but making <i>humans</i> more genocidal does appear to be part of their plan. However, if they're sincere about their cause, there could be no racial group entitled to protection, because in their eyes, that would keep them and their blood weak, which would be a diservice to them, the vampires who feed on them and the Blood that they deify because their plan serves no other purpose. Although in practice, I expect that it would get hijacked by run of the mill chauvinists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-25T12:30:49-07:00","id":1420161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1420118#post1420118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is not expressed explicitly, but would anyone be surprised if the narrator started blaming all the problems of weak blood on a particular race or group? Would anyone be surprised if the narrator said the first thing to do was kill all of a particular group?</div> </div> </div> </div>it wouldn't surprise me because V5 devs seem to love that kind of thing,<br /> <br /> however, from the write-up alone, the vampire seems only concerned by the effects of the blood on their power,<br /> <br /> they would maybe target a group of people, like a group of worthless NEETs (like me),<br /> but race...each ethnic group has its strong and weak, its smart and dumb, its creative and uncreative, its useful and worthless,<br /> I doubt they would care, unless they were a Ventrue and had some prey exclusion against a specific ethnic group","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-26T01:58:50-07:00","id":1420228,"title":"","content":"My view is that V5 is more willing to use real racism instead of fantastic racism but I also believe that it keeps enough of it ambiguous that people who play V:TM to GET AWAY from this shit in RL are able to ignore it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-02T17:53:14-08:00","id":1421533,"title":"","content":"<b>#Motst\u00e5</b><br /> <br /> Motst\u00e5 is a Norwegian word meaning \u201cto resist, withstand, oppose.\u201d Probably by coincidence it sounds somewhat like the English word \u201cmonster\u201d if it were pronounced by a child or someone with a bad Boston accent.<br /> <br /> This is not a bad section, but it feels\u2026 odd for lack of a better term. It recounts in first person a night in the existence of a secret Sabbat defector to the Camarilla. This defector is sympathetic to the Anarchs, finding them to be closer to his own political sensibilities. At the same time the narrator is more or less going native inside the Camarilla, trading in favors, killing the Sheriff\u2019s lackies and enjoying their night to night existence.<br /> <br /> The story provides another depiction of subverting the Camarilla from within, but it also depicts coming to call the Camarilla home for reasons of conveyance if not for ideology.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-03T09:24:44-08:00","id":1421638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1420228#post1420228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My view is that V5 is more willing to use real racism instead of fantastic racism but I also believe that it keeps enough of it ambiguous that people who play V:TM to GET AWAY from this shit in RL are able to ignore it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Respectfully, you should remember that we're not just dealing with a game or literary work, we're dealing with a product. I feel V5 pulls all it's punches and yet kicks during a boxing match. It tries too hard to be sensitive and accommodating to the point that the World of Darkness sounds better than the real world and there's little to fight for, and yet when it does want to cause a stir it goes for low hanging fruit and/or presents it's ideological enemy as simple minded fools who should caste off their foolish beliefs and know greatness when they see it. It waves flags of virtue and It creates false consciousness. It breaks the &quot;show, don't tell&quot; rule and often feels like it's preaching to the hive on more than one occasion; I can spend hours citing instances. Oh and it backed out on Chechnya, an area where it actually did some good. So I stress again: <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">We should really consider this more from a market-in-mind perspective than a literary one. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> Especially as it feels more like a corporate appropriation of woke than actual woke. It's doing it's best to increase sales (Which, y'know, isn't inherently bad from a certain perspective; the book doesn't have to be mean for you or your storyteller could add in all the edge they want, but i do feel in this instance, it is bad, and that certain mechanical vicissitudes have arose from a desire to make the setting more egalitarian.)<br /> <br /> So, yeah, I don't think it's more willing to use real racism at all. Especially considering the use of sexism we've seen so far. V5 does the 'Women are equal to men, except when they're magically better' thing at every possible instance. It has straw-manned struggles against patriarchy in clans where such is almost entirely inappropriate (Tremere, Settites) and has never as much depicted sexists as more than monsters or clowns. I don't think we will possibly see more use of real racism, especially when it doesn't sell as well as *feminism* and doesn't resonate well among international markets. There's plenty of empowered minorities, I think that carries with it an implicit, patronizing kind of racism. But I don't we'll ever read a slur.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 11-03-2020, 12:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-03T09:26:56-08:00","id":1421639,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I strongly disagree.<br /> <br /> For example, you keep clinging to the &quot;patriarchy doesn't exist&quot; in Tremere and Setite things but both of those were 1st Edition and 2nd Edition both.<br /> <br /> Carna and Keminitri are both about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-03T10:01:40-08:00","id":1421643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1421639#post1421639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I strongly disagree.<br /> <br /> For example, you keep clinging to the &quot;patriarchy doesn't exist&quot; in Tremere and Setite things but both of those were 1st Edition and 2nd Edition both.<br /> <br /> Carna and Keminitri are both about it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Is Carna first edition, and is she not a deranged serial killer?<br /> Keminitri isn't all about it. She just hates <i>this one guy. </i><br /> I find your counterargument rather unconvincing and not all that much relevant; apart from having literal patriarchs, neither clan is a good backdrop for a war against 'the patriarchy'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 11-03-2020, 02:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-03T11:41:26-08:00","id":1421656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1421643#post1421643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Is Carna first edition, and is she not a deranged serial killer?<br /> Keminitri isn't all about it. She just hates <i>this one guy. </i><br /> I find your counterargument rather unconvincing and not all that much relevant; apart from having literal patriarchs, neither clan is a good backdrop for a war against 'the patriarchy'</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, I wasn't going to make a counterargument at all to begin with because I don't think that it actually warranted much of one. We all have our different views of what qualifies as true at our tables or not. What works for one Storyteller doesn't necessarily work for another. However, I think that you are internalizing a great deal of your own interpretation of the material versus recognizing it's your interpretation. I also feel a bit hypocritical saying that because I do that ALL THE TIME on this forums and am only now getting better on it.<br /> <br /> But to make a slightly longer argument:<br /> <br /> 1. V:TM and specifically V5 is a horror power fantasy of the kind very common to the Nineties and very similar to the &quot;Dark Age of Comics.&quot; You are both simultaneously as monster, sexy, horrifying and alluring. Spawn, the Darkness, Chastity, Lady Death, the Midnight Sons, and Blade are pretty much the Kindred (pun intended) of V:TM. Being a vampire is something meant to be freeing from the social restrictions of morality while simultaneously introducing you into different forms of oppression. Being black, gay, a woman, or other minority means little as a vampire but it also is something that you are still surrounded by and can affect.<br /> <br /> 2. They &quot;backed down&quot; on the Chechnya issue for reasons that I think they should be given a pass on. Mark Rein Hagen stated that the people involved were actually threatened and the distributors of Russian White Wolf were put on national television. There was also fear of going after people there. It got a lot of attention and raised money for saving lives but replacing the content was probanly good to protect real lives. It didn't help a lot of Western fans did not understand what the point was trying to make.<br /> <br /> 3. &quot;Woke&quot; as a verb means that a person is aware of systematic prejudice and institutionalized disparities so V:TM has always been &quot;woke.&quot; In fact, the irony is that Werewolf: The Apocalypse has always been the MOST woke as it is a game that is from top to bottom about corporate greed, indigineous issues, and the cruelties of traditionalist religious power structures. In V:TM, it's always been &quot;The Elders on top, neonates on the bottom, humans as their prey.&quot;<br /> <br /> 4. Part of what made CBN 1st Edition so great was that having been a player since grade school of Dungeons and Dragons, the game introduced me to a collection of vampires that were a mix of multiple races (black people in books! GASP! Gay people too!) as well as orientations that I previously hadn't seen. Its baked into the core DNA of the game that this is meant to be more representative of a diverse population than games typically were of its era.<br /> <br /> I feel V5 tackles grittier subject matter and remembers this because 2nd and 3rd got too wrapped up in the apocalypse and sect warfare. Vampires vs. human traffickers is just as compelling as vampires vs. Sabbat (though I tend to prefer vampires vs. human traffickers who work for the Sabbat).<br /> <br /> 5. Part of what makes Carna entertaining is the assumption that she is correct about the fact that she is an oppressed minority within the Tremere AS WELL as a serial killer. We haven't seen her write-up but part of what makes Carna and Rudi interesting are they may be substantively right but they're also fucking awful people. One of my favorite characters from CBN1st Edition was Dickie Fulcher and while a lot of people focused on his name being the same as a comedian's, I was always fascinated that he's a die-hard supporter of Maldavis and a mass murdering serial killer.<br /> <br /> 6. Another area that I think handles the issue well is one we've disagreed with repeatedly and that's how to handle Followers of Set orthodoxy. Yes, Keminitri is only against Set but Set is the cult leader and the Followers of Set are a cult (specifically one cult and dozens of sub-cult that it franchises). Set apparently Embraced multiple beautiful redheaded women, made them nearly omnipotent 4th geenration Demigods, and then BRAINWASHED THE SHIT out of them with his free love murder cult. Their sex, drugs, and rock and roll cult stems from them downward to oppress more women and men in its ranks.<br /> <br /> I don't think you should make the Followers of Set a bunch of incels but I actually think THE CHILLING ADVENTURES OF SABRINA makes a good example of them. Women are encouraged to be sexy, seductresses, and told they're &quot;free&quot; while simultaneously men and the orthodox cult atke advantage of that. Its not the main defining element of the cult but is certainly a way to use it.<br /> <br /> 7. Sexism in the Tremere is something that Ailsing Sturbridge dealt with, Carna, Erichtho, and multiple other female Tremere that mentioned it in their backstories. Merlinda may be one of the Seven but apparently she doesn't care. Also, the people the Tremere recruit from for the past 1000 years are generally not the same groups as other Clans that have a more even female-to-male ratio. The sexism of society means that the average Tremere recruited from scholarly and ocuclt backgrounds are going to preclude women until the 20th century. No wonder the Clan has a reputation for sexism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 11-03-2020, 02:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-03T12:15:31-08:00","id":1421660,"title":"","content":"1- It seems your gender, race and orientation means absolutely everything now. It's downright condescending. <br /> 3- VTM has always been woke. I've never said otherwise. However, V5 is &quot;Woke&quot;. Like, v1 was a cunning and insidious master-stroke of satire. V1 was something anyone could pick up and it could shift their viewpoint. V5 is the satirical equivelent of that CERTAIN CADENCE public speakers use when they want everyone to know that THEY ARE AGAINST THE THING EVERYONE ELSE IS AGAINST. But honestly, to use the marxist term; it's a false consciousness. We're getting pumped up with agression towards peripheral concerns and lead away from actually meaningful discourse. It reads like outrage culture. It doesn't inform. There's nothing there to change or harmonize views, if anything it's just a fence for you to get on one side of. It's a distinctly unhealthy way to be &quot;progressive&quot;. So yeah, it seems like a corporate appropriation of liberal values. <br /> 4 - as 1; <br /> 5- ok. but consider the framing of V5 and what it'd be like to read that were you unfamiliar with the Tremere. That'd be fine on it's own, but also, if you are familiar with the Tremere, you can't trust your old knowledge because they've fundamentally changed significant aspects of the Tremere; There's enough there to make you think you should be taking House Carna at face value... and also.... Are the Tremere actually a highly patriarchal organization? I mean there's been women in the inner circle. Sure, they're a clan more likely to pick up a few incels than most, but are they actually dicks to women? Because I've always read that they're the new-money-profesional counter to the Old-money Ventrue boys club; which should infer that they aren't sexist generally speaking. <br /> 6- look, i just need to clarify it for you; not liking a cult has absolutely nothing to do with patriarchy. Not liking 'free love' is not taking down the patriarchy. Secular speak; Women are allowed to like sex. Men are allowed to like women who like sex. <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">I mean you're all going to hell if you have sex without matching wedding rings, but hell's a given for vampires anyway. </span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-03T13:20:34-08:00","id":1421669,"title":"","content":"Well as a fan since First Edition, I disagree and think that with rare exceptions that V5 feels like V1 and that's a good thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 5- ok. but consider the framing of V5 and what it'd be like to read that were you unfamiliar with the Tremere. That'd be fine on it's own, but also, if you are familiar with the Tremere, you can't trust your old knowledge because they've fundamentally changed significant aspects of the Tremere; There's enough there to make you think you should be taking House Carna at face value... and also.... Are the Tremere actually a highly patriarchal organization? I mean there's been women in the inner circle. Sure, they're a clan more likely to pick up a few incels than most, but are they actually dicks to women? Because I've always read that they're the new-money-profesional counter to the Old-money Ventrue boys club; which should infer that they aren't sexist generally speaking. </div> </div> </div>The thing is that of all the female Tremere NPCs, a substantial number indicate....the Tremere are dicks to women?<br /> <br /> Ailsing Sturbridge: Treated with incredible disdain and has a backstory related to Alistair Crowely wanting to use her as a sex slave.<br /> <br /> Erichtho: Embraced as a sex slave for Nicolai despite her vast occult gifts.<br /> <br /> Carna: Embraced as a sex slave, driven insane by her sire, and now a serial killer.<br /> <br /> We know Merlinda is the exception but how much of a dick to women do members of the Clan do they have to be before its a problem?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 6- look, i just need to clarify it for you; not liking a cult has absolutely nothing to do with patriarchy. Not liking 'free love' is not taking down the patriarchy. Secular speak; Women are allowed to like sex. Men are allowed to like women who like sex. </div> </div> </div>I'm saying that controlling of women by forcing them into certain roles in the religion, specifically because we KNOW Set enslaved and brainwashed his female progeny, is perfectly in-character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 11-03-2020, 04:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-03T13:35:08-08:00","id":1421673,"title":"","content":"Point of order, your looking at writing from early 20's something year olds who ran convention larps to pick up goth chicks......maybe not the most nuanced of authors?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-03T13:36:19-08:00","id":1421675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1421673#post1421673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Point of order, your looking at writing from early 20's something year olds who ran convention larps to pick up goth chicks......maybe not the most nuanced of authors?</div> </div> </div> </div>Grant Morrison claims this desire inspired his entire writing career.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-03T13:37:51-08:00","id":1421677,"title":"","content":"I mean fair enough, Dwight but on the other hand there is the \u2018Death of the Author\u2019 to consider. What the writers intended is interesting and should probably be kept in mind but it\u2019s not the end-all-be-all of what an audience can gain in terms of meaning from a cultural product.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-03T13:41:21-08:00","id":1421678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1421677#post1421677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean fair enough, Dwight but on the other hand there is the \u2018Death of the Author\u2019 to consider. What the writers intended is interesting and should probably be kept in mind but it\u2019s not the end-all-be-all of what an audience can gain in terms of meaning from a cultural product.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing about House Carna is that they're not fighting for progressive women's rights either or at least in the context that they're complaining about job opportunities or a glass ceiling or the right to vote in the Pyramid. House Carna's feminist agenda is supernatural based with the fact that they want to divorce the Pyramid from male orientated magic to atavistic nature magic with a feminine role in the supernatural. It's a fundamentally occult-based rebellion that could be summarized as, &quot;Less Order of Hermes, more Verbena!&quot;<br /> <br /> I think this was a good decision because while vampires may or may not care about oppression, at least any except their own, I feel like their complaints will be a lot...WEIRDER than your typical humans.<br /> <br /> If a Follower of Set complains about sexism, she's probably complaining about the Church of Set refusing to allow women to perform the Rite of the Heirophant and demand they submit to the 5th Benediction of Nephyths.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 11-03-2020, 04:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-04T02:05:29-08:00","id":1421751,"title":"","content":"'less order of hermes, more verbenae' is like telling a bunch of engineers to trust in The Force, western surgeons to take up faith healing, or getting corporate lawyers to ignore their law books and try to win their cases on what's morally right. I realise v5 blood sorcery is a fundamentally different animal to vtm thaumaturgy, but we didn't get an excellent thaumaturgy trillogy for this to be ok. Send me back in time so i may slay the fool that decided rational and evidence based thinking was masculine and that we should celebrate nonsense for the sake of the 'fairer sex'. Otherwise I'll go tell my GP she's in the wrong fucking field and should start selling me herbal remedies. <br /> <br /> The only thing that bribgs me solace is the purely in-universe rational that the culture swap of House Carna is just a sale's pitch and really they're standard Tremere with the facade of liberalism. <br /> Unfortunately, with the patern we're seeing, there's a good probability that what we are seeing should be taken at face value.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-04T02:51:54-08:00","id":1421758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1421751#post1421751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">'less order of hermes, more verbenae' is like telling a bunch of engineers to trust in The Force, western surgeons to take up faith healing, or getting corporate lawyers to ignore their law books and try to win their cases on what's morally right. I realise v5 blood sorcery is a fundamentally different animal to vtm thaumaturgy, but we didn't get an excellent thaumaturgy trillogy for this to be ok. Send me back in time so i may slay the fool that decided rational and evidence based thinking was masculine and that we should celebrate nonsense for the sake of the 'fairer sex'. Otherwise I'll go tell my GP she's in the wrong fucking field and should start selling me herbal remedies.<br /> <br /> The only thing that brings me solace is the purely in-universe rational that the culture swap of House Carna is just a sale's pitch and really they're standard Tremere with the facade of liberalism. Unfortunately, with the pattern we're seeing, there's a good probability that what we are seeing should be taken at face value.</div> </div> </div> </div>And yet, Carna is absolutely 100% correct that the most Tremere are orthodox followers of Hermetic magic when there is no reason that Blood Sorcery/Thaumaturgy practitioners should be limited to it. We have Technomancy, Assamite Babylonian and Caanite Sorcery, Followers of Set Egyptian true name sorcery, and Marcus Vitel's Roman Numena that may actually have been a Lasombra or Venture sorcery that has since been lost. Baba Yaga is also a perfect source of Verbena-esque Sorcery.<br /> <br /> Is it weird I find the conflict over styles of magic (feminine, sex, blood, and moon based vs. methodical, book, number, and name based) more interesting for House Carna vs. Tremere than I would over more &quot;normal&quot; sexism and oppression? Maybe. On the other hand, that's what the Loresheets imply. Besides, THE BOOK OF THE GRAVE WAR is about liberating yourself and your mind from mind-control and the Blood Bond so it's not like Carna is LIMITED to women.<br /> <br /> It's just her magic style primarily appeals to them.<br /> <br /> But it helps explain why Carna is in the Camarilla and not the Anarchs once she had a choice. Carna is concerned with issues unrelated to Anarch ones. You are 100% correct that Carna Tremere are still the same scheming Elders and plotters of regular Clan Tremere. They're just wearing pointy hats and standing over cauldrons with silver slippers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 11-04-2020, 06:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-04T03:24:29-08:00","id":1421762,"title":"","content":"She's 100% wrong. First off, consider how much of a fucking pain it would be to manage a chantry where everyone's speaking a different language compared to a chantry where everyone's doing the same fucking thing. The standardization of Hermetic thaumaturgy is an absolute gift; Everyone's on the same page when it comes to teaching and learning. It may not be as exciting, but it's a thousand times more effective. Oh and they're not killing eachother over superstition disputes or anything like that, which is nice.<br /> Second.<br /> Different styles of magic have advantages and disadvantages to them. A Setite sorcerer absolutely needs to larp as a priest(ess) to do a ritual, Dur-An-Ki requires you to get into an ecstatic state. The former has you worship the dark god and defend a shrine and the latter has you mess with entities you don't quite understand and get high while you're doing it. Sure, these styles come with their small advantages that the Tremere don't have, but the tremere have done really well in eliminating the weaknesses of their style.<br /> <br /> Next, of course, Hermeticism is an all-encompassing philosophy. If it exists, they can make magic of it. &quot;As above, so below&quot;. If you're following a pagan pantheon, you are limited to learning magics appropriate to your view of that pantheon: You can't learn Lure of Flames if you don't have a fire deity in your pantheon, or if the fire deity in your pantheon is opposed to the god you like. Most pantheons don't have a tech God, so you can never learn technomagic... But, if your pantheon had, say, something totally cool like a Goddess of Bees, and you could make the &quot;Path of Bees&quot;, the Tremere wouldn't take all that long to steal it and adapt it to their system. You would never be able to use the Path of Bees if you didn't have a God of Bees.<br /> <br /> The Tremere don't celebrate their Thaumaturgy above others entirely because of hubris; by most rationalization their magic is the best, and their organization and ability to diseminate magic safely and effectively is the reason why they 'won' their monopoly over magic. You could make the same argument for the Order of Hermes: it's not a coincidence that they lead the traditions.<br /> <br /> In summary; Abandoning Hermetic Thaumaturgy to accept all kinds of magicians is just foolish.<br /> <br /> Edit: I get that you might like Carna because it caters to more casual play of thaumaturges and it's nice to put your own worldview into things, that's fine. I'm not going to deride you for that. But from a pure-in universe perspective, it's bad and shouldn't work, and I think the direction <i>Rites Of The Blood</i> was going by adding all sorts of Anarch sorcery categories would do much better in accommodating everyone. Because what was in RotB worked for everything. Additions like House Carna (if played straight) or the witches of echidna are just harmful to people who enjoy the original material. (and overthinking a work of fiction)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 11-04-2020, 07:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-04T03:44:11-08:00","id":1421765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1421762#post1421762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: I get that you might like Carna because it caters to more casual play of thaumaturges and it's nice to put your own worldview into things, that's fine. I'm not going to deride you for that. But from a pure-in universe perspective, it's bad and shouldn't work, and I think the direction <i>Rites Of The Blood</i> was going by adding all sorts of Anarch sorcery categories would do much better in accommodating everyone. Because what was in RotB worked for everything. Additions like House Carna (if played straight) or the witches of echidna are just harmful to people who enjoy the original material. <b>(and critical thinking)</b></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Yeah, let's not add those kind of jabs.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-04T03:57:11-08:00","id":1421766,"title":"","content":"<b>Anarchs, Thaumaturgy, Blood Sorcery, and the Tremere</b><br /> <br /> Honestly, my opinion is that Thaumaturgy is way overplayed and I don't have an especial fondness for House Tremere. I feel like it was frequently treated as the &quot;one discipline to rule them all&quot; and it was my hope that V5 would work to expand the flexibility of other Disciplines so that people would want to get Protean every bit as much as Blood Sorcery. Unfortunately, the Combo Discipline limitations and lack of Elder DIsciplines severely limits this and I'm disappointed vampire powers remain so limited. I'm glad they've simplified Blood Sorcery and limited Paths to rituals so that it's not quite such a broken OP collection.<br /> <br /> Nevertheless, I admit that the Tremere aren't my OTP. I do have MANY players who absolutely love them, though, and are utterly and completely obsessed with playing them. I don't get it, probably because I'm Chaotic Neutral in real life and thus the idea of playing in a rigidly controlled Freemasons-esque secret society doesn't quite appeal to me. My love of Clans can basically go like this:<br /> <br /> 1. Malkavians<br /> 2. Brujah<br /> 3. Followers of Set<br /> 4. Tzimisce (Dark Ages)<br /> 5. Lasombra<br /> 6. Duskborn/Caitiff<br /> 7. Toreador<br /> 8. Ventrue (love to hate em)<br /> 9. Tremere<br /> 10. Gangrel<br /> 11. Nosferatu<br /> 12. Giovanni<br /> 13. Assamites<br /> 14. Ravnos<br /> <br /> One of the things that are consistent in my players' love of the Tremere is that they very much like playing up the controlling nature of the Tremere. House Carna liberating members from the Pyramid's heriarchy and the sudden death of the Council of Seven. Whether or not you approve of these events, they're interesting Tremere-based events that are worth exploring in-game because they're related to their concepts. Like, killing Aunt May is a big deal in Spider-Man and terrible for him personally, but it's certainly a storyline.<br /> <br /> The &quot;Rebellion Tremere&quot; has always been a concept I've been interested in as it's an environment of near total control of thought, actions, and activity versus the relative freedom of other clans.<br /> <br /> I think Carna opens up new roleplaying opportunities and storylines for Tremere, which means it should be supported.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 11-04-2020, 07:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-04T04:42:42-08:00","id":1421771,"title":"","content":"Thaumaturgy: A victim of it's own marketing. It's really not that strong. It's just too cool for it's own good. And I am utterly displeased with V5's thaumaturgy. Talk about a total overcorrection. It's as complicated as Potence. It makes sense if you imagine it as written for Carna's amateurs and not for the enlightened hermetics of clan Tremere. I get that this edition is filled with broad, sweeping changes, but blood magic only has the veneer of thaumaturgy; It's a completely different discipline, and outside of a few rituals is very much a nerd power rather than something actually desirable.<br /> Thaumaturgy is not meant to be easily accessible. You are meant to invest significant time and effort into it. That's it's deal. That's a defining feature. Thaumaturgy isn't supposed to be for everybody. You need pages of paths to work through. House Carna embracing amatuers just seems out of character. House Carna claiming to cast off oppressive structure just seems wrong. And the Tremere are THE clan you're meant to love to hate (Again, a victim of their own success)<br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">Also why do you rank assamites so low? and why's there no vanilla tzmisce on your list? </span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1421765#post1421765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Yeah, let's not add those kind of jabs.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Wasn't my intention. I think I fixed it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-04T09:22:24-08:00","id":1421807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1421678#post1421678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing about House Carna is that they're not fighting for progressive women's rights either...</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm struck by how the &quot;feminist&quot; narrative has taken over so much of the dialogue about House Carna, when (A) it plays a small part in the official material about the group and (B) not much has been written about them in any case. While some of the women involved have grievances - not the least being Carna herself - it's not the only thing they've got going on. If anything House Carna could become a mini-sect, rather like the Hecata. Basically, they could easily be home to anyone not practicing Blood Magic in the proscribed and orthodox way mandated by the now (gone) Tremere clan pyramid and Vienna chantry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-04T09:26:52-08:00","id":1421809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1421807#post1421807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm struck by how the &quot;feminist&quot; narrative has taken over so much of the dialogue about House Carna, when (A) it plays a small part in the official material about the group and (B) not much has been written about them in any case. While some of the women involved have grievances - not the least being Carna herself - it's not the only thing they've got going on. If anything House Carna could become a mini-sect, rather like the Hecata. Basically, they could easily be home to anyone not practicing Blood Magic in the proscribed and orthodox way mandated by the now (gone) Tremere clan pyramid and Vienna chantry.</div> </div> </div> </div>My view on Carna's history is:<br /> <br /> 1. Carna discovers a magic ritual that breaks Blood Bonds, Dominate, and other mind-control. It is the Book of the Grave War.<br /> <br /> 2. She passes it around among her fellow American Tremere and others she invites<br /> <br /> 3. She flees Milwaukee with it and her fellow defectors to the West Coast. Carna and her followers, however many exist, expect a massive retaliation.<br /> <br /> 4. The Tremere Pyramid unexpectedly is annihilated by the Second Inquisition, possibly with the help of an outside party<br /> <br /> 5. Carna discovers she DOESN'T NEED to join the Anarchs as her enemies are now far weaker.<br /> <br /> 6. Carna leverages her position to becoming a Clan Faction protected by the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> 7. The Loyalist Tremere lose their shit but can't fight a war against them right now.<br /> <br /> 8. Carna develops her Loresheet that is a lot of sex and cauldron magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-04T10:50:11-08:00","id":1421814,"title":"","content":"So she just rebrands the Vaulderie and that's it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-04T10:59:22-08:00","id":1421817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1406359-wir-5e-anarchs?p=1421814#post1421814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So she just rebrands the Vaulderie and that's it?</div> </div> </div> </div>It also fixes Dominate.<br /> <br /> But I'm almost 100% certain the Book of the Grave War probably rewrites your brain to serve another Methuselah because we can't have nice things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Au